{
	chapter.10472A19D0BE2DB6.title: "&cKill All the Things"
	chapter.115CF138BD9FA023.title: "&4LV4 - End Game"
	chapter.16945E353746C2E9.title: "&fLV1 - Early Game"
	chapter.173F873148866E0A.title: "&2LV3 - Reactors Age"
	chapter.1991B9A423A366DE.title: "Farming and Cooking"
	chapter.1AAFA4CDA1C2D85F.title: "&9LV3.5 - Space Age"
	chapter.1AF8D22F2AEAA21B.title: "&6LV2 - Oil Age"
	chapter.1C2214FB8892E6B1.title: "&zApplied Energistics 2"
	chapter.1C33CA70D8E6530E.title: "Tips and Tricks"
	chapter.1EDE5872E48B4B4D.title: "Building and Decorating"
	chapter.1F518E45BAA52F0F.title: "&3OpenComputers"
	chapter.6B33585FD658A43F.title: "&5Advanced Logistics"
	file.0000000000000001.title: "Nuclear Tech: New Horizons"
	quest.00F1CE20E2AAFA68.quest_desc: ["&3Conveyor Ejectors&r can be fitted with two upgrade types. &6Stack Ejection&r increases how many items are output at once, while &6Ejection Speed&r increases how quickly items are output. Both upgrades can be applied up to level 3."]
	quest.00F1CE20E2AAFA68.title: "Conveyor Upgrades"
	quest.0128FC80D7B5235E.quest_desc: [
		"&3Network Separator&r splits a power network into separate segments and lets you control how power flows between them. It only outputs energy from the port marked with a red arrow and only accepts energy on the green arrow side, so power cannot flow back from the output network into the input network. A power gauge on the device shows how much electricity is passing through."
		""
		"Priority and throughput are set in its GUI. Energy always flows to the separator with the highest priority. All other machines have NORMAL priority, so a HIGH priority separator will draw power first while possible, and a LOW priority separator will only receive power after the buffers of all other machines are full. You can also shut the separator off by supplying redstone power from beneath it."
	]
	quest.091DD5CE6163A914.quest_desc: [
		"The &3Combinator Funnel&r is a cheap, unpowered machine that automates 2x2 or 3x3 recipes using the same item, like nuggets into ingots or small powder into full powder. It is very useful for &eBedrock Ore Processing&r."
		""
		"Pick the recipe pattern with the toggle in the bottom-right of the GUI. Input goes in the top slot, output comes out the bottom, and items can be pulled from the sides to avoid clogging. It has 9 top and 9 bottom slots, works with normal hoppers, and can run up to 9 operations per tick."
	]
	quest.09B8D16D011B439B.quest_desc: [
		"There is a web-based RBMK simulator, in which you can build and test different RBMK setups, as well as check out other people's creations!"
		""
		"[ { \"text\": \"https://rbmksim.nvrsrv.com\", \"underlined\": true, \"clickEvent\": { \"action\": \"open_url\", \"value\": \"https://rbmksim.nvrsrv.com\" } } ]"
	]
	quest.0B4CB4F3882C729D.quest_desc: ["&6Borax&r is found as depth deposits near bedrock - bring explosives to mine it. It can also be extracted from bedrock ores. Acidize it with bsulfuric acidr in an &3Ore Acidizer&r for &6boron&r (best yield with effectiveness upgrades), or run it through an &3Electric Arc Furnace&r. Borax is also an efficient &6flux&r and an ingredient of the &6saturnite&r blend in a &3Rotary Furnace&r (reformate gas, copper and high-speed steel powder)."]
	quest.0F272D305C14E39D.quest_desc: ["&3RoR Panels&r are crafted from a blank panel and act as control panel blocks. Interactive types like Keypads and Levers send commands to controllers, while aesthetic types like Gauges, Graphs, Digital Displays, and Indicator Lamps show values received from readers. Each component must be enabled with the red buttons in its GUI. Once placed, Shift-Click with a screwdriver to open the configuration screen and set IDs, colors, labels, and modes."]
	quest.0F272D305C14E39D.title: "Displays, Buttons and More"
	quest.101A87A802FFDCFF.quest_desc: ["&3Conveyor Boxers&r package a certain amount of items into a box, configurable inside a &3Conveyor Boxer&r, and output them as a single item on a conveyor belt. They are then unpackaged at the &3Conveyor Unboxer&r."]
	quest.101A87A802FFDCFF.title: "Conveyor Boxers"
	quest.101D2FB4DF862790.quest_desc: ["The §3Industrial Boiler§r is an upgraded version of the Boiler which has a higher capacity of held liquid. Additionally, it doesnt explode."]
	quest.101D2FB4DF862790.title: "Industrial Boiler"
	quest.101E16B80F3B2D1E.quest_desc: ["§6Hafnium§r is a rare light metal needed to produce the §6Hafnium chips§r, which at this stage in progression can only be obtained by centrifuging niobium crystals, which must be created from niobium ore, only found on §eDres§r and §eEve§r."]
	quest.101E16B80F3B2D1E.title: "Hafnium"
	quest.10269349C8E8ADF9.quest_desc: [
		"The §6Internet Card§r grants computers access to the internet. It provides ways to perform simple HTTP requests, as well as to open plain TCP client sockets that can be read and written to."
		""
		"Installing an internet card in a computer will also attach a custom file system that contains a few internet related applications, such as one for downloading and uploading snippets from/to pastebin as well as a \"wget\" clone that allows downloading data from arbitrary HTTP URLs."
	]
	quest.10269349C8E8ADF9.title: "Internet Card"
	quest.102DF16DD9F21E94.quest_desc: [
		"The Martian Invasion Ship is a late-game boss which is killed to get the UFO Coin, used in crafting Gerald."
		""
		"It can be summoned by crafting the Martian Invasion Ship item."
	]
	quest.102DF16DD9F21E94.title: "Martian Invasion Ship"
	quest.102E979E9EEEB5DB.quest_desc: ["The §3Cell Workbench§r allow to filter cells to accept specific items. It can prove useful for when making a subnet for §eBedrock Ore Processing§r."]
	quest.102E979E9EEEB5DB.title: "Cell Workbench"
	quest.10379B60934B5F5A.quest_desc: ["The §6Red Key§r is able to open any container that requires a regular key, regardless of the pin configuration of the lock, and it is one of the only two keys capable of opening the keyhole found on strange stone, in order to open a §eRed Room§r. The key has no durability, and can be reused indefinitely."]
	quest.10379B60934B5F5A.title: "Red Key"
	quest.10392D1C9CF89596.quest_desc: ["The §3Molecular Assembler§r is used to autocraft anything that can be made in a crafting table."]
	quest.10392D1C9CF89596.title: "Molecular Assembler"
	quest.105A809219F3FEC8.quest_desc: [
		"The §3ICF§r reactor is a very expensive and powerful reactor, which can produce a substantial amount of energy. Apart from the multiblock itself, §3ICF Lasers§r must be constructed for the reactor to work. §bStellar Flux§r will be produced during its operation which is needed to craft §6Gerald§r. Consider making use of §bLiquid Lead§r as it is a very efficient coolant for the ICF."
		""
		"It is recommended that the wiki is checked out as it has built-in calculators for the laser power consumption and the amount of hot coolant it produces."
		""
		"[url]https://nucleartech.wiki/wiki/Inertial_Confinement_Fusion_Reactor[/url]"
	]
	quest.105A809219F3FEC8.title: "ICF"
	quest.1061A96F3FA19CFF.quest_desc: ["This modpack makes it possible to complete the entire game in §6Martian mode§r! If you notice any gaps in the progression or logic, please post in the #help channel on the NTNH Discord server."]
	quest.1061A96F3FA19CFF.title: "Earth? Fake news"
	quest.10699F18F3550F59.quest_desc: ["The §3Crystal Growth Accelerator§r is a machine that uses energy to accelerate the process of crystal purification. This process transforms crystal seeds into pure versions of their fully developed counterparts."]
	quest.10699F18F3550F59.title: "Crystal Growth Accelerator"
	quest.10766FD76F8EBC44.quest_desc: ["The §6Atmospheric Scanner§r shows the atmospheric consistency of planets. Useful for when terraforming."]
	quest.10766FD76F8EBC44.title: "Atmospheric Scanner"
	quest.1078DC51F89BE446.quest_desc: [
		"This system is highly WIP (including this very quest), so do not expect it to be perfect."
		""
		"This is an advanced mineral exploration technique for professional miners, providing very detailed information. The §3Geological Surveyor§r machine uses a controlled explosion to send seismic waves into the ground, and by analysing the echoes that come back, builds a map of underground ore densities."
		""
		"As well as the Geological Surveyor itself, you will also need the following:"
		""
		"1. At least 3 §3Geophones§r placed in a suitable arrangement around the Geological Surveyor. The geophones must be within 16 blocks of the Surveyor, but no closer than 8 blocks to the Surveyor or to each other."
		"2. Supplies of §6Paper§r, §6Ink§r and §6Gunpowder§r in the appropriate slots of the Surveyor."
		"3. A §6Button§r or other means of supplying a redstone signal to the Surveyor."
		""
		"The Surveyor can operate in either §emonochrome§r or §ecolour§r mode, selected using the button beside the ink slots. Colour mode provides more information about types of ores, but is more expensive. §2Monochrome mode requires only black ink, whereas colour mode requires all four colours of ink.§r"
		""
		"When all the necessary conditions are satisfied, the Surveyor wil show \"§6Ready§r\" in the GUI, and a single green light on the outside of the machine. The Surveyor is trigged by a redstone signal. The easiest way to deliver this is to put a button on the side of the machine."
		""
		"§lBe prepared for a loud noise.§r Do not be alarmed; the explosion is well contained and should not cause any damage."
		""
		"Analysing the results and printing the map will take several seconds, during which time the machine will show a flashing §agreen light§r. When finished, two steady green lights will appear. The map can then be collected from the output slot of the GUI."
		""
		"A §cred light§r indicates an error condition; open the GUI to find out more information."
	]
	quest.1078DC51F89BE446.title: "Geological Survey"
	quest.107B2ED4A3DABDE4.quest_desc: [
		"The §6Siphon§r is a tool used to extract input fluids from a machine. Right-clicking a machine with content in it's input tanks will fill any fluid barrels, universal tanks or pipettes (if the fluid amount cannot fill any of the previous options)."
		""
		"§6Pipettes§r can be used to input specific amounts of fluids. Right-clicking or Shift-Right-clicking will increase or decrease the fluid amount."
	]
	quest.107B2ED4A3DABDE4.title: "Additional Fluid Tools"
	quest.107D566FDAD89F9E.quest_desc: ["The §4§3Heat Exchanging Heater§r is used to cool down coolants used in reactors while also genearting §eTU§r. A §3Boiler§r can be placed ontop of it to heat up other fluids, such as §bSteam§r, to be used in §3Steam Turbines§r."]
	quest.107D566FDAD89F9E.title: "Heat Exchanging Heater"
	quest.107FCE1E54B3CDED.quest_desc: [
		"A §3Keyboard§r is needed to type text on §3Screens§r, be they in the world or built into devices such as §3Robots§r or §6Tablets§r."
		""
		"For the keyboard to work with a screen in the world, it has to be placed next to the screen, facing that screen, or placed directly on the screen (on top or on one of the sides)."
		""
		"The §6EEPROM§r is what contains the code used to initialize a computer when it is being booted."
		""
		"This data is stored as plain byte array, and may mean different things to different §6CPU§r architectures. For example, for Lua it is usually a small script that searches for a file systems with an init script, for other architectures it may be actual machine code."
		""
		"An §6OpenOS Disk§r can be crafted using an empty floppy disk and a manual."
	]
	quest.107FCE1E54B3CDED.title: "Computer"
	quest.109226580F7C0492.quest_desc: [
		"The §6Cable§r serves as a way of connecting computers and machines that are far apart. If you have a compact build where all components touch each other (directly or indirectly, most blocks also behave the same way as cables) you will usually not need cables."
		""
		"The §3Power Converter§r serves as the fastest way to convert energy from other mods' power systems to OpenComputers' internal energy. Placing an §3HE to RF Converter§r next to the PC will also work."
		""
		"The §3Capacitor Stores§r energy to be used by the network, acting as an energy buffer when needed. It is very useful for tasks that demand a lot of energy, such as assembling or charging devices such as robots and drones."
	]
	quest.109226580F7C0492.title: "OC Power"
	quest.1094522588577B41.quest_desc: [
		"§6Oily Sand§r is a surface-level block that generates among normal sand, typically in deserts. It acts as a marker for §bBedrock Oil§r deposits directly beneath it - if you find it, there is oil underground."
		""
		"It can be ground in a §3Grinder§r into §6Oil Waste§r, which can then be processed to obtain §6Arsenic§r - a really important mid-game material."
	]
	quest.1094522588577B41.title: "Oily Sand"
	quest.10A12703B53E8D3F.quest_desc: ["§bBrine§r, which is found in deposits similar to oil ones on earth, can be processed to obtain materials such as §6Nickel§r, §6Copper§r and §6Sulfur§r, and fluids such as §bHydrogen§r and §bOxygen§r."]
	quest.10A12703B53E8D3F.title: "Brine Processing"
	quest.10A4DE8FE69FC44C.quest_desc: [
		"The §3Assembly Machine§r is used in every stage of the game, with it being used to manufacture practically every other complex machine. Recipes for it can be chosen inside the GUI."
		""
		"§2Some unique recipes require blueprints, that can be found in dungeons and/or bought from Bobmazon."
	]
	quest.10A4DE8FE69FC44C.title: "Assembly Machine"
	quest.10A4F188D34FC8CC.quest_desc: ["The §3Security Terminal§r can be used to specify what players are allowed to interact with in the ME network which can be useful in multiplayer. It can also be used to link a §6Wireless Terminal§r to the ME network. Atleast one §3Wireless Access Point§r is required, and its range can be expanded using §6Wireless Boosters§r."]
	quest.10A4F188D34FC8CC.title: "Wireless Terminal"
	quest.10C667A0D3E10907.quest_desc: [
		"One Space Laboratory will produce &eFlight Data&r for &6Disk Drives&r every 15 minutes."
		""
		"Flight data needs to be processed in the &3Supercomputer&r."
	]
	quest.10C667A0D3E10907.title: "Flight Data"
	quest.10E88B1A8AB29CC3.quest_desc: ["§dModern Markings§r adds wall and floor decorations suited for many purposes. Use the §6Chisel§r on the floor or wall signs to change their design."]
	quest.10E88B1A8AB29CC3.title: "Modern Markings"
	quest.10EB497660514FB6.quest_desc: ["The §3ME Interface§r is a block which allows the ME Network to interact with machines and inventories. On their own, they can be used to automatically stock inventories, but can be used with §6ME Patterns§r later on for autocrafting."]
	quest.10EB497660514FB6.title: "ME Interface"
	quest.10FCAF8CBEB1E139.quest_desc: ["Here ya go, your reward"]
	quest.10FCAF8CBEB1E139.title: "§c§l§4§lHOW THE FUCK?!"
	quest.111FE781EAE3E25C.quest_desc: [
		"An upgraded version of the §3Anvil§r, [T3], which unlocks additional recipes."
		""
		"Alternatively, the §3Desh Anvil§r can be skipped by making a §3Ferrouranium Anvil§r, [T4], from scavanged §e§r§6Uranium-238§r found in structures."
	]
	quest.111FE781EAE3E25C.title: "Desh Anvil"
	quest.112A2356FF3746F1.quest_desc: [
		"The §3ZIRNOX§r is the first and cheapest nuclear reactor one can make. Unlike the §3PWR§r and §3RBMK§r, it is a fully assembled reactor which requires §bWater§r and §bCarbon Dioxide§r to operate."
		""
		"Due to its modest steam output, the ZIRNOX can be paired with several §3Steam Engines§r, though an §3Industrial Turbine§r is recommended for its §e100%§r efficiency. A single §3Steam Condenser§r handles the exhaust on lower power fuels. 24 §6Natural Uranium Fuel Rods§r using 14kmB of carbon dioxide will yield a power output of around §e240kHE/s§r."
	]
	quest.112A2356FF3746F1.title: "ZIRNOX"
	quest.1135D2548546E1BB.quest_desc: [
		"The §3Stirling Engine§r uses heat from a §3Heating Oven§r or a §3§r§3Firebox§r to produce power. If a Heating Oven is used to heat a Stirling engine, it will likely over-speed and damage it, sending the main gear flying. The heavy Stirling engine does not have this issue."
		""
		"A firebox running on coal with a stirling engine produces §e2kHE/s§r, while a heating oven with a heavy stirling engine produces §e10kHE/s§r."
	]
	quest.1135D2548546E1BB.title: "Stirling Engine"
	quest.113616AF92CDDCA2.quest_desc: [
		"Walking around the world, you can find a §6Mustard Willow§r on dead or §6Oily Dirt§r. The willow itself will not be needed anytime soon, but it is better to collect it and the soil underneath it."
		""
		"§6Industrial Hemp§r is used to craft ropes, strings and biomass."
	]
	quest.113616AF92CDDCA2.title: "Industrial Hemp & Mustard Willow"
	quest.11375AEAD5B9F6C6.quest_desc: ["§6Tungsten Carbide§r is an alloy made from §6Tungsten§r and §bSyngas§r in a §3Pyrolysis Oven§r. It is mainly used in crafting neutron reflectors for reactors and nukes."]
	quest.11375AEAD5B9F6C6.title: "Tungsten Carbide"
	quest.113E182864DE905E.quest_desc: [
		"With access to §6Tantalium§r for §6Control Units§r and fissile matterials, it is possible to assemble a nuclear bomb. To detonate the bomb one can use a detonator or a redstone signal."
		""
		"A nuclear explosion will transform ores into more valuable ones, such as §6Coal§r to §6Diamonds§r or §6Uranium§r to §6Schrabidium§r. Be prepared with radiation resistant armor before venturing into the crater."
		""
		"Make sure to stand behind some strong cover if you wish to see the explosion from close by."
		""
		"§2This quest serves as a list of components needed for various bombs. Some of these components can be mounted onto rockets that will carry the payload over large distances."
	]
	quest.113E182864DE905E.title: "Nuclear Bombs"
	quest.1158CA1BCEDE2CB6.quest_desc: ["With the §3Spent Fuel Pool Drum§r to cool down §3ZIRNOX§r or §3PWR§r depleted nuclear fuel and the §3PUREX§r to further process them, many new materials are now available."]
	quest.1158CA1BCEDE2CB6.title: "Nuclear Fuel Processing"
	quest.115B2636BF0AC8E9.quest_desc: ["The §6Infinity Booster Card§r allows one to access their ME system across any distance and dimension. To apply simply open the §6Wireless Crafting Terminal§r and insert the card in it."]
	quest.115B2636BF0AC8E9.title: "Infinity Booster Card"
	quest.11634D0909B1B2AB.quest_desc: [
		"§dArchitectureCraft§r introduces the §3Architect's Workbench§r which can be used to change the shapes blocks."
		""
		"The §6Architect's Hammer§r can be used to easily rotate the blocks."
		""
		"The §6Architect's Glowbrush§r can be used to apply light to any block."
	]
	quest.11634D0909B1B2AB.title: "ArchitectureCraft"
	quest.117117CAB5B1035D.quest_desc: ["They shoot you with explosive fireballs but they are weak when you hit them or knock the fireballs back with a weapon. Better upgrade your armor with fire and blast protection."]
	quest.117117CAB5B1035D.title: "Time to Kill (Ghast)"
	quest.117DE2E074E3ABBD.quest_desc: ["The §6Card Base§r is a common crafting material for card components in OC, such as §6Graphics Cards§r and §6Network Cards§r."]
	quest.117DE2E074E3ABBD.title: "Card Base"
	quest.11930FCB9E89092C.quest_desc: [
		"The §3Pyrolysis Oven§r is a mid-to-late game oil processing machine that allows easier production pf §6Crystalline Fullerite§r, which is needed in bulk for late-game machines onwards."
		""
		"It can process an item with an optional fluid to produce another item and/or fluid. Functionally, it works similar to the §3Combination Oven§r, mostly in bedrock ore processing."
		"Its main use however is in production of §6Fullerene§r, as it can turn §6Tar§r into §6Fine Soot§r, eliminating the RNG of a §3Smokestack§r."
		""
		"Operating the pyrolysis oven will consume §e200kHE/s§r."
	]
	quest.11930FCB9E89092C.title: "Pyrolysis Oven"
	quest.1194102BBB0EE722.quest_desc: [
		"§6Ionized Particles§r are the main product of the §3Fusion Reactor§r and are used in making §6Ferric Scrabidate§r, as well as some particle capsules needed in the §3Particle Accelerator§r."
		""
		"§2Ionized Particles can be infinitely produced by utilizing Ionic Gel."
	]
	quest.1194102BBB0EE722.title: "Ionized Particles"
	quest.11AFDB66DEA5100D.quest_desc: [
		"§bReformate§r is a product of §bCrude Oil§r obtained via a §3Vacuum Refinery§r or from processing §bNaptha§r in a §3Hydrotreater§r."
		""
		"§2This step can be skipped if making Jet Fuel and BTX using a Hydrotreater."
	]
	quest.11AFDB66DEA5100D.title: "Reformate"
	quest.11BD8CF70BB308C8.quest_desc: ["The ME Controller acts as the routing hub of an ME network. It can support up to 8 devices connected to it."]
	quest.11BD8CF70BB308C8.title: "ME Controller"
	quest.11BEEB2C1D872BF5.quest_desc: ["§bHydrazine§r is a powerful rocket fuel which is needed to operate a §3Drop Pod§r."]
	quest.11BEEB2C1D872BF5.title: "Hydrazine"
	quest.11CA265B52DA0311.quest_desc: [
		"§3Tanks§r and §3Barrels§r are useful storage devices that can hold various fluids in various amounts. Each tank and barrel supports holding different types of corrosive, hot, or exotic fluids, and knowing which ones can hold your desired fluids can be vital to your fluid processing and storage facilities."
		""
		"Tanks can hold up to 256,000mb of fluids, while a Steel Barrel can hold 16,000."
		""
		"§4§2Tanks cant hold highly Antimatter and Corrosive fluids and as such a Big-Ass Tank 9000 or a Magnetic Tank is needed respectively."
	]
	quest.11CA265B52DA0311.title: "Tank"
	quest.11D2D2E3B8CC5475.quest_desc: [
		"Three mods overhaul farming and food in this pack."
		""
		"§dPam's HarvestCraft§r adds 40+ crops, many fruit trees, 10 fish, beekeeping, and 75+ foods. Key blocks: §3Presser§r (produces oils, honey, etc.), §3Market§r (buys seeds and saplings for emeralds), §3Shipping Block§r (sells crops for emeralds). Right-clicking a mature crop harvests and replants it."
		""
		"§dAgriCraft§r adds genetics-based crop breeding. Plants have six stats - Growth, Gain, Strength, Resistance, Fertility, and Mutativity - inherited from parent crops when cross-breeding. Higher stats are dominant. Mutations can unlock new crop species entirely. Weeds will compete with and eventually kill unmanaged crops. Plants have specific soil, light, and fluid requirements, so placement matters."
		""
		"§dHunger Overhaul§r requires farmland to be placed adjacent to water - untouched dry tilled soil will not function."
		""
		"§2Note that the crops should be planted on the Crop Sticks."
	]
	quest.11D2D2E3B8CC5475.title: "Agriculture and Farming"
	quest.11D5ECA34D0C7BC9.quest_desc: [
		"The §6Welded Technetium/Cadmium Steel Plate§r is the welded varient of the cast technetium/cadmium steel plate and is used in some recipes that require strong materials."
		""
		"§2Make sure to have good energy generation and storage infrastructure as each plate costs 1.2 Billion HE."
	]
	quest.11D5ECA34D0C7BC9.title: "Welded Technetium/Cadmium Steel Plate"
	quest.11D7CC7535CE2A5E.quest_desc: [
		"The §3StarDar§r is your base of operations for mission planning, helping you to locate and scan potential landing zones on planets, and §6Program Drives§r that can be inserted into your rocket's astronavigational systems to make journeys to said planets."
		""
		"The §3Drive Processor§r processes drives that have been programmed by the StarDar, allowing them to be inserted into rocket navigation computers."
	]
	quest.11D7CC7535CE2A5E.title: "Stardar and Drive Processor"
	quest.11DD50AC87DA4996.quest_desc: [
		"The §3Disk Drive§r can be used to read §6Floppy Disks§r using a computer connected to it."
		""
		"This is useful to get started, since the lower tier §3Computer Cases§r do not have a built-in floppy slot, and you'll need an operating system to boot up the computer."
	]
	quest.11DD50AC87DA4996.title: "Floppy Disks and Disk Drive"
	quest.11E76D6BAE975D28.quest_desc: [
		"§6Servers§r are a form of higher tier computer."
		""
		"They can be configured by holding them in the hand and using them - like opening a backpack for example. Servers can also be configured after having been installed into a Rack by activating them (aiming at the corresponding position on the frong face on the rack). To operate, the server has to be placed inside a §3Rack§r."
	]
	quest.11E76D6BAE975D28.title: "Servers"
	quest.11EABEA8C6F4DA47.quest_desc: [
		"§eSubnetworks§r are ME networks which can be accessed from a §eMain Network§r. In §dNTM§r§r they can be useful for storing items from passive processes without flooding the main storage network."
		""
		"§2This quest serves as a guide on how to set up a subnet, which can be used to store the resourses that Bedrock Ore Processing produces.§r"
		""
		"In the image below are two ME networks, the §cRed§r one as the §cMainnet§r, and the §9Blue§r one as the §9Subnet§r."
		""
		"[img height=1000]betterquesting:textures/BQ_NET1.png[/img]"
		""
		"For the purposes of this quest, the main network will store dirt blocks, while the subnet will store copper blocks."
		""
		"[img height=1000]betterquesting:textures/BQ_NET2.png[/img]"
		""
		"[img height=1000]betterquesting:textures/BQ_NET3.png[/img]"
		""
		"To make the contents of the subnet, the copper blocks, visible to the main net, one must make an §3Interface§r-§3Storage Bus§r§r combo. The storage bus must be on the side of the main network."
		""
		"[img height=1000]betterquesting:textures/BQ_NET4.png[/img]"
		""
		"Make sure to filter the main network storage bus, and to also make it \"Extract Only\"."
		""
		"[img height=1000]betterquesting:textures/BQ_NET5.png[/img]"
		""
		"Now the main network has access to materials stored on the sub network, which can be used for crafting."
		""
		"[img height=1000]betterquesting:textures/BQ_NET6.png[/img]"
	]
	quest.11EABEA8C6F4DA47.title: "ME subnetting"
	quest.11ED30B512BE89A1.quest_desc: [
		"The §3Automatic Thresher§r harvests crops such as §6Wheat§r, §6Hemp§r, §6Sugarcane§r, ect in a 7x7 area when supplied with fuel. It will eject all items from the back."
		""
		"[F1] for more information."
	]
	quest.11ED30B512BE89A1.title: "Automatic Thresher"
	quest.11F072A81EF331B1.quest_desc: [
		"§3P2P ME§r can be used to transport massive amounts of channels without laying many cables."
		""
		"§2This quest serves as a guide on how to effectively use P2P ME.§r"
		""
		"Once an §3Energy Acceptor§r has been set up, it is highly recommended (and likely needed) that an §3Energy Cell§r is placed next to it as to ensure that there is enough power going to the system, as more components increase the energy demands of the ME system."
		""
		"After that, 2 §3ME Controllers§r are required, one to provide the channels that machines will use, and another to transport the other's channels by the P2P connections. The top controller can be made bigger by attaching more controllers next to it."
		""
		"[img height=1000]betterquesting:textures/QB_Controller1.png[/img]"
		""
		"After the controllers are placed, on the top controller, a P2P Tunnel - ME needs to be placed on any side. The §9Blue Cable§r will serve as the cable that connects the P2P connections, and as such, it needs to be connected to the bottom controller."
		""
		"[img height=1000]betterquesting:textures/QB_Controller2.png[/img]"
		""
		"By linking the P2P connections together using a §6Memory Card§r, the 32 channels from one side of the top controller will only use 1 channel from the bottom controller to be transported to any destination. The §cRed Cable§r now has access to 32 channels."
		""
		"[img height=1000]betterquesting:textures/QB_Controller3.png[/img]"
		""
		"[img height=1000]betterquesting:textures/QB_Controller4.png[/img]"
		""
		"By expanding on the previous example, more connections can be added to fully utilize all channels."
		""
		"[img height=1000]betterquesting:textures/QB_Controller5.png[/img]"
		""
		"[img height=1000]betterquesting:textures/QB_controller6.png[/img]"
	]
	quest.11F072A81EF331B1.title: "P2P ME Networking"
	quest.11F31C7FC48FCCFF.quest_desc: [
		"Notes:"
		""
		"§b1) This questbook does not contain all the content from the mod, such as the guns, many armor sets and others. Make sure to browse NEI."
		""
		"&b2) §lThere are two types of quests §r§3§b- primary and secondary. Primary quests are quests with unique shape and bold lines between each other."
		""
		"&b3) When updating the modpack to newer versions that has introduced changes to the questbook, in case the quests dont update, delete the betterquesting folder in the world file."
		"&bAfter it is deleted, turn on cheats and do \"/bq_admin edit true\", head over to the chapter of your choice, press the designer button (the one with many squares), click on your quest of choice and finally press the autocomplete button (checkmark) to complete the quests previously completed."
		""
		"§r§bSpecial thanks to everyone on discord who helped out with questions and recommendations while making the quests, as well as the official NTM Wiki for providing information used in the quests."
	]
	quest.11F31C7FC48FCCFF.quest_subtitle: "This Questbook was originally made by _SkippyPlaysMC_ for NT:I/ST:I modpacks and modified by Bufka2011."
	quest.11F31C7FC48FCCFF.title: "Quests information"
	quest.11F53F2F283F144B.quest_desc: ["The Crafting CPU is a multiblock structure composed of §3Crafting Co-Processing Units§r and §3Crafting Storage§r. When placed next to eachother they form one CPU which is used when placing orders via §3Interfaces§r. The more crafting co-processing units the more tasks the CPU can do in parallel while more crafting storage allows for bigger orders to be made."]
	quest.11F53F2F283F144B.title: "Crafting CPU"
	quest.120C477FB7BC62B8.quest_desc: ["§6Weapon steel§r is a steel alloy made by further refining steel in a §3Rotary Furnace§r. As its name implies, it is used in the crafting of weapons and ammunition. It is the next tier of weapons grade alloy after §6Gunmetal§r."]
	quest.120C477FB7BC62B8.title: "Weapon Steel"
	quest.12177EF6475C7B91.quest_desc: ["This planet has some of the most prized resources in the whole system, with even the primary fraction of bedrock ore consisting of incredibly valuable metals and materials. §6Niobium§r, §6Coltan§r, and §6Lanthanium§r ore is present here in vast quantities."]
	quest.12177EF6475C7B91.title: "Dres"
	quest.1218BF33D1991B3A.quest_desc: [
		"§dHBM's NTM§r is an industrial mod, so you'll need §eelectricity§r to continue your journey. The energy is measured in §6HE (HBM Energy)§r."
		""
		"§2If the wood-burning generator is not enough, more advanced energy sources can be unlocked on the left side of this questbook, such as the §3Stirling Engine§2, §3Solar Tower Boiler§2, or §3Radial Performance Engine§2.§r"
	]
	quest.1218BF33D1991B3A.title: "Electricity"
	quest.121D07E889595F99.quest_desc: [
		"Due to the expansive nature of rocket assembly, it is highly recommend that the wiki is checked out as it provides more information."
		""
		"[url]https://nucleartech.wiki/wiki/Vehicle_Assembly_Base_(NTM:_Space)[/url]"
	]
	quest.121D07E889595F99.title: "Rocket Preparations"
	quest.1235CEBDDFF2530A.quest_desc: ["The §3Industrial Greenhouse§r converts §bCarbon Dioxide§r into §bOxygen§r via crop growth. The greenhouse can also be supplied with §6Fertilizer§r for faster growing."]
	quest.1235CEBDDFF2530A.title: "Industrial Greenhouse"
	quest.12418AE23BC310C5.quest_desc: [
		"§3Pneumatic Pipes§r are an instant form of item transportation which can cover large distances. The pipes must have a compressed gas inside them to work."
		""
		"A §6Screwdriver§r is needed to create a connection, and right clicking on the connection with a fluid id will set the gasseous fluid it will use."
	]
	quest.12418AE23BC310C5.title: "Pneumatic Pipes"
	quest.124DA3DFB5D5D6E0.quest_desc: [
		"The §3Radar Survey Satellite§r detects all radar-visible entities - players, rockets, and more - within a 1000-chunk radius of its target position. It compiles results into a searchable list with entity types and exact coordinates, and can filter results by class name without requiring a new scan."
		""
		"RoR commands: \"survey\" scans the area and saves results to both a base list and a filtered list. \"filter name\" replaces the filtered list with only entries matching that class name - the original list is preserved, so this can be run multiple times for different types without rescanning. \"count\" writes the number of filtered results to RX. \"gettargetid index\" returns the unique entity ID for a given entry, which can be passed to other satellites for precise targeting. \"getposition index\" writes exact X/Y/Z coordinates - separated by semicolons - to RX. \"getname index\" writes the class name of the entry to RX."
		""
		"§2Pair this satellite with an §3AUTOCAL§r and the §3Orbital Precision Laser§r for automated missile interception."
	]
	quest.124DA3DFB5D5D6E0.title: "Radar Survey Satellite"
	quest.124E1A876928D343.quest_desc: [
		"Oil products can be combusted or burnt to produce massive amounts of energy."
		""
		"The §3Industrial Combustion Engine§r combusts fuels, such as §bHeating Oil§r or §bDiesel§r to produce power. Various piston sets exist, which are needed for the engine to work, each one giving its own efficiency bonuses to fuel grades."
		""
		"The §4§3Turbofan§r is the best place to use aviation type fuels, such as §bKerosene§r, as it provides §e100%§r power efficiency. Be careful not to stand infront of it while its operational!"
		""
		"The §3Combined Cycle Gas Turbine§r is the only generator that can burn gaseous fuels at §e100%§r efficiency. The CCGT uses §3§bEngine Lubricant§r, and produces §bDense Steam§r."
		""
		"The §3Flare Stack§r is used for burning gasses such as §bUnsaturated Hydrocarbons§r for power, as well as dealing with excess fluids."
		""
		"The §3Fluid Burner§r is a much more efficient way of producing power from gases. Place a §3Boiler§r ontop and run the §bSteam§r through a turbine to generate power."
		""
		"Consider installing a §6Muffler§r on some of these machines as they are very loud. Shift-Click on a machine while holding a Muffler to apply."
	]
	quest.124E1A876928D343.title: "Refinery Power"
	quest.124E2B0C0BD0C6E1.quest_desc: ["An upgraded version of the §3Anvil§r, [T4], which unlocks additional recipes."]
	quest.124E2B0C0BD0C6E1.title: "Ferrouranium Anvil"
	quest.124ED709C5632299.quest_desc: ["§6Microchips§r are the bread and butter of electronic component crafting. They come in different tiers, for crafting different tiers of components."]
	quest.124ED709C5632299.title: "Microchips"
	quest.126046ADF573BEF7.quest_desc: [
		"The &3Particle Accelerator&r is a highly modular machine that uses high strength superconducting magnets to accelerate particles to relativistic speeds in order to collide them together. For recipes that demand high momentum, additional loops are needed. This quest serves as a guide on how to change the direction of particles."
		""
		"Below is a miniature particle accelerator built for showcasing purposes. It is not connected to power or coolant and does not have any coils. It does not have RF cavities and uses two particle detectors as outputs. A compass is also provided in the image."
		""
		""
		"{image:quests:textures/pa1.png width:427 height:240 align:center}"
		""
		"After constructing your Particle Accelerator, assuming the beamlines face the right directions, head over to the magnet that bridges the first and second loops."
		""
		"{image:quests:textures/pa2.png width:427 height:240 align:center}"
		""
		"Open its GUI and configure the dipole magnet. The first line is for particles that have not reached the desired momentum. The second line is for particles that have reached the desired momentum. The third line is for particles that have reached the desired momentum AND are powered by redstone. The cRed Liner shows the direction the particle will travel towards and the &9Blue Liner show&s where the player is facing."
		""
		"{image:quests:textures/pa3.png width:427 height:240 align:center}"
		""
		"Make sure that for this specific dipole magnet the third line has the particle orientation facing towards the second loop, NORTH in this case."
		""
		"After this, the redstone logic must be set in order to be able to turn the particle orientation when powered. Simply provide power underneath the dipole magnet as such. A redstone signal should only exist when a particle needs momentum greater than what the first tier of coil allows."
		""
		"{image:quests:textures/pa4.png width:427 height:240 align:center}"
		""
		"Head over, WEST in this case, to the dipole magnet which is after the transitionary dipole and right before the detector, and which connects to the rest of the loop."
		""
		"{image:quests:textures/pa5.png width:427 height:240 align:center}"
		""
		"Open its GUI and configure it. Make sure the second line is facing towards the particle detector and the first line towards the other dipole magnets."
		""
		"{image:quests:textures/pa6.png width:427 height:240 align:center}"
		""
		"Due to the complex and expansive nature of the particle accelerator, it is highly recommended that the wiki is checked out as it provides more information."
		""
		"[ { \"text\": \"https://nucleartech.wiki/wiki/Particle_Accelerator\", \"underlined\": true, \"clickEvent\": { \"action\": \"open_url\", \"value\": \"https://nucleartech.wiki/wiki/Particle_Accelerator\" } } ]"
		""
		"&2This quest demands the most essential parts of the particle accelerator, and does not represent the amount needed for it to function.r"
		""
		"Quest requirements: Build a &3Particle Accelerator&r with at least two loops, two dipole magnets, and two particle detectors. Configure the first dipole magnet so its third line faces toward the second loop when powered by redstone. Configure the second dipole magnet so its second line faces the particle detector and its first line faces the other dipole magnets. Provide redstone power underneath the first dipole magnet. Visit the Particle Physics quest chapter."
		""
		"[F1] For more information."
	]
	quest.126046ADF573BEF7.title: "Particle Accelerator"
	quest.1260C4922D63F74C.quest_desc: ["§6Gallium Arsenide§r is made from mixing §6Gallium§r, which can be procured by processing rich mineral deposits from §eMoho§r or §eIke§r, and §6Arsenic§r which is found on Ike in bedrock ore, or on §eEarth§r via dirt and stone that has been damaged by hydraulic fracking."]
	quest.1260C4922D63F74C.title: "Gallium Arsenide"
	quest.126400984FE33B35.quest_desc: ["§3Anvils§r are a tiered crafting station that allows for the creation of various machines, structures, and items in some cases. There are multiple tiers of anvils with greater anvil tier primarily corresponding to a greater quantity of recipes being available."]
	quest.126400984FE33B35.title: "Anvil"
	quest.1268E524C8CC5F87.quest_desc: ["The §6Chicken Nugget§r is the best food item in the mod, completely filling up both hunger and saturation. It is made by colliding 2 raw chickens in a §3Particle Accelerator§r."]
	quest.1268E524C8CC5F87.title: "Chicken Nugget"
	quest.12798C8517E00117.quest_desc: ["§6Osmiridium§r is the second most expensive material and is used primarely in the §3DFC§r."]
	quest.12798C8517E00117.title: "Osmiridium"
	quest.128CDD11DDB9CA43.quest_desc: [
		"§6Rubber§r is an essential material used in many crafting recipes. It is created in a §3Chemical Plant§r with §bUnsaturated Hydrocarbons§r obtained from a §3Catalytic Cracking Tower§r."
		""
		"§6Latex§r is a rubber alternative which can be used in some recipes instead of normal rubber. It can be created early on using a §3Burner Press§r by processing dandelions or jungle wood."
		""
		"§2In NTM: Space cracked oil is required to obtain the first piece of rubber."
	]
	quest.128CDD11DDB9CA43.title: "Rubber"
	quest.1293D0E9C727F2F3.quest_desc: [
		"Well, you've completed the space stage of the game; now the entire space knows and fears you (you are a true space pirate). Here are a couple more nuances about the §3Dyson swarm§r:"
		""
		"§2Do not place §3converters§r directly next to the §3receiver§r - this will cause a malfunction.§r"
		""
		"§2Multiple players in the same game world can create multiple §3swarms§r, but keep in mind that different swarms reduce each other's §eefficiency§r. This can encourage players to either work together on one common §3swarm§r or compete to extract more §eenergy§r from their own §3swarm§r.§r"
	]
	quest.1293D0E9C727F2F3.title: "The End of Space..."
	quest.129DA7B3D4FC6EB0.quest_desc: ["The Air Liquefaction Tower is intended for obtaining liquid nitrogen from compressed air."]
	quest.129DA7B3D4FC6EB0.title: "Armospheric Liquefaction Tower"
	quest.12A3D96CE4C7B4FB.quest_desc: [
		"§3Wireless Connectors§r allow for channel linking without ME cables, making it possible to send channels through walls. The further away the connectors are the more energy consuming they become."
		""
		"A §3Wireless Hub§r can be used to link channels between multiple wireless connectors."
	]
	quest.12A3D96CE4C7B4FB.title: "Wireless Connectors"
	quest.12ADFCC689DEC965.quest_desc: [
		"The §6Hard Disk Drives§r are a higher tier storage medium in OC."
		""
		"All storage media perform at the same speed: higher tier storage provides more space. There are also some devices that can only use disk drives (although servers could use an external disk drive, for example). Hard drives can be placed inside a §3Raid§r, allowing multiple drives to share the same file system. Note that placing a hard drive in a raid wipes the drive of its contents."
	]
	quest.12ADFCC689DEC965.title: "Hard Drives"
	quest.12C569BCFF0CBB96.quest_desc: [
		"Exploration is an important part of the §dNTM§r experience as salvaging abandoned structures is a viable strategy for early game. Large caverns also exist in this modpack, so dont hesistate going caving."
		""
		"§dBackpacks§r will be a massive help, as they can be used to carry around more loot. Crates can also be used to transport items, but backpacks also come packed with dedicated tool slots, a crafting table, a bed aswell as fluid tanks."
		""
		"A §dNature's Compass§r can be used to easily locate biomes of interest."
		""
		"A §6Hose§r can be used to quickly input and output fluids stored in the backpack."
	]
	quest.12C569BCFF0CBB96.title: "Backpacks and Exploration"
	quest.12C632A845C6C0E9.quest_desc: ["§6Technetium-99§r is a common waste product from the fission of §6Uranium§r and §6Plutonium§r. It is mainly used in making §6Technetium Steel§r and §dAE2 Storage Components§r."]
	quest.12C632A845C6C0E9.title: "Technetium-99"
	quest.12CA1559468CA5EE.quest_desc: ["The §6ME Storage Housing§r is the outer shell of a §6Storage Cell§r. There are many tiers of storage cells, all of which require the use of NTM machines to be crafted."]
	quest.12CA1559468CA5EE.title: "Storage Components"
	quest.12D1A4FC157BC1B4.quest_desc: [
		"§l§c§lPainsaw.§r"
		""
		"Although the §6Chainsaw§r is similar in functionality to the §6axe§r, its arsenal is much broader. By default, the saw simply mines blocks, but it also has two additional operating modes: §eSilk Touch§r and §eVein Miner (5)§r."
		""
		"It runs on many types of §bliquid fuel§r (see the item description for a list). Mining one block consumes 1 mB§r of fuel."
		""
		"Besides its primary purpose, the Chainsaw can also serve as a decent melee weapon, as it deals significant damage and has modifiers: §ePainsaw§r and §eDecapitator§r."
	]
	quest.12D1A4FC157BC1B4.title: "Chainsaw"
	quest.12D3123BD92E94F0.quest_desc: [
		"§6Flint Tools§r are required to obtain first wood and stone. Break some tree leaves and get saplings, to recraft them into sticks."
		""
		"Axes automatically break tree blocks from top to bottom to prevent floating trees. Hold Shift to disable this and break blocks normally."
	]
	quest.12D3123BD92E94F0.title: "Flint Tools"
	quest.12DFE55B4E55DDF0.quest_desc: ["The §6M1TTY Environment Suit§r is a cheap electric armor set that comes with many abilities. It is an excellent armor set for exploring as it comes with very high speed buffs as well as fast swimming speed."]
	quest.12DFE55B4E55DDF0.title: "M1TTY Environment Suit"
	quest.12E9393F5917BBE9.quest_desc: ["Screaming doesn't help. You're going in the soup."]
	quest.12E9393F5917BBE9.title: "Time to Kill (Chicken)"
	quest.12EB3296DFC228F1.quest_desc: [
		"§6Bismuth§r is an important material needed in many advanced crafting recipes. Bismuth can be obtained from either §3RBMK§r fuel depletion and processing though a §3FEL§r and §3SILEX§r, or from bedrock ore processing using §bHigh-Performance Solvent§r."
		""
		"§6Arsenic§r will require an additional §bOre Acidizer§r aswell as access to high-performance solvent."
		""
		"§2Due to the lack of bismuth bedrock ore available on earth and the amount of time it takes to process RBMK fuels, it is recommended that some arsenic is used instead of bismuth."
	]
	quest.12EB3296DFC228F1.title: "Bismuth"
	quest.12FEB3CEE4E6C433.quest_desc: [
		"The §3Wood-Burning Generator§r is basic method of producing energy by burning wood. It can run on any burnable items but provides burn time bonuses to logs and wood. It can also run on any flammable fuel by clicking on the arrow below the on/off switch, but it is considerably more inefficient than other fluid burning generators."
		""
		"Burning logs in the generator produces §e2kHE/s.§r"
	]
	quest.12FEB3CEE4E6C433.title: "Wood-Burning Generator"
	quest.13072927A87B7234.quest_desc: ["§6Technetium/Cadmium Steel§r is a steel based alloy mixed with technetium-99/Cadmium which has extreme corrosion resistance. It is frequently used in the late-game and acts as one of the main material gates of the §3Fusion§r and §3Watz§r powerplant."]
	quest.13072927A87B7234.title: "Technetium/Cadmium Steel"
	quest.130F0C97E91D77C4.quest_desc: [
		"The §3Crucible§r is an important machine as it is the central component of metallurgy. It is used as a method of ore processing, alloying, and metal casting. It requires an external heat source to melt the inputs into liquids and when filled, it emits a consistent amount of soot that can cause a fair amount of pollution that cannot be mitigated. Some alloys, as mentioned before, can be made alternatively using a §3Blast Furnace§r, however this is generally slower."
		""
		"[F1] For more information."
	]
	quest.130F0C97E91D77C4.title: "Crucible"
	quest.1310167A06AF8303.quest_desc: ["The §3Plasma Forge§r is a large and advanced assembler that requires a running fusion reactor to work. It can weld plates at twice the speed of a normal welder. It does not accept upgrades, however, it can use up otherwise useless fission fragments and unstable isotopes to gain a temporary §ex4§r speed bonus with no penalty."]
	quest.1310167A06AF8303.title: "Plasma Forge"
	quest.1313749EE1B40CCE.quest_desc: [
		"The §3Firebox§r and the §3Heating Oven§r are machines capable of producing heat from solid fuels for any machines that require heat to operate."
		""
		"Heat is measured in §eTU§r (§eThermal Units§r)."
		""
		"Both machines are similar in operation. In order for them to transfer heat, another machine for receiving the heat must be placed on top, such that the copper heat plate on the receiving machine sits on top of the copper heat plate of the heat producing machine."
		""
		"Once constructed, these machines can be filled with solid fuel, which will burn until either the fuel runs out, or the heat buffer is filled. No fuel will be consumed if its buffer is full - as such, both machines are fairly efficient at conserving fuel."
		""
		"The primary difference in these two machines lie in their speed: the firebox burns fuel much slower at full efficiency, whilst the heating oven produces five time the heat (but eight times faster). Despite its inefficiency, the heating oven is often preferred for its much higher heat outputs and heat capacity. However, it cannot heat a stirling engine, as its base output (500 TU/t) will automatically over-speed the engine; the heavy stirling engine does not have this issue."
		""
		"Additionally, the heating oven can receive heat from other heat producing machines placed underneath it: multiple can be stacked for heat-hungry machines like the crucible. The heat received, however, is halved when transferring to the machine above."
	]
	quest.1313749EE1B40CCE.title: "Heating Oven/Firebox"
	quest.131D9775D2733A9A.quest_desc: [
		"The §6Building Gadget§r is an advanced building tool which allows the user to create many complex shapes with ease. Press the ALT key to open its menu."
		""
		"§2It consumes power for blocks placed.§r"
	]
	quest.131D9775D2733A9A.title: "Building Gadget"
	quest.132540187EDDB198.quest_desc: ["With §dSchematica§r, you can create schematics of your builds and post holograms of them on other worlds. Check out the keybinds to get started."]
	quest.132540187EDDB198.title: "Schematica"
	quest.1334CC35F6B30D11.quest_desc: ["The §6Packing Tape§r allows one to break and move drawers without all the items falling on the floor."]
	quest.1334CC35F6B30D11.title: "Packing Tape"
	quest.13484CF685A4E6B2.quest_desc: [
		"The §6Neutrino Lens§r is an armor modification which can detect and highlight special blocks, such as §eBedrock Ore deposits§r, the §6Pink Log§r and §6Alexandrite§r."
		""
		"For the lens to work, it must first be linked to a §6Depth-Resource Scanning Module Satellite§r and then inserted into an armor piece using the §3Armor Modification Table§r."
		""
		"§2The HUD key has to be activated for it to work."
	]
	quest.13484CF685A4E6B2.title: "Neutrino Lens"
	quest.13508BE0527FC98A.quest_desc: ["Imagine using the same chemical plant for sulfuric acid AND strawberry ice cream production..."]
	quest.13508BE0527FC98A.title: "Strawberry Ice Cream"
	quest.136A504042030C5E.quest_desc: ["The §3Chemical Plant§r is a machine needed for several processes, turning fluids into other fluids, synthesis of different compounds, ect. Like the §3Assembly Machine§r, recipes can be selected entirely within the GUI."]
	quest.136A504042030C5E.title: "Chemical Plant"
	quest.1370FEFF587D7783.quest_desc: [
		"The §3Orbital Precision Laser§r is a solar-powered orbital weapon, a lighter alternative to the §3Orbital Death Ray§r. It fires an instantaneous beam dealing massive damage to entities within a 5-block radius, though its explosive yield is only roughly equivalent to a single block of TNT. Recharge time between shots is §e5 seconds§r."
		""
		"It can be aimed with a §6Satellite (Laser) Designator§r or controlled via §dRedstone-over-Radio§r through a §3Satellite Ground Station§r. The \"fire\" command fires at the current target coordinates, or at a tracked entity if one has been set - entity target data is consumed after a single shot. The \"canfire\" command writes TRUE or FALSE to RX depending on whether the laser has finished recharging. The \"setentitytarget\" command accepts an entity ID from a §3Radar Satellite§r for precision tracking."
		""
		"§2Entity target data is consumed after one shot, reverting back to coordinate targeting."
	]
	quest.1370FEFF587D7783.title: "Orbital Precision Laser"
	quest.13757997FC9E7B4E.quest_desc: ["§6Euphemium§r is a fictional material which serves as one of the mod's most endgame materials. It's extremely expensive to produce in large amounts and you will need great advancement through the mod to use it effectively."]
	quest.13757997FC9E7B4E.title: "Euphemium"
	quest.137BCC2C5A54599A.quest_desc: [
		"The §3Vehicle Assembly Base§r is a structure which is one of the most vital parts of your space-faring efforts. It'll allow you to stack your rockets and plan out each segment of your journey. Note that each rocket stage allows for one launch from a celestial body to another, so a two-stage rocket can make a round-trip between, say, the Earth and the Mun."
		""
		"The §3Rocket Launch Pad§r is the only launch pad capable of supporting the various fuel loads and complex requirements of the stacked rockets. This is the only way to fuel up a rocket too, so you'll want to make multiple stages for launching from bodies without a pad. The pad itself has a GUI that'll indicate what your rocket requires to be launched."
	]
	quest.137BCC2C5A54599A.title: "Rocket Assembling and Launching"
	quest.137FA826DC4CEA15.quest_desc: [
		"The §3Chemical Factory§r is a large version of the §3Chemical Plant§r, capable of performing 4 recipes in parallel. It has double the speed of the chemical plant but consumes twice as much power. Additionally, it consumes §bWater§r as a coolant, and produces §bLow-Pressure Steam§r, so a closed water cycle is recommended."
		""
		"The §3Assembly Factory§r is a large version of the §3Assembly Machine§r, capable of performing 4 recipes in parallel. It functions the same as the chemical factory."
	]
	quest.137FA826DC4CEA15.title: "Large Factory Multiblocks"
	quest.138672EC33099524.quest_desc: ["While it is possible to travel here with only a tier 2 drive processor to exploit the incredibly powerful schrabidic resources that exist here, players will not last long without the appropriate armor inserts, due to the highly corrosive atmosphere melting any armor it comes into contact with."]
	quest.138672EC33099524.title: "Eve"
	quest.13964C38F04E1ACA.quest_desc: [
		"The §3Cyclotron§r is a machine that bombards element powders with element boxes to get heavier elements. Operating the machine will consume§e 20MHE/s§r."
		""
		"It can also create §bAntimatter§r as a byproduct for certain operations, which makes it a reliable but expensive method of large-scale advanced material production."
		""
		"§2Consider installing the highest level of Power Saving and Speed upgrades to reduce both recipe time and power consumption.§r"
	]
	quest.13964C38F04E1ACA.title: "Cyclotron"
	quest.139899A8DB38189D.quest_desc: ["With the §3Nuclear Waste Disposal Drum§r to decay waste and a §3SILEX§r, §3RBMK§r nuclear fuels can be processed into many new materials."]
	quest.139899A8DB38189D.title: "RBMK Fuel Processing"
	quest.13A3F9697D34C768.quest_desc: [
		"The §6Geiger counter§r is a device used to measure §eRAD/s§r, in order to inform the player of any eventual radiation. It is an upgrade to the §6Dosimeter§r. It can measure three different types of radiation, those types being chunk radiation, environmental radiation and player contamination."
		""
		"It can be used in one of two forms, either as a hand-held item or in its block form."
		""
		"Holding it in the inventory will show a meter on the bottom left of the screen, and right clicking while holding it will send a message in chat showing the various doses of radiation."
		""
		"It will also click whenever it reads any kind of radiation, a signature function of any dosimeter."
	]
	quest.13A3F9697D34C768.title: "Geiger Counter"
	quest.13A9691F1810525F.quest_desc: [
		"The §3ME Export Bus§r is an ME component which is used to export items from the ME network into a machine or other input inventory."
		""
		"The §3ME Import Bus§r is an ME component which is used to import items directly into the ME Network from a machine or other output inventory."
		""
		"§2It is recommended that Interfaces are used over Export/Import buses for performance reasons."
	]
	quest.13A9691F1810525F.title: "ME Buses"
	quest.13AE801D18F056ED.quest_desc: [
		"The §3Radiation-Powered Engine§r turns nuclear waste into decayed waste while also making energy in the process and giving guaranteed consistent decay times."
		""
		"§2Blueprints can be found in structures or purchased from Bobmazon."
	]
	quest.13AE801D18F056ED.title: "Radiation-Powered Engine"
	quest.13B0022594EEE664.quest_desc: [
		"§6Semtex§r is an explosive that is used in conjunction with C-4 in many crafts."
		""
		"Semtex is used in many crafts of various ammunition and mines, such as the §6Stinger missile§r, §6anti-personnel mines§r, and so on. In all crafts that use Semtex (except, of course, the Semtex block and Semtex bar, as well as the explosive reactive armor plate), it can be replaced with a C-4 bar."
		""
		"It is used to create the bomb of the same name."
		""
		"§2Semtex can be eaten, making you feel like a real American soldier.§r"
	]
	quest.13B0022594EEE664.title: "Semtex"
	quest.13BE53B8513351C3.quest_desc: ["The §3High-Power Steam Condenser§r is the a steam condenser which runs on electricity. It processes up to 60 mB/t of §bLow-Pressure Steam§r."]
	quest.13BE53B8513351C3.title: "High-Power Steam Condenser"
	quest.13CADE131CBE795F.quest_desc: ["The §3Soldering Station§r is the machine in which §6§rcircuit components§r can be combined§6§r into §6Circuits§r and where §6Machine Upgrades§r can be created."]
	quest.13CADE131CBE795F.title: "Soldering Station"
	quest.13DC67C439AD0F75.quest_desc: [
		"Phew, that was quite a journey... Hopefully there is more to come with some modpack updates!"
		""
		"Now [warn]GO TOUCH SOME GRASS IMMIDIATELY[/warn]."
		""
		"§6§lRATE OUR MODPACK: §r[url]https://moddex.gg/modpack/ntnewhorizons[/url]"
	]
	quest.13DC67C439AD0F75.title: "§cDone"
	quest.13EE54015429D15C.quest_desc: ["The §3Player Decontaminator§r will remove Rads received while standing on it. It can be very cost efficient, as other methods such as §6RadAways§r require constant replenishment."]
	quest.13EE54015429D15C.title: "Player Decontaminator"
	quest.13F319A6007FCEB7.quest_desc: ["The §3Industrial Steam Turbine§r is a multiblock machine that is a much larger and more powerful version of the regular §3Steam Turbine§r. It has an efficiency of §e100%§r and energy output slowly ramps up as §bSteam§r is supplied and slowly goes down as steam cuts out."]
	quest.13F319A6007FCEB7.title: "Industrial Steam Turbine"
	quest.13F684024916E1C6.quest_desc: ["The §6Transistor§r is one of the most basic crafting ingredients in OC. It is mainly used to craft §6Microchips§r and other electronic goods."]
	quest.13F684024916E1C6.title: "Transistors"
	quest.13FB49C33C15B448.quest_desc: ["A fair-dinkum planet, hot as hell, and full of rare resources generally only found in the Nether. §6Australium§r is only found here, in vast quantities deep under the surface. Some of the largest caves ever generated within Minecraft can be found here."]
	quest.13FB49C33C15B448.title: "Moho"
	quest.1406B750A11B107E.quest_desc: ["§dRandomThings§r adds §cBlood Moons§r, semi-rare events where mob spawning is increased and the player cant sleep. Blood Moons can be quite useful, if one is prepared, as rare mob drops such as §6Launch Codes§r and §6Geiger Counters§r can be obtained early on."]
	quest.1406B750A11B107E.title: "Blood Moon"
	quest.140DD343784A0DEE.quest_desc: ["The §3Strand Caster§r is a large basin that can cast items in batches of 9. It also requires §bWater§r in order to cast, where it makes §bLow-Pressure Steam§r that can be turned back into water."]
	quest.140DD343784A0DEE.title: "Strand Caster"
	quest.1423D9BD65BD7C4E.quest_desc: [
		"The §3Solar Panel§r converts sunlight into §eelectricity§r. §2(Incredible)§r"
		""
		"It can operate on planet surfaces or in space. The device uses the general light level, so the panel's spatial orientation does not affect energy production. The energy output port is at the back."
		""
		"§2Energy production calculations for planets and their orbits:"
		""
		"Kerbin - §e2kHE/s§2"
		"Mun - §e2kHE/s§2"
		"Minmus - §e2kHE/s§2"
		"Duna - §e880HE/s§2"
		"Ike - §e880HE/s§2"
		"Moho - §e13.3kHE/s§2"
		"Dres - §e240HE/s§2"
		"Eve - §e3.84kHE/s§2"
		"Laythe - §e80HE/s§r"
	]
	quest.1423D9BD65BD7C4E.title: "Solar Panel"
	quest.1428943087D73C2B.quest_desc: ["The §3Drive Processor Tier 3§r allows for travel to §eLaythe§r."]
	quest.1428943087D73C2B.title: "Drive Processor Tier 3"
	quest.142AFEC0C7E52B31.quest_desc: [
		"The §6Wireless Network Card§r is an upgraded §6Network Card§r that can send and receive wireless network messages."
		""
		"Tier two cards can also send and receive wired messages. The signal strength directly controls the distance up to which a sent message can be received, where the strength is equal to the distance in blocks."
	]
	quest.142AFEC0C7E52B31.title: "Wireless Network Card"
	quest.142F52C6EAEEC1C4.quest_desc: ["The §3Alkylation Unit§r is designed to convert lighter hydrocarbons into useful heavier hydrocarbon products. From §bNatural Gas§r it can produce §bUnsaturated§r and §bAromatic hydrocarbons§r, commonly used for §6Rubber§r and §6Bakelite§r, and even produce §bBTX§r via the use of §bHigh-Performance Solvent§r. As a utility, it can also alkylate §bPetroleum Gas§r into §bLight Oil§r."]
	quest.142F52C6EAEEC1C4.title: "Alkylation Unit"
	quest.1436858517EA6758.quest_desc: ["The §3Oil Derrick§r extracts §bCrude Oil§r and §6§bNatural Gas§r from §eOil Deposits§r that are directly below them. When supplied with power, it will begin to drill downwards until it cannot drill further or reach an oil deposit. Upon reaching a deposit, it will continuously extract oil and gas from it until the deposit is entirely depleted."]
	quest.1436858517EA6758.title: "Derrick"
	quest.146CFB74FCD81EFF.quest_desc: ["The §3Ore Acidizer§r is a useful machine, used for processing various items for utility, ore multiplication, and more. It is powered by electricity and requires various solvents depending on the item. The acidizer is quite the power hungry machine, consuming §e20kHE/s§r."]
	quest.146CFB74FCD81EFF.title: "Ore Acidizer"
	quest.1474327D6E24C94F.quest_desc: [
		"The §3Watz§r powerplant is a fission reactor which can produce §bPoisonous Mud§r, an important component of §6CMB Steel§r. Although the reactor is not really powerful in terms of energy output, it can be stacked ontop of eachother for increased mud and power production."
		""
		"If the poisonous mud buffer reaches its maximum, the reactor will melt down and explode, irradiating a wide area around it and causing fallout to fall in a small area around it. As well as this, it will spew poisonous mud in a very wide area which will then corrode any blocks that it comes in contact with, similar to corium."
	]
	quest.1474327D6E24C94F.title: "Watz Powerplant"
	quest.147529F89B8D0AB1.quest_desc: [
		"For greater distances, and improved aesthetics, a new distribution node is available, the §3Large Electricity Pylon§r."
		""
		"§3Substations§r are needed to step up/down the voltage that the line carries."
		""
		"These Pylons can prove useful as favorable §eBedrock Ore§r or §eOil deposits§r may be located far away from the main base."
	]
	quest.147529F89B8D0AB1.title: "Long Distance Energy Transportation"
	quest.148EC0A09562DAB7.quest_desc: ["The §3Armor Modification Table§r allows for armor modifications to be inserted in armor, giving either buffs, new abilities or extra resistance."]
	quest.148EC0A09562DAB7.title: "Armor Modifications"
	quest.149574CC52FADE48.quest_desc: [
		"Tired of using buckets to give §bWater§r to your machines? Try using water pumps or infinite water tanks!"
		""
		"§6Infinite Water Tank§r will give §e50mb/t"
		""
		"§6Enhanced Infinite Water Tank§r will give §e500mb/t"
		""
		"§6Steam-Powered Groundwater Pump§r will give §e1000mb/t§r but requires §bSteam§r to operate (which is obvious)."
	]
	quest.149574CC52FADE48.title: "Infinite Water Sources"
	quest.149638C548C9CF72.quest_desc: [
		"The §6Building Wand§r allows one to place many blocks at once, making walls and roads easier to construct. The stronger material the wand is made out of, the more blocks it can place."
		""
		"§2To replace water blocks using wands bind the key, Change Fluid Mode, in settings."
	]
	quest.149638C548C9CF72.title: "Better Builder's Wands"
	quest.14A3CDC3DA189131.quest_desc: [
		"Gimme yo §oSkuuuuull!!!§r <-- The thought of every non-noob player upon seeing one."
		""
		"BTW, in case you didn't know, you can summon the Wither by placing 4 soul sand blocks in a T shape, with 3 wither skulls on top. Don't do so in your base."
	]
	quest.14A3CDC3DA189131.title: "Time to Kill (Wither Skeleton)"
	quest.14B3CBCF9CE76461.quest_desc: ["The §6Book of Boxcars§r is an item which allows the crafting of many special items. The book can be found inside §eMeteorite Dungeons§r found randomly in the wilderness on extra-terrestial bodies, indicated by a black pillar, or in §eRed Rooms§r."]
	quest.14B3CBCF9CE76461.title: "The Book of Boxcars"
	quest.14B3F3CBDD44B1B9.quest_desc: [
		"§6The Nether§r is §c§lACTUALLY HOT§r causing your skin to burn."
		""
		"§6Fire Proximity Armor Set§r is essential for your first Nerther trip, as it protects you from burning fire."
	]
	quest.14B3F3CBDD44B1B9.title: "Highway To Hell"
	quest.14B7C33191DA6CBB.quest_desc: [
		"The §3Launch Pad§r is the main launch table for most missiles. Although it is the earliest available, missiles must first be erected before launch, resulting in a small delay."
		""
		"The §3Silo Launch Pad§r is a miniaturized version of the launch pad. It can launch every generic missile with a delay of only 5 seconds. A rusted variant can be found in the naturally-occurring silo structure, holding the damaged Doomsday Missile."
	]
	quest.14B7C33191DA6CBB.title: "Launch Pad"
	quest.14B8CB44BA49B571.quest_desc: ["The §6Schrabidium Hammer§r is the most powerful weapon in the mod, being able to one-shot everything."]
	quest.14B8CB44BA49B571.title: "Schrabidium Hammer"
	quest.14CDB54FC0B3D4A6.quest_desc: [
		"The §3ICF§r can process different combinations of fuels at different laser power levels. A cheap and renewable fuel that can be used to gather the §bStellar Flux§r needed for §6Gerald§r and make decent power is §bHelium-4 - Hydrogen§r."
		""
		"Applying a Muon Particle to a fuel pellet will decrease the power that is needed to run it."
	]
	quest.14CDB54FC0B3D4A6.title: "ICF Fuels"
	quest.14CE9C57F7AA5BE9.quest_desc: ["Balls-O-Tron is the second boss of NTM. It can be summoned by interracting the Mechanist's circle, found in the Enargite Temple which spawns in jungles, with a Silver Key, made using the Maskman Coin."]
	quest.14CE9C57F7AA5BE9.title: "Balls-O-Tron"
	quest.14DEA2D48669119E.quest_desc: ["Particles are important items required to create exotic materials which are needed for most of the endgame content."]
	quest.14DEA2D48669119E.title: "Particle Capsules"
	quest.14E6D093CE6B3A3A.quest_desc: ["The §6Spark Laser Crystal§r unlocks new recipes, most importantly it is used to create §6Osmiridium§r."]
	quest.14E6D093CE6B3A3A.title: "Spark Laser Crystal"
	quest.14EF349DF57A4FD1.quest_desc: ["§6Polymer§r is a basic plastic material needed for many recipes. Important uses of it are the §3Centrifuge§r, the §3Catalytic Cracking Tower§r and the §3Electric Arc Furnace§r."]
	quest.14EF349DF57A4FD1.title: "Polymer"
	quest.14F0F01AD51B3790.quest_desc: ["§6Microchips§r are one of the most important components of future circuits and will be used in bulk throughout progression."]
	quest.14F0F01AD51B3790.title: "Microchip"
	quest.15126D47206D79A2.quest_desc: [
		"The §3Narrowband Emission Scanning Satellite§r precisely locates specific high-energy events within a 250-meter radius of a target point. It is the high-precision counterpart to the §3Wideband Radio Emission Detector Satellite§r, sensitive to: neutron radiation from nuclear reactors, high-energy particles from fusion reactors and particle accelerators, radar waves from ground radars, and radio waves from §3Satellite Ground Stations§r with an active TX signal."
		""
		"All results are stored internally and accessed via §dRedstone-over-Radio§r. \"esurvey\" performs the scan. \"ecount\" writes the result count to RX. \"egetinfo\" followed by an index writes the emission type to RX. \"egetposition\" followed by an index writes the X/Z coordinates - separated by a semicolon - to RX."
		""
		"§2Events are time-limited. Run repeated scans at short intervals to avoid missing short-lived emissions."
	]
	quest.15126D47206D79A2.title: "Narrowband Emission Scanning Satellite"
	quest.151411F4648B6033.quest_desc: ["Now you are ready to fully begin your journey in this modpack! Happy gaming!"]
	quest.151411F4648B6033.title: "The Actual Beginning"
	quest.1529AE15C634AE82.quest_desc: ["Be meaner."]
	quest.1529AE15C634AE82.title: "Delinquent 2: Delinquent Harder"
	quest.152F828FD36DEC33.quest_desc: ["By having an orbital station have an §3Orbital Station Computer§r and §3Drop Pods§r, one can move their station to any destination they wish, massively cutting down on material costs needed to make new rockets."]
	quest.152F828FD36DEC33.title: "Mobile Orbital Station"
	quest.1532FDB5C13D2798.quest_desc: ["§6CMB Steel§r is an alloy made from §6Poisonous Mud§r and §6Magnetized Tunsten§r in a §3Crucible§r. This alloy is used in endgame machinery, such as the §3ICF§r and §3DFC§r."]
	quest.1532FDB5C13D2798.title: "CMB Steel"
	quest.154CE1240E041B94.quest_desc: ["§3Drive Processor Tier 1§r allows for travel to §eDuna§r, §eIke§r and §eMoho§r."]
	quest.154CE1240E041B94.title: "Drive Processor Tier 1"
	quest.154EBC9944C88F36.quest_desc: [
		"The §6Dense ME Fluix Cables§r can be used to transmit §e32 channels§r from an §3ME Controller§r."
		""
		"One controller is capable of connecting up to 6 dense cables, in turn each can branch off to 4 smaller cable lines connecting up to 192 ME devices to the network."
		""
		"The §6Smart Dense Cable§r also displays the amount of channels that are been used, but is known to be less performance friendly than the dense covered cables."
		""
		"In addition there are 16 colored cables made with the appropriate dye. The colored cables allow contact with other cables without sharing the signal or connecting to any other cable but the ones of the same colour."
	]
	quest.154EBC9944C88F36.title: "Dense ME Cable"
	quest.154F40394DA63BBA.quest_desc: [
		"§3Conveyors§r provide the simplest way of moving items around. There are multiple blocks that can interface with machines as well as items moving along conveyor belts."
		""
		"§3Conveyor Belts§r are blocks used to transport items. They can pick up dropped items or items from conveyor ejectors. Conveyor inserters can take items from conveyor belts. If there are no conveyor inserters present, the item will be dropped at the end of the conveyor belt line."
		"{@pagebreak}"
		"§3Conveyor Inserters§r are blocks that take items from conveyor belts and outputs them into a storage space. Conveyor ejectors are the opposite, they take items from storage and place them onto conveyor belts."
		""
		"Inserters have an option to destroy surplus items if the input buffer has run full, otherwise the items that can neither be inserted in the target nor the inserter's buffer is simply dropped."
		""
		"The ejector has a whitelist/blacklist system (the default mode is blacklist with no restrictions - this means that everything will go through). Right-clicking the white arrow will toggle between whitelist and blacklist. An item can be added to the blacklist/whitelist by \"depositing\" it into the blue inventory square - the item will not be consumed, however."
		"{@pagebreak}"
		"The §3Conveyor Splitter§r is a type of conveyor belt that splits items evenly onto 2 lanes."
		""
		"§3Conveyor Sorters§r are blocks that can sort various items to a specific conveyor belt. They do not have a buffer and simple move items to connected conveyor belts based on their filter options, therefore they can sort items as quickly as they receive them."
		"The sorter has six outputs with five slots each, making it able to route multiple items to one belt."
	]
	quest.154F40394DA63BBA.title: "Conveyor Belt"
	quest.15505F72B7625FC2.quest_desc: [
		"The §6ME Glass Cable - Fluix§r is a cable used to transmit data and energy between devices in an ME Network. It is capable of transmitting §f§e8 channels§r simultaneously."
		""
		"The §6Quartz Fiber§r is used to transfer energy, but not channels."
		""
		"§6Cable Anchors§r can be used to seperate ME cable connections. They can also be used to make §6Facades§r for the cables."
	]
	quest.15505F72B7625FC2.title: "Cable Fluix"
	quest.1554D2E89B37FC27.quest_desc: ["The §3FenSU§r is the ultimate energy storage block, being able to store §k1239217§rTHE."]
	quest.1554D2E89B37FC27.title: "FEnSU"
	quest.15579FA7A501BBCD.quest_desc: [
		"Who hasn't experienced this... You're just minding your own business, mining a few diamonds, and suddenly, you wake up in your bed, all your items gone."
		""
		"Time to strike back!"
	]
	quest.15579FA7A501BBCD.title: "Time to Kill (Creeper)"
	quest.155BC9D06D378648.quest_desc: ["After collecting a couple of those wither skeleton heads, you feel like you could use some more action. So why not kill a wither?"]
	quest.155BC9D06D378648.title: "Time to Kill (Wither)"
	quest.1576172D732179BB.quest_desc: [
		"The §6Impact Drill§r is an electric pickaxe which has prebuilt enchantments and abilities on it. It is a very useful tool which will make mining way more efficient."
		""
		"Similar electric tools exist for the axe and shovel."
	]
	quest.1576172D732179BB.title: "Impact Drill"
	quest.157FC9BEE28872ED.quest_desc: ["The §3Air Intake§r, when powered, produces §bCompressed Air§r needed in §3Pneumatic Pipes§r and §bHot Air Blast§r."]
	quest.157FC9BEE28872ED.title: "Air Intake"
	quest.15844E2EDE82DBD1.quest_desc: [
		"The §3Diesel Generator§r is a compact, single-block generator that burns liquid fuels to produce energy. Its small footprint and compatibility with common oil-processing byproducts make it a strong choice for early- and mid-game power."
		""
		"It holds up to §b4,000 mB§r of fluid internally, consumed at a steady rate of §e20 mB/s§r. It also carries a §e50 kHE§r energy buffer - but combustion does not pause when the buffer is full, so any excess energy is wasted. To avoid this, ensure your machines are drawing power consistently."
		""
		"Fuel can be supplied via fluid ducts or by placing barrels in the internal item slots. A §6Fluid Identifier§r can be inserted to lock the accepted fuel type. Not all fuels are equal - effectiveness varies by grade: medium-grade fuels run at §e50%%§r efficiency, high-grade at §e75%§r, and aviation fuels at just §e10%§r. Low-grade and gaseous fuels are rejected entirely."
		""
		"§2Tip: High-grade fuels like diesel, gasoline, and biofuel get the best return - prioritize refining your oil into these where possible.§r"
	]
	quest.15844E2EDE82DBD1.title: "Diesel Generator"
	quest.1585858020F8ADF2.quest_desc: [
		"The §3Sieve§r filters gravel, dirt, stone, and other blocks to yield useful material fragments - including iron, copper, lead, and more."
		""
		"Use §3Heavy Sieve§r with §6Compressed Blocks§r to get more fragments."
		""
		"§2Use NEI to list all possible drops."
	]
	quest.1585858020F8ADF2.title: "Sieving"
	quest.158C3E4560D27092.quest_desc: ["The §3Vacuum Solderer§r is a machine that can only function in a vacuum, and produces vacuum circuits. They can be placed into the §3Drive Processor§r to enable it to process higher tier planetary drives."]
	quest.158C3E4560D27092.title: "Vacuum Solderer"
	quest.158F241ADC7F3B8F.quest_desc: [
		"The §3Energy Acceptor§r transfers energy into the ME system. In combination with an §3HE to RF Converter§r, the ME system can be powered."
		""
		"[img height=1000]betterquesting:textures/QB_EnergyAcceptor.png[/img]"
	]
	quest.158F241ADC7F3B8F.title: "Energy Acceptor"
	quest.1593D9BEA2DF9311.quest_desc: ["§bHelium-4§r is a product of fusion and is mainly used in crafting §6Quantum Processing Units§r."]
	quest.1593D9BEA2DF9311.title: "Helium-4"
	quest.159A9D1CA1864B33.quest_desc: ["The§3 Murky Anvil§r is the ultimate version of the §3Anvil§r, having all recipes unlocked."]
	quest.159A9D1CA1864B33.title: "Murky Anvil"
	quest.159BA733F40B9A17.quest_desc: [
		"§6Certus Quartz§r is an important material in AE2. It is dropped when mining or processing certus quartz ore at the rate of one to four, the yield is affected by a tool's Fortune enchantment. Certus Quartz is often interchangeable with vanilla §6Nether Quartz§r in the recipes for basic tools, such as the §6Quartz Cutting Knife§r. Certus quartz ore can be acidized or centrifuged for an increased yield."
		""
		"§2Certus quartz can later be made in a Chemical Plant using nether quartz."
	]
	quest.159BA733F40B9A17.title: "Certus Quartz Crystal"
	quest.15B8D3F0F84DC3A3.quest_desc: [
		"The §3Fusion Reactor§r is a large, expensive, and advanced reactor type that runs by fusing various plasma types to generate heat."
		""
		"The main part of the fusion reactor, the §3\"Torus\"§r, features four connecting ports for external components. It requires electricity and §bPerfluoromethyl§r cooling to operate."
		""
		"The §3Klystron§r is the main power source of the fusion reactor, which uses electricity and compressed air, to generate input energy, §eKyU§r, for the connected torus. It will throttle if the buffered electricity or compressed air falls below §e50%§r, and if it falls below the torus' required input level, the plasma will extinguish."
		""
		"The different plasma types also generate different useful byproducts and differing levels of neutron flux for breeding bulk quantities of materials, such as §6Lithium§r into §6Tritium§r."
		""
		"Welding the coils will require a §6Blowtorch§r or an §6Acetylene Welding Torch§r."
		""
		"§2For the additional components and power generation methods, please check out the two quests below.§r"
	]
	quest.15B8D3F0F84DC3A3.title: "Fusion Reactor"
	quest.15BE98285A04AD99.quest_desc: ["The §6Spark Singularity§r is a singularity made from combining all the types of singularities with §6Dineutronium§r."]
	quest.15BE98285A04AD99.title: "Spark Singularity"
	quest.15CC8CDD6556CD11.quest_desc: [
		"§6Balefire§r is an extremely radioactive substance which can be used to make powerful fuels for the §3RBMK§r, aswell as §bBF Rocket Fuel§r for power production. High radiation resistant equipment is needed to hold the item. §6Thermonuclear Ashes§r can be produced sustainably as a byproduct from §bAntimatter - BF Rocket Fuel§r."
		""
		"The High-Tech Bomb Defusing Device can extract balefire shards from duds."
	]
	quest.15CC8CDD6556CD11.title: "Balefire"
	quest.15E328778F0C09AB.quest_desc: ["§bAntimatter§r is a dangerous substance which can be obtained from a §3Cyclotron§r or a §3Particle Accelerator§r. If dropped on the floor a violent explosion will occur. Antimatter cant be stored in normal tanks, and as such, a §3Magnetic Antimatter Container§r is required."]
	quest.15E328778F0C09AB.title: "Antimatter"
	quest.15E8CF183BDFD608.quest_desc: [
		"What's with the §6numbers in the corner§r? That is the §dIn-Game Info (IGI)§r mod. Some of the info it gives is useful right away, some of it shines later on in progression."
		""
		"If you want to hide it, type \"§6/igi disable§r\"§r in the chat. Type \"§6/igi enable§r\" if you want to turn it back on."
		""
		"The command \"§6/igi config§r\" opens the configuration window to control its position, scale, and size."
		""
		"If you need suggestions on solving TPS/FPS problems, feel free to ask for help in the NTNH Discord."
	]
	quest.15E8CF183BDFD608.title: "Numbers in the Corner?"
	quest.15EA29F3222F1519.quest_desc: ["§6Chlorophyte§r is a product of fusion and is used in the §3DFC§r and §6Digamma Particle§r."]
	quest.15EA29F3222F1519.title: "Chlorophyte"
	quest.15EE2AD0762B1209.quest_desc: ["§6Desh Stamps§r have infinite durability, perfect for automation."]
	quest.15EE2AD0762B1209.title: "Desh Stamps"
	quest.15F342A815796661.quest_desc: [
		"The §3Catalytic Reformer§r is an optional late-game oil processing machine. It converts certain oil products into more valuable ones."
		""
		"The §3Hydrotreater§r is another optional late-game oil processing machine that allows for easier production of §bSour Gas§r, which can also turn §bCrude Oil§r into §bDesulfurized crude Oil§r."
		""
		"§2The Hydrotreater requires pressurized Liquid Hydrogen in all its recipes, requiring the use of a Compressor."
	]
	quest.15F342A815796661.title: "Advanced Oil Processing"
	quest.15FEBE7C6CDFB04E.quest_desc: ["§6Desh Servos§r are an armor modification which give incredibely strong buffs when used, such as increased strength, mining speed and jump boost."]
	quest.15FEBE7C6CDFB04E.title: "Desh Servo Set"
	quest.1601176D41816E77.quest_desc: [
		"The §6Hammer§r is a tool from §dEx Nihilo§r used to crush blocks down into finer forms. Its primary role is producing the materials needed for the §3Sieve§r: cobblestone is crushed into gravel, gravel into sand, and sand into dust, each of which can be sieved for different resources."
		""
		"To use it, simply break a target block with the §6Hammer§r as you would with a pickaxe. Hammers come in the standard tool tiers -"
		"wood through diamond - and differ only in durability. They can be enchanted, though the available enchantments differ from those on a pickaxe."
		""
		"Ores can also be hammered down through a multi-step crushing chain. Each step has a small chance to yield bonus"
		"material, making the §6Hammer§r a basic form of ore multiplication before dedicated processing machines are available."
		""
		"§2Hammering can be automated with machines that simulate block breaking, such as the Auto Hammer from §dEx Compressum§r§2."
		"§2Check NEI for the full crushing chain of any block."
	]
	quest.1601176D41816E77.title: "Nailed It!"
	quest.1615BC084F234557.quest_desc: [
		"The §3Shredder§r is a machine that shreds resourses into their powder form, or in many cases, their crafting materials. It can also be used to double ores."
		""
		"§2Shredder blades are required in order for the machine to work."
	]
	quest.1615BC084F234557.title: "Shredder"
	quest.1620C68FD039CDDD.quest_desc: ["§6Bauxide§r and §6Cryolite§r can be further processed to obtain §6Aluminium§r, with additional byproducts of §6Iron§r, §6Titanium§r and §bMercury§r."]
	quest.1620C68FD039CDDD.title: "Aluminium Processing"
	quest.16296724D8FA9CCE.quest_desc: ["The §6Oil Reservoir Detector§r will help one in the search for an §eOil Deposit§r by pointing it out in chat. If the oil deposit is located very far away, it can be mined and moved to a stationary oil refinery."]
	quest.16296724D8FA9CCE.title: "From Flint to Oil - USA Simulator"
	quest.162CEDB1FAD34702.quest_desc: ["The §3Cryogenic Distillation Machine§r can split atmospheric gases into 4 useful fractions, like for example, taking trace amounts of §bNitrogen§r out of the Dunaian atmosphere to produce soil for planting crops."]
	quest.162CEDB1FAD34702.title: "Cryogenic Distillation Machine"
	quest.1640A1421750011E.quest_desc: ["The §3Heavy Magnetic Storage Tank§r is a large version of the §3Magnetic Antimatter Container§r. It will be particularly useful when making §6Gerald§r, as he will need very large quantities of §bStellar Flux§r."]
	quest.1640A1421750011E.title: "Heavy Magnetic Storage Tank"
	quest.16474CB292CE162D.quest_desc: ["§3Transport Drones§r are flying machines which will transport items and fluids between different containers. The drones require no power, and can transport both up and down. §3Waypoints§r can be used to make a better path for the transport drones to move around."]
	quest.16474CB292CE162D.title: "Transport Drones"
	quest.1648169A3B4DC5AA.quest_desc: [
		"The §6Cable Network Analysis Tool§r is used to check the integrity of power grids and analyze their main functional components. To perform a test, right-click the analyzer on wires or mechanisms in the power grid. The device displays the following data:"
		""
		"§eLinks§r - these include wires and mechanisms that can conduct energy (e.g., energy storage units, utility poles)."
		""
		"§cProviders§r - all mechanisms capable of producing energy and/or feeding it into the grid (energy storage units in \"§agreen§r\" and \"§6orange§r\" modes, turbines, etc.)."
		""
		"§9Receivers§r - everything that absorbs energy from the grid (energy storage units in \"§9blue§r\" mode, grinders, and other mechanisms)."
		""
		"§2The analyzer not only displays the above components but also counts them. Each grid is assigned a unique code."
		""
		"Particles only spawn in a 20 block radius!"
	]
	quest.1648169A3B4DC5AA.title: "Cable Network Analysis Tool"
	quest.165D09DA90F1ACD2.quest_desc: ["Uh, fancy teleport pearls. You need them. All of them. Now!"]
	quest.165D09DA90F1ACD2.title: "Time to Kill (Enderman)"
	quest.166AE7BBD498483B.quest_desc: [
		"§dHunger Overhaul§r makes hunger a genuine threat rather than a mild inconvenience."
		""
		"Hunger now drains passively over time, even while idle. Reaching zero kills you instantly. Low hunger inflicts slowness, weakness, and reduced mining speed before that point. Eating grants a §6Well Fed§r effect that boosts health regeneration - the larger the meal, the longer it lasts."
		""
		"Food values are re-balanced by meal size. Raw ingredients restore very little; prepared meals restore substantially more. Larger meals take longer to eat and stack less in your inventory."
		""
		"Crops only grow during daytime and take much longer to mature. Wood and stone hoes are removed - you need at least an iron hoe to till soil. Farmland must be placed adjacent to water or it will not function."
		""
		"§dSpice of Life: Carrot Edition§r rewards dietary variety. Each unique food eaten for the first time permanently increases your maximum health. Eating the same food repeatedly provides no bonus."
		""
		"§2The more diverse your diet, the more hearts you have - build a varied farm as early as possible.§r"
	]
	quest.166AE7BBD498483B.title: "Hunger System"
	quest.167385714CBD8EBE.quest_desc: [
		"The most basic block for transmission is the §3Red Copper Cable§r, which comes in two varieties, a block form and a skinnier cable form. The block form also has a paintable version which can help it blend into your designs better."
		""
		"For better looking, as well as longer distance energy transportation, a §l§r§6Cable Drum§r with §3Electricity Connectors§r can be used. These powerlines are non solid and can also pass through floors and walls."
	]
	quest.167385714CBD8EBE.title: "Energy Cables"
	quest.1682E1F78D40C0F5.quest_desc: ["Maskman is the first NTM boss. To summon it, you need to be under radiation poisoning (50 rad). A 20-minute timer starts per player when requirements are met. Once it runs out, Mask Man spawns. A warning appears 1 minute before spawn. If you are no longer irradiated, the timer resets."]
	quest.1682E1F78D40C0F5.title: "Maskman"
	quest.168E6FF329367EC5.quest_desc: [
		"The §3DFC§r is the last reactor of the mod and as such is very expensive to craft. Apart from the DFC parts, two §6Catalysts§r are needed for the reactor to work."
		""
		"It is recommended that the wiki is checked out."
		""
		"[url]https://nucleartech.wiki/wiki/DFC[/url]"
	]
	quest.168E6FF329367EC5.title: "DFC"
	quest.16941710503334ED.quest_desc: [
		"The §3Blast Furnace§r is a solid fuel-powered furnace used to create different alloys out of two inputs. The main starter alloys are: §6Minecraft Grade Copper§r and §6Steel§r. Inserting §bHot Air Blast§r, made by putting §bCompressed Air§r in a §3Boiler§r, grants all recipes a §e3x§r boost."
		"§bFlue Gas§r produced from operating the machine can be burnt for energy or vented into the atmosphere."
		""
		"Steel tools come equiped with vein mining, making them an excellent early-game tool."
		""
		"§2For more advanced tools later on, pressing the ALT key will bring up a menu from which one can select multiple abilities at once.§r"
	]
	quest.16941710503334ED.title: "Blast Furnace"
	quest.1698ED691DFF3D06.quest_desc: ["Arrows are nice, if you shoot them. If one hits you, well, bad things happen."]
	quest.1698ED691DFF3D06.title: "Time to Kill (Skeleton)"
	quest.16A7C7334C1C273B.quest_desc: ["The §3Big-Ass Tank§r is the largest fluid storage container, capable of storing 2048000mB of fluids, aswell as being able to hold strongly corrosive fluids. It has to be placed on the solid surface, otherwise it is going to break."]
	quest.16A7C7334C1C273B.title: "Big-Ass Tank"
	quest.16B1D76101EEA824.quest_desc: ["The §6Network Tool§r, when right-clicking on any network device will bring up the tool's interface showing all devices connected to the network as well as network details. As any wrench, shift clicking on a cable will remove it."]
	quest.16B1D76101EEA824.title: "Network Tool"
	quest.16B468DF79E16422.quest_desc: [
		"The §6Analog Circuit§r is the first true circuit board used in crafting certain essential machines and tools such as the §6Oil Deposit Detector§r, the §3Chemical Plant§r, and the §3Electric Arc Furnace§r."
		""
		"§2A cheaper recipe for Capacitors will be available if a Shredder is owned."
	]
	quest.16B468DF79E16422.title: "Analog Circuit Board"
	quest.16B86DEAD3426B04.quest_desc: [
		"The §3Electrolysis Machine§r enables the separating of elements from fluids and the advanced processing of ores, making it an important machine in ore processing. Operating the machine consumes §e200kHE/s§r."
		""
		"The electrolysis machine has 2 functions: one for the separation of fluids and one for ore processing."
		""
		"In the first mode, the machine will take in a compatible fluid and separate it into 2 other fluids."
		""
		"In the second mode, it will require §bNitric Acid§r and will process any kind of ore-derived crystal, allowing the maximum yield of the ore. There are 2 outputs, for the molten main product the outlet marked green and the secondary the one marked red, plus a byproduct kept in its item form. The outlets follow the same mechanics as the §3Crucible§r."
		""
		"§2Consider installing a Power Saving upgrade above level 2 on the electrolysis machine as it will significantly reduce the power consumption with only a minimal speed penalty."
	]
	quest.16B86DEAD3426B04.title: "Electrolysis Machine"
	quest.16B970416CA7F147.quest_desc: [
		"The §3Fusion Reactor Coupler§r turns outgoing plasma energy from a torus into usable §eKyE§r which can then be used to power another torus. Some fuel combinations require this, as the minimum §eKyE§r energy needed to ignite the plasma exceeds what four §3Klystrons§r could deliver."
		""
		"The §3Fusion Reactor Breeding Chamber§r uses neutron flux from a torus to in order to process materials. It can perform any recipe from an §3RBMK irradiation channel§r, with some additional recipes aswell. The neutron flux is not affected by port sharing rules, and the output level is the same on any side."
		""
		"The §3Fusion Reactor Collection Chamber§r increases the byproduct production rate by §e50%§r."
	]
	quest.16B970416CA7F147.title: "Additional Fusion Attachments"
	quest.16E3D3780D40532A.quest_desc: [
		"§6Fluix Crystals§r are another crystal type which is used in crafting recipes throughout the mod. The crystal comes in two forms, the regular fluix crystal and the §6Pure Fluix Crystal§r."
		""
		"To create a fluix crystal, 1§6 Charged Certus Quartz§r, 1 §6Nether Quartz§r, and 1 §6Redstone Dust§r must be dropped into a pool of §bWater§r. They will be consumed and output 2 fluix crystals."
		""
		"§2Fluix crystals can later be made in a Chemical Plant using charged certus quartz and redstone."
	]
	quest.16E3D3780D40532A.title: "Fluix Crystal"
	quest.16F6340A52084470.quest_desc: ["High-speed steel§r is an advanced and specialized form of standard steel. It used in many recipes, such as the §3Oil Derrick§r and the §3Industrial Mixer§r."]
	quest.16F6340A52084470.title: "High-Speed Steel"
	quest.170A833EE27B065A.quest_desc: ["The §3ME Terminal§r is used to access all available items in the ME Network, including craftable ones."]
	quest.170A833EE27B065A.title: "ME Terminal"
	quest.170E200FCBA8570F.quest_desc: ["§6ME Patterns§r are used to encode recipes to be used in §3Interfaces§r. They can be encoded in a §3Pattern Terminal§r."]
	quest.170E200FCBA8570F.title: "ME Pattern"
	quest.17164D2564C8E1F8.quest_desc: ["The §6Chisel§r is a building tool which can be used to change the textures of blocks, and even unlock new and unique designs."]
	quest.17164D2564C8E1F8.title: "Chisel"
	quest.1716A6188D9843B7.quest_desc: ["The §3Rotary Furnace§r is a large furnace which is powered by both §bSteam§r and §6§rsolid fuel. §rIt outputs molten material which can be cast similarly to the outputs of the §3Crucible§r and §3Arc Furnace§r. The Rotary Furnace is the only machine that can produce §6Saturnite§r and §6Weapon Steel§r."]
	quest.1716A6188D9843B7.title: "Rotary Furnace"
	quest.171C12C9C2AC110F.quest_desc: ["When a century-old joke gets out of hand... At least you can make a juicy quesadilla."]
	quest.171C12C9C2AC110F.title: "The Mun is Cheese..."
	quest.171F39D8C263D418.quest_desc: [
		"Structures generate throughout the world and are among the best sources of early-game resources. Raiding them before investing heavily in production can save significant time and materials."
		""
		"§2Exploration pays off early - check your surroundings before grinding for resources you might find for free.§r"
	]
	quest.171F39D8C263D418.title: "Abandoned Structures"
	quest.172074CFD507D17D.quest_desc: [
		"The §3Xenium Resonator Satellite§r provides unlimited on-demand teleportation with no cooldown. Before launch, its frequency must be linked to a §6Satellite Designator§r using the §3Satellite ID Manager§r."
		""
		"A standard §6Satellite Designator§r requires coordinates to be entered manually. A §6Satellite (Laser) Designator§r is simpler - aim the crosshair at a block and right-click."
		""
		"§2Interdimensional teleportation is not supported."
	]
	quest.172074CFD507D17D.title: "Xenium Resonator Satellite"
	quest.1724385F3F535594.quest_desc: ["§6Solid Fuel§r is a compact solidified petroleum product with superior burn time and heat output compared to coal. Essential for advanced furnace operations and rocket propulsion systems."]
	quest.1724385F3F535594.title: "Solid Fuel"
	quest.1735B4B92204A325.quest_desc: [
		"The §c§r§4§r§6Digamma Particle§r is created by colliding a §6Sparkticle Capsule§r with a §6Higgs Boson Capsule§r in a §3Particle Accelerator§r. Making it in the particle accelerator will require §6Chlorophyte Coils§r and momentum of 70,000."
		""
		"The digamma particle emits a different kind of radiation, §4DRX§r, which currently can only be countered by the use of digamma medication, most notably §6Enteramine Pills§r, which provide full immunity against DRX for 10 minutes. After the §3DFC§r, Fau armor can be crafted which provides full resistance against DRX."
	]
	quest.1735B4B92204A325.title: "The Digamma Particle"
	quest.1741E691CE17FECC.quest_desc: [
		"In order to obtain a hidden catalog, you have to do a few things:"
		""
		"Get a regular sign"
		"Answer the four questions and put the answers on said sign in the same order (all lowercase)"
		"Right click the written sign"
		"There will be answers with more characters than signs allow, just type out as many as possible."
		""
		"There will be no hints, so don't even try it."
		"You'll need the bobmazon level 6 achievement to order anything."
		""
		""
		""
		"1"
		"When we scream into the distance, who will answer?"
		""
		"2"
		"The invisible force, sometimes subtle and sometimes not, covers our eyes directed at the skies."
		""
		"3"
		"The fluorescent oscilloscope gives us the passcode of random numbers. Who holds the answers?"
		""
		"4"
		"Ever revolving, never still, a sight for the patient that reeks of tobacco, dancing perpetually."
	]
	quest.1741E691CE17FECC.title: "Secret Catalogue"
	quest.174F34F5A3BED4F7.quest_desc: ["The §3Drainage Pipe§r allows the dumping of fluids and gasses into the environment at the cost of pollution."]
	quest.174F34F5A3BED4F7.title: "Drainage Pipe"
	quest.175585CF19B66BA8.quest_desc: [
		"The §3Presses§r are machines that can be used to make §6Plates§r, §6Wires§r, §6Circuits§r, §6Bullet Casings§r as well as §6Compressing§r non-smeltable powders back into their normal form. They require §6Stamps§r to work, which can be made from the basic §6Flat Stamp§r on the §6Iron Anvil§r."
		""
		"§2A preheater can be placed next to the Burner Press to increase its speed."
	]
	quest.175585CF19B66BA8.title: "Burner Press"
	quest.175C2965392E3CD0.quest_desc: [
		"Fluids are measured in §emB§r (§emilli-Buckets§r) and §eB§r (§eBuckets§r)."
		""
		"1 bucket = 1000mB."
		""
		"The §6Multi Fluid Identifier§r is used to select the type of NTM fluid one needs. Shift-Click while holding it to select a fluid."
	]
	quest.175C2965392E3CD0.title: "Fluids"
	quest.1769B28F2A74FAFB.quest_desc: ["The §3Cooling Tower§r is a larger version of the §3Auxiliary Cooling Tower§r§r, able to process up to 500 mB/t of §bLow-Pressure Steam§r."]
	quest.1769B28F2A74FAFB.title: "Cooling Tower"
	quest.176D95A59D132B03.quest_desc: ["The §3Exposure Chamber§r is a machine in which many materials can be created by exposing ingots to certain particles, most important of which being §6Dineutronium§r."]
	quest.176D95A59D132B03.title: "Exposure Chamber"
	quest.177148EEE61F79E9.quest_desc: ["§eIke§r, the sole moon of §eDuna§r, has hints of a past as a significant hazardous waste dump, with large spires and pyramids reminiscent of potential designs on Earth for warning future civilizations of great danger in relation to nuclear waste. §eMeteor dungeons§r spawn more frequently here, and pools of §bAlkyl Bromide§r can be found on the surface."]
	quest.177148EEE61F79E9.title: "Ike"
	quest.178B57FD53744504.quest_desc: [
		"Parallelisation of processes can significantly cut down on waiting time and as such it is highly recommended that P2P Interfaces are used."
		""
		"§2This quest serves as a guide on how to use P2P Interfaces.§r"
		""
		"As any P2P Connection goes, there needs to be one input, which in this case, holds the §6ME Patterns§r."
		""
		"[img height=1000]betterquesting:textures/QB_P2P_Interface1.png[/img]"
		""
		"After patterns are inserted in the first P2P interface, place down the rest of the output interfaces you want and link them together using a §6Memory Card§r."
		""
		"In the image below, the P2P interface highlighted in green stores the patterns, while the ones in blue, are the output ones which will connect machines to the ME system."
		""
		"[img height=1000]betterquesting:textures/QB_P2P_Interface2.png[/img]"
		""
		"Make sure to have blocking mode enabled on all output P2P interfaces as to prevent clogging and having multiple recipes trying to be executed at once in the same machine."
		""
		"[img height=1000]betterquesting:textures/QB_P2P_Interface3.png[/img]"
		""
		"Finally, place your desired machines at the output P2P interfaces and add a way of retrieving the items once the operation is done, in this case import buses."
		""
		"[img height=1000]betterquesting:textures/QB_P2P_Interface4.png[/img]"
	]
	quest.178B57FD53744504.title: "P2P Interface Parallelisation"
	quest.17A1355238F4F9A3.quest_desc: [
		"The §6Powered Drill§r is a modular mining device which can make resourse gathering and excavation much faster than normal pickaxes."
		""
		"Various modifications can be attached in the §3Weapon Modification Table§r, such as new drillbits for a larger mining radious or even new engines, which let it run on electricity."
	]
	quest.17A1355238F4F9A3.title: "Powered Drill"
	quest.17B1E84ACD3B8A87.quest_desc: [
		"The §6Control Unit§r is used to create §6CPUs§r and §6Component Buses§r."
		""
		"The §6Arithmetic Logic Unit§r is used for crafting components that perform calculations, such as CPUs and §6Graphics Cards§r."
	]
	quest.17B1E84ACD3B8A87.title: "Control and Arithmetics Units"
	quest.17BAFEDC06849715.quest_desc: [
		"The §6Dosimeter§r is an tool for detecting radiation and assessing radioactive contamination."
		""
		"It is functionally similar to a §6Geiger Counter§r, but it collects much less data - only the general radiation contamination of the environment. Only a handheld version of the dosimeter is available. To obtain radiation information, right-click while holding the dosimeter."
		""
		"Like a counter, it makes a characteristic crackling sound when radiation is detected."
		""
		"§2The maximum radiation displayed is 3.6 RAD/S."
		""
		"Not great, not terrible."
	]
	quest.17BAFEDC06849715.title: "Dosimeter"
	quest.17C364EEF8A60581.quest_desc: ["§6Graphite§r is a crystalline carbon allotrope, consisting of stacked layers of graphene. Graphite is the most stable form of carbon, and is useful in many environments. It's ability to moderate neutrons makes it indispensable for §3nuclear reactors§r that rely on thermal neutrons to maintain criticality. It's ability to withstand high temperatures and electrical conductivity make it useful as electrodes in the §3Arc Furnace§r and §3Arc Welder§r."]
	quest.17C364EEF8A60581.title: "Graphite"
	quest.17CDAEEF5897C51B.quest_desc: [
		"The §6Trench Mask§r is a basic mask that will protect the user from some dangerous airborne particles while mining. To craft one you must first obtain §6Cloth§r and then piss on it by right clicking while holding it."
		""
		"§2String can be easily obtained by harvesting Hemp, found in the wild."
		""
		"§rI hate to say it, but you are basically sniffing your own piss..."
	]
	quest.17CDAEEF5897C51B.title: "Trench Mask"
	quest.17CE311B0BE5023F.quest_desc: ["§bBTX§r is a high-grade powerful fuel which generates a lot of power when burnt. An important use of BTX is in the creation of §6Crystalline Fullerite§r and §6Hard Plastic Bars§r. BTX can be obtained from a §3Hydrotreater§r, but it is more efficient to use §bReformate§r from a §3Vacuum Refinery§r."]
	quest.17CE311B0BE5023F.title: "BTX"
	quest.17DC9AC6796563BD.quest_desc: ["The §3Stirling Sawmill§r uses heat to cut wooden related items, producing §6Sawdust§r in the process. Sawdust can be used to obtain §6Paper§r, and if further processed, can be turned into §6Charcoal§r in a §3Combination Oven§r."]
	quest.17DC9AC6796563BD.title: "Stirling Sawmill"
	quest.17DD2EF00E103829.quest_desc: ["The §3ME Storage Bus§r, when attached to an block/tile entity with an inventory (generally a storage unit, such as chests or a §3Drawer Controller§r), will include that inventory's contents in the ME System."]
	quest.17DD2EF00E103829.title: "ME Storage Bus"
	quest.17F449696F1EAAD7.quest_desc: ["The §dSignPicture§r mod allows one to put any image on a sign, opening the door to many unique building designs. Press \\ to get started."]
	quest.17F449696F1EAAD7.title: "Sign Pictures"
	quest.17F8BC902CCF6BD9.quest_desc: ["Now a Hell version of your slime!"]
	quest.17F8BC902CCF6BD9.title: "Time to Kill (Magma Cube)"
	quest.1803FA5BC8A8FBA2.quest_desc: ["§3Pipe Anchors§r are non solid fluid ducts which can be used instead of normal ducts."]
	quest.1803FA5BC8A8FBA2.title: "Pipe Anchors"
	quest.180E85F0A746EF54.quest_desc: ["The §3Steam Radiator§r is a steam condenser that works in the vacuum of space."]
	quest.180E85F0A746EF54.title: "Steam Radiator"
	quest.1822DEB2EC5F844F.quest_desc: [
		"In §6NTNH§r, ore generation has been §ocompletely§r overhauled and is still receiving updates and fixes. If you don’t like it and/or find it too complicated, you have two options:"
		"1) Report it to us, the developers"
		"2) Disable the Custom Ore Generation mod and configure ore generation in hbm.cfg to your liking (ask for help with this on the Discord server)"
		""
		"[warn]Important![/warn]"
		"The old online Google Docs spreadsheet was DEPRECATED, use the one in the Guide Book."
	]
	quest.1822DEB2EC5F844F.title: "Ore Generation System"
	quest.183040AA625795AC.quest_desc: ["The §3Industrial Mixer§r is a machine that is used to mix a fluid with an item and/or another fluid. It can be used instead of a §3Chemical Plant§r for some recipes."]
	quest.183040AA625795AC.title: "Industrial Mixer"
	quest.18311E8339EACF48.quest_desc: ["The §6Network Visualisation Tool§r is used to visuallize an ME Network by right-clicking on any of its blocks, making it very useful when making a large network, especially one that uses §3P2P§r."]
	quest.18311E8339EACF48.title: "Network Visualisation Tool"
	quest.1843EA856B6FD6E9.quest_desc: ["The §6Integrated Circuit Board§r is the first circuit board to use §6Silicon§r, being used extensively in mid game machines, automation devices, missiles, and various small tools such as the §6Geiger Counter§r."]
	quest.1843EA856B6FD6E9.title: "Integrated Circuit Board"
	quest.18516A040BF2321C.quest_desc: [
		"The §3PUREX§r is a machine that can reprocess depleted nuclear fuel into various materials. Most recipes require both §bNitric Acid§r and §bKerosene§r to function."
		""
		"§6Schrabidium§r can also be extracted from certain recipes, which require §bSchrabidic Acid§r. The schrabidium extracted yields double the schrabidium used to make the acid."
	]
	quest.18516A040BF2321C.title: "PUREX"
	quest.18636A54C44323B1.quest_desc: ["Sand in an §3Ore Acidizer§r can be turned into §6Fiberglass§r, which provides more than §e4x§r the amount of §6Silicon§r in an §3Arc Furnace§r. Additionally, it provides a great recipe for insulators."]
	quest.18636A54C44323B1.title: "Fiberglass"
	quest.18642A11F04906D4.quest_desc: ["Incase of an §3RBMK§r meltdown, §6Fuel Chunks§r will be thrown near the reactor. The §6Liquidator Medal§r is an armor modification which passively reduces radiation, making it very useful when handling radioactive items or venturing into irradiated areas."]
	quest.18642A11F04906D4.title: "Liquidator Medal"
	quest.186A15287FB0A374.quest_desc: [
		"The §6Chlorine Pinwheel§r is a yellow propeller capable of producing chlorine indefinitely."
		"Acquisition"
		""
		"It cannot be crafted, but can be found in structures (e.g., in a starship)."
		""
		"The chlorine spinner is an endless source of §bChlorine§r; to use it, simply place it in a container slot (e.g., in a barrel). The item will produce chlorine indefinitely, although the production rate is low (1 mb/t or 20 mb/s)."
		""
		"The §6Oxygen Pinwheel§r is analogous to the Chlorine Pinwheel, producing §bOxygen§r instead of §bChlorine§r."
	]
	quest.186A15287FB0A374.title: "Pinwheels"
	quest.1895DB4E3FE24A43.quest_desc: ["The §3P2P Interface§r is a P2P device which can be used to easily paralellize recipes across many machines."]
	quest.1895DB4E3FE24A43.title: "Interface P2P"
	quest.18B7F21145527B22.quest_desc: ["§6Cladding§r is one of the most important armor modifications which reduce radiation intake. It can be inserted to all armor pieces."]
	quest.18B7F21145527B22.title: "Cladding"
	quest.18C323EFA7E48AEF.quest_desc: ["An upgraded version of the §6Wireless Terminal§r, capable of crafting items on the go."]
	quest.18C323EFA7E48AEF.title: "Wireless Crafting Terminal"
	quest.18CDACB190D27DA7.quest_desc: [
		"The §2§3PWR§r is a modular fission reactor. It is more limited than the §3RBMK§r in terms of capability and fuel types but it is much safer and easier to use due to it melting down more gently and being far more stable in its operation."
		""
		"Due to the complex and expansive nature of the PWR, it is highly recommend that the wiki is checked out as it provides more information."
		""
		"[url]https://nucleartech.wiki/wiki/PWR[/url]"
		""
		"§2This quest demands the most essential parts of a PWR, and does not represent the amount needed for a functioning reactor. There are also many other types of PWR Components that can be used."
	]
	quest.18CDACB190D27DA7.title: "PWR"
	quest.18DF9F2C8B3CFAF6.quest_desc: [
		"The §3Chicago Pile§r is a modular breeding reactor with no GUI, built to transmute §6Natural Uranium§r into plutonium isotopes through neutron bombardment. It must be operated manually or via §dRedstone-over-Radio§r."
		""
		"Build a rectangular prism of §6Chicago Pile Graphite Bricks§r, at minimum 5*5*5 and at most 15*15*15. Once assembled, drill a non-edge block on one of its lateral faces with the §6Hand Drill§r to establish the core and fix the reactor's channel orientation. Channels are straight lines drilled through the pile and may not intersect. Fuel channels share the core's face orientation and accept rods via a §3Chicago Pile Fuel Loader§r on the input port; spent rods are ejected from the opposite side. Ventilation channels run perpendicular to the core and require a §3Chicago Pile Vent§r supplied with §bcompressed air§r at §e1 PU§r - each vent cools only the fuel channels within one block above or below it. Vertical control rod channels are optional and reduce reactivity between channels."
		""
		"Every reaction requires a neutron source. The §6Ra226Be Neutron Source§r is the starter option; the more powerful §6Po210Be Neutron Source§r can replace it later. §6Natural Uranium Rods§r breed into §6Plutonium-239 Rods§r, which can be bred further into §6Reactor-Grade Plutonium Rods§r. Leaving fuel beyond that point produces §6Nuclear Waste Rods§r, which generate extreme heat and risk meltdown. To safely push out spent rods without fresh fuel, use §6Zirconium Rods§r - they are inert and transparent to neutrons."
		""
		"§2Verify cooling is working before loading any fuel. The pile melts down at 800°C, causing an explosion and widespread fire."
		""
		"The quest asks for a §3Chicago Pile§r of at least 5*5*5 with a core established, a §3Chicago Pile Fuel Loader§r and §3Chicago Pile Vent§r attached, and a §6Ra226Be Neutron Source§r loaded alongside at least one §6Natural Uranium Rod§r."
	]
	quest.18DF9F2C8B3CFAF6.title: "Chicago Pile"
	quest.18E842E523922CCA.quest_desc: ["Enables remote access to StarDar."]
	quest.18E842E523922CCA.title: "StarDar Remote Access Console"
	quest.18EE7DE020F84DBC.quest_desc: ["Delicious squid. We're making Tom Yum seafood."]
	quest.18EE7DE020F84DBC.title: "Time to Kill (Squid)"
	quest.18F6B5A8DB138564.quest_desc: ["The §3Leviathan Steam Turbine§r is a massive turbine capable of processing gargantuan amounts of §bSteam§r at once, only hindered by the fluid system's transfer rate. It is significantly more powerful than even the §3Industrial Steam Turbine§r in terms of raw steam processing power. This turbine runs on §e85%§r Efficiency, so it is recommended that only 1-2 are used for very large reactors."]
	quest.18F6B5A8DB138564.title: "Leviathan Steam Turbine"
	quest.18F717BF32C7348D.quest_desc: ["The §3Combination Oven§r is a unique type of furnace that transforms items into their respective product and produce liquid byproducts. It can be used to produce §6Coke§r, §bWood Oil§r and §6Aluminium§r more efficiently."]
	quest.18F717BF32C7348D.title: "Combination Oven"
	quest.19208529C0044179.quest_desc: [
		"With a §3Drop pod§r, one can access their space station without needing to build new rockets. They can also be used to land on other planets once the station has reached them."
		""
		"§2Make sure to keep spare drives.§r"
	]
	quest.19208529C0044179.title: "Drop Pod"
	quest.19414C22C5C57962.quest_desc: ["The §3ME Drive§r serves as the storage of the ME system, in which §6Storage Cells§r can be put and store items."]
	quest.19414C22C5C57962.title: "ME Drive"
	quest.1942EDE06DBC674C.quest_desc: ["The &6Sensor Relay Satellite&r is used to produce &eOrbital Data&r. A single relay takes &e100 hours&r to produce one drive worth of orbital data. It can be sped up by installing more relays. Each additional Relay reduces the time linearly, meaning that a satellite with 100 relays will produce orbital data in just &eone hour&r."]
	quest.1942EDE06DBC674C.title: "Sensor Relay"
	quest.1943026FAA3EF1EF.quest_desc: [
		"§eBedrock Ore Deposits§r are an infinite source of resourses which can be obtained by using a §3Large Mining Drill§r and a §3Bedrock Ore Processor§r."
		""
		"Operating the drill will consume§e 200kHE/s§r."
		""
		"Before excavation can happen, the §eDepth Rock§r covering the bedrock ore deposit needs to be removed. An easy way of doing that is blowing up the rock with §6Mining Charges§r."
		""
		"The large mining drill is used to excavate §6Raw Bedrock Ores§r from their deposits. The drill requires a §6Drillbit§r to work§r, which can be upgraded to increase the speed at which it operates at. §eFortune§r on a drillbit affects the quality of mined bedrock ore, each level of fortune adds §e10%§r of the value to the item."
		""
		"The bedrock ore processor takes §6§rraw bedrock ore obtained from the drill and breaks it down into smaller pieces, each with different products that can be obtained from them."
		"§a§bOre Slop§r, which is created when the machine is operating, can be processed into many useful products, especially when it is sent through an §3Electrolysis Machine§r."
		""
		"The §6Bedrock Ore Desity Scanner§r shows information on the composition of Bedrock Ore deposits."
		""
		"Bedrock ore processing can be both an energy and resourse expensive operation so it is recommended that it is explored after having good infrastructure."
		""
		"§2Consider adding a Power Saving Upgrade to the drill as it only reduces power without affecting the mining speed. Additionally, installing an Effectiveness Upgrade on the ore slopper will make it give out more resourses.§r§r"
	]
	quest.1943026FAA3EF1EF.title: "Bedrock Ore Processing"
	quest.1945721F26087490.quest_desc: [
		"The §3Soyuz-FG Rocket§r is an immensely powerful Soviet rocket that is the primary launch vehicle for all satellites. The rocket must be launched from a suitably large mount - in this case, the §3Soyuz Launch Platform§r."
		""
		"It requires 128,000mB of §bKerosene§r and §bLiquid Oxygen§r to be launched as well as §e750kHE§r of power. Pressing the launch button starts a 30 second countdown. After the countdown has completed, the Soyuz will launch."
		""
		"The Soyuz can, alongside its primary ability to deliver any satellite to orbit, also be set to a cargo mode, in which it can deliver any provided cargo to a distant spot across the world. Obviously, this is an incredibly expensive way to transport goods, and currently doesn't provide much utility."
		""
		"§2Blueprints for the Soyuz can be found in structures or purchased through Bobmazon."
	]
	quest.1945721F26087490.title: "Soyuz-FG"
	quest.195A1B38A29613AF.quest_desc: ["The §3Drive Processor Tier 2§r allows for travel to §eDres§r and §eEve§r."]
	quest.195A1B38A29613AF.title: "Drive Processor Tier 2"
	quest.195DCE0E926A5675.quest_desc: ["I think I need a new backpack. Let's slaughter a few cows."]
	quest.195DCE0E926A5675.title: "Time to Kill (Cow)"
	quest.1961609CFDBBB5DE.quest_desc: ["The §6Versatile Circuit Board§r is the final tier of circuit board, requiring §6Bismuth/Arsenic§r and §6Hard Plastic/PVC Bars§r.  As well as this, it is by far the most expensive circuit board, requiring nearly 55 insulators to craft a single one. Used rarely but in small amounts in advanced machines like the §3Fusion Reactor§r and in large amounts in components for the §3ICF Reactor§r."]
	quest.1961609CFDBBB5DE.title: "Versatile Circuit Board"
	quest.196B5884027D9FDB.quest_desc: [
		"The §3Hydraulic Fracking Tower§r is used to extract infinite oil from a §eBedrock Oil Deposit§r. To operate, the machine needs §bFracking Solution§r. During its operation, the surrounding environment will sustain considerable damage. §6Oily Dirt§r and §6Oily Sand§r can be used to create §6Arsenic§r, a substitute of §6Bismuth§r."
		""
		"Operating the hydraulic fracking tower will consume §e100kHE/s§r."
	]
	quest.196B5884027D9FDB.title: "Hydraulic Fracking Tower"
	quest.1996D29A454AE962.quest_desc: [
		"The formation of a volcano is driven by the §3volcanic core§r, a block that continuously erupts §blava§r, allowing the volcano to grow. The §blava§r cools quickly, turning into §6basalt§r or §6basaltic ore§r."
		""
		"The resulting volcano grows quite slowly, reaching about 60 blocks in height over 20-30 minutes."
		""
		"§bVolcanic lava§r differs from §bregular lava§r not only in appearance. It \"melts\" any non-explosion-resistant blocks, so the volcano can extend underground."
		""
		"§6Basaltic ores§r (§6asbestos§r, §6sulfur§r, §6fluorite§r, §6molysite§r) form when the §blava§r cools, each with a 0.5% chance."
		""
		"§6Volcanic gem ore§r spawns with a 5% chance if the following conditions are met:"
		"- All 6 blocks around the cooling §blava§r are §6basalt§r or §blava§r;"
		"- The block 10 blocks above the cooling §blava§r is §6basalt§r or §blava§r;"
		"- There are fewer than 3 §blava§r blocks around the cooling §blava§r."
		""
		"The §6ore§r also forms after §bvolcanic lava§r contacts §6diamond ore§r."
		"This means §6volcanic gems§r most often appear near the §3core§r or §3crater§r of the volcano."
		""
		"§3Forming a Radioactive Volcano§r"
		"If the §3volcanic core§r is exposed to radioactive fallout (e.g., after a nearby nuclear explosion) for some time, the §3core§r will begin generating new §bvolcanic radioactive lava§r (yellow in color), ultimately leading to the formation of a so-called §3radioactive volcano§r. Such a volcano will consist not of §6basalt§r but of various types of §6quenched sellaphite blocks§r and §6sellaphite ores§r. The §blava§r will convert §6diamond ores§r into §6radioactive gem ore§r."
	]
	quest.1996D29A454AE962.title: "My First Volcano!"
	quest.199E7BCE91BE5393.quest_desc: [
		"§6Desh§r is an alloy made up of 9 rare earth metals to make its blend form, which is solidified and refined using §bMercury§r and §bLight oil§r in the §3Chemical Plant§r. Desh is an almost unbreakable material and as such its tools have infinite durability."
		""
		"§a§2Desh can also be made using DeshReady™ in a Rotary Furnace, or later on, in an Ore Acidizer.§r"
		""
		"Mercury at this stage of the game can be obtained from centrifuging §eRedstone Ore§r or putting §eCinnabar§r in a §3Combination Oven§r. Large cinnabar veins can be found as depth ore."
		""
		"Later on, mercury can be obtained from processing §bOre Slop§r or §bVitriol§r in an §3Electrolyzer§r."
	]
	quest.199E7BCE91BE5393.title: "Desh"
	quest.19A4292F1E6DC1FA.quest_desc: ["The &6Crystal Circuit Board&r is an end game circuit used for making &6Gerald&r and the &3DFC&r. The finished item will be received via the &3Cargo Landing Pad&r."]
	quest.19A9F550A80975CB.quest_desc: ["An upgraded version of the §3Anvil§r, [T2], which unlocks additional recipes."]
	quest.19A9F550A80975CB.title: "Steel Anvil"
	quest.19ACEE82F8C5543C.quest_desc: [
		"§6P2P§r Tunnel or \"Point to Point Tunnels\" are a versatile configurable system to move items / redstone / power / and fluids from one location to another though an existing ME Network without storage."
		""
		"Tunnels are §e1 input to N outputs§r. This means you can output to as many points as you want, but only input at a single point per tunnel."
		""
		"Networks can support any number of tunnels, of any different types, and they all function independently."
		""
		"ME tunnels can be used to carry channels from one location to another, and can carry up to §e32 channels§r, same as a §6ME Dense Cable§r, while only requiring a single channel per point, making tunnels a very powerful tool to expand me networks, especially over a distance. However with the great flex-ability they give you comes a limitation, the channel of a p2p tunnel cannot be carried by another p2p tunnel, meaning that you cannot nest them recursively."
		""
		"To configure a P2P tunnel you must first attune the tunnel to carry what you want it to, then you need to configure the outputs to their input. You configure the connections by using the §6Memory Card§r. First Shift+Right Click the input to save it on your memory card, then simply right click the different outputs to store the input onto the outputs. this also sets the type of the output to match the type of the input."
		""
		"§2An advanced version of the Memory Card can also be made, which interacts with the entire network."
	]
	quest.19ACEE82F8C5543C.title: "P2P"
	quest.19B29AB1A32ED9F9.quest_desc: [
		"§3Magnetohydrodynamic Turbines§r are advanced components of the fusion reactor that make electricity out of the plasma energy directly without needing additional turbines. While more expensive and requiring §bPerfluoromethyl§r cooling, they have a §e+35%§r convertion bonus from §eTU§r to §eHE§r. In addition, the MDH turbine requires a minimum input of"
		"§e5MTU/t§r of plasma energy to operate normally, otherwise efficiency will be halved."
	]
	quest.19B29AB1A32ED9F9.title: "Magnetohydrodynamic Turbines"
	quest.19B673B6BF82EBE8.quest_desc: [
		"Here is my own (Bufka2011) map of our Kerbol system!"
		"[img height=300]resources:SpaceMap_by_Bufka2011.png[/img]"
	]
	quest.19B673B6BF82EBE8.title: "Space Map"
	quest.19B9E1C2879CB99E.quest_desc: ["You killed them all! §cYou're monster!"]
	quest.19B9E1C2879CB99E.title: "§4§lMEGAKILL!"
	quest.19C197BC7D843226.quest_desc: ["The §3ME IO Port§r can transfer the contents of storage cells into an ME Network and back."]
	quest.19C197BC7D843226.title: "ME IO Port"
	quest.19C388D83D206780.quest_desc: [
		"§bHigh-Performance Solvent§r is the best tier of solvent which can be used in bedrock ore processing, yielding many rare materials such as§6 Bismuth§r and §6Technetium-99§r."
		""
		"§2These materials are not available from earth bedrock ores."
	]
	quest.19C388D83D206780.title: "High-Performance Solvent Bedrock Ore Processing"
	quest.19D6D944CF0F707A.quest_desc: ["The red planet, home to vast quantities of §6Iron§r. §6Molysite§r and §6Volcano Gems§r can be found here in basaltic caves, found within basins where vast oceans were theorized to once exist."]
	quest.19D6D944CF0F707A.title: "Duna"
	quest.19DAD995AD453134.quest_desc: [
		"The §3RBMK§r is a modular boiling-water type nuclear fission reactor which consists entirely of concrete columns. Each of these columns is either blank or has a specific function that it performs such as holding fuel rods, moderating neutrons, or storing §bWater§r to be boiled into §bSteam§r. Each column will also exchange heat with the column next to it such that temperature differences between columns will gradually equalize within the reactor. If any column reaches §e1500°C§r, the reactor will explode incredibly violently, spraying scrap and immensely radioactive material in every direction."
		""
		"Due to the complex and expansive nature of the RBMK, it is highly recommend that the wiki is checked out as it provides more information."
		""
		"[url]https://nucleartech.wiki/wiki/RBMK[/url]"
		""
		"§2This quest provides an optional retrieval task for a cheap and safe RBMK design which can produce High-Performance Solvent§r §2without cooling. Simply Place the RBMK Irradiation Channel next to the RBMK Fuel Rod, apply the covers on the collumns and surround them with a solid block."
	]
	quest.19DAD995AD453134.title: "RBMK"
	quest.19E71D2877456D96.quest_desc: ["The §3Industrial Liquification Machine§r is a general use machine for the liquifying various items. It becomes very useful for cobblestone generation, and thus §6Silicon§r automation."]
	quest.19E71D2877456D96.title: "Industrial Liquification Machine"
	quest.19EB29D5C9EC62D8.quest_desc: [
		"Your first destination! Absolutely chock full of §6Lithium§r, §6Quartz§r and most importantly your first source of §6Nickel§r to start producing §6Stainless Steel§r for space-grade machinery. The §eMun§r is the first atmosphere-less body available in a regular playthrough, necessary for making the first tier of §6Drive Processors§r in the §3Vacuum Solderer§r."
		""
		"The B-Side destination alternative to the Mun, §eMinmus§r is characterized by a distinctive mint-choc-chip ice-cream aesthetic. §3Pumps§r function here, but instead of producing §bWater§r, this moon bizarrely produces §bMilk§r, allowing for full automation of §6Butter§r, §6Milkshakes§r and §6Ice-Cream§r."
	]
	quest.19EB29D5C9EC62D8.title: "Mun/Minmus"
	quest.19EBC43CA3F7E2DC.quest_desc: [
		"§6CMB Iserts§r are an armor modification which will protect its user from the corrosive atmosphere of §eEve§r."
		""
		"The §3Gas Giant Harvester§r will return back with §bJool Air§r, to be processed by the §3Cryogenic Distillation Machine§r."
	]
	quest.19EBC43CA3F7E2DC.title: "CMB Insert"
	quest.19FFAAEA46C93543.quest_desc: ["A very valuable gemstone that is used to create a §6Cast Pickaxe§r, §6Meteorite Talisman§r, §6Black Diamond§r, §6Composite Euphemium Plates§r and §6Special 227mm Shells§r."]
	quest.19FFAAEA46C93543.title: "Volcanic Gem"
	quest.1A002F30E2312ED4.quest_desc: [
		"§bHigh-Performance Solvent§r is a solvent which is used in an §3Ore Acidizer§r to further increase the products of bedrock ores, as well as other recipes. It can be created from §bReformate Gas§r, from a §3Vacuum Refinery§r, and §bChlorine§r in an §3Industrial Mixer§r or be obtained from an §3RBMK§r Irradiation Channel."
		""
		"To transport High-Performance Solvent by hand, a §6Hazardous Material Tank§r is needed."
		""
		"§2High-Performance Solvent made from an RBMK irradiation channel requires an ore acidizer."
	]
	quest.1A002F30E2312ED4.title: "High-Performance Solvent"
	quest.1A05F28E78682BED.quest_desc: ["Instead of using the §bHot Coolant§r for power, one can use it to make the §3Steel Furnace§r go at ludicrous speeds."]
	quest.1A05F28E78682BED.title: "PWR powered Steel Furnace"
	quest.1A1C0CEBD9224C0D.quest_desc: ["\"Zombie Pigman\"? What the hell is going on with you zombies?! Maybe you should encase your animals better at night..."]
	quest.1A1C0CEBD9224C0D.title: "Time to Kill (Pigman)"
	quest.1A2030E39FD87D2A.quest_desc: ["Sticky and bouncy! Now in many variations. Say hello to my little friend, Lemon Slice!"]
	quest.1A2030E39FD87D2A.title: "Time to Kill (Slime)"
	quest.1A293F003F37A87F.quest_desc: [
		"§3Barrels§r are storage blocks that can hold both fluids and solid blocks. Wooden barrels will leak liquids over time and burn down if filled with lava, so use a stone barrel for those recipes."
		""
		"Barrels placed under open sky will collect rainwater during downfall."
		""
		"When filled with organic material, a barrel will begin composting once completely full. After roughly 100 seconds it produces a dirt block, ejected by right-clicking. Dirt left near mycelium will slowly convert into a mycelium block, no Silk Touch needed."
		""
		"A wooden barrel filled with §bWater§r placed next to cobblestone will slowly convert it into mossy cobblestone, costing §e100 mB§r per block. The surrounding blocks must be unaffected by rain. Placing a barrel on mycelium converts its water into §5Witch Water§r, though the barrel itself may disappear in the process. Water flowing above a barrel filled with lava transforms into obsidian."
		""
		"Stone barrels can spawn creatures when tapped with a doll: a barrel of lava with an Angry Doll summons a Blaze, and a barrel of §5Witch Water§r with a Creepy Doll summons an Enderman."
		""
		"Barrels can convert items using fluids: §5Witch Water§r turns sand into soul sand, lava turns redstone into netherrack or glowstone dust into end stone, and §bWater§r can turn dust into clay, milk into slime balls, or mushroom stew into §5Witch Water§r."
		""
		"§2Hoppers can be used to insert and eject items from barrels, making composting easy to automate.§r"
	]
	quest.1A293F003F37A87F.title: "Do a Barrel!"
	quest.1A2AC0CA7433073F.quest_desc: [
		"§6Hard Plastic/PVC Bars§r are very durable plastics needed for many late game recipes."
		""
		"§2Both can be used in the same recipes."
	]
	quest.1A2AC0CA7433073F.title: "Hard Plastic/PVC Bars"
	quest.1A4DBB5639EEC8C9.quest_desc: ["The §3Auto Chisel§r allows for automated chiseling of blocks. Simply insert any chisel in the machine and the block that will act as the template."]
	quest.1A4DBB5639EEC8C9.title: "Auto Chisel"
	quest.1A51CB3CE9CB565F.quest_desc: [
		"The §3Fusion Reactor Boiler§r is simplest method of extracting power from a fusion reactor, outputting §bSuper Dense Steam§r to be run through normal turbines."
		""
		"Due to using plasma energy, both the MHDT and the boiler are affected by port sharing rules, meaning that having multiple connected MHTDs, or boilers, decreases the amount of energy each turbine gets, but overall increases the total amount of extracted from the torus."
	]
	quest.1A51CB3CE9CB565F.title: "Fusion Power"
	quest.1A5AEEA7C90D0A06.quest_desc: ["The §6Versatile Integrated Circuit§r is the first circuit to use §6Bismuth/Arsenic§r. It is used in more advanced machines such as the §3Vacuum Refinery§r and is one of the main components of §6Versatile Circuit Boards§r."]
	quest.1A5AEEA7C90D0A06.title: "Versatile Integrated Circuit"
	quest.1A68E54D35F6001E.quest_desc: [
		"The §3Coker Unit§r is a machine that turns oil products into §6Petroleum Coke§r, which is the same to the other kinds of coke, aswell as additional fluids as byproducts. The coker unit will require an external heat source in order to function, similar to the §3Crucible§r."
		""
		"§2§r§2Alongside the §2§r§2§r§2Electric Arc Furnace, the coker unit is one of the most polluting machines of the mod. It spreads 20 soot per second, making it a dangerous machine to use next to a glyphid nest."
	]
	quest.1A68E54D35F6001E.title: "Coker Unit"
	quest.1A82FC0322F90D24.quest_desc: [
		"§6Glyphids§r are large insects that have many different types. They primarily spawn with naturally generated §6§rhives§r structures. All of the types are armored and they take less damage than against normal mobs. Glyphids are normally attracted to pollution created by the player, and usually have to be dealt with by the player."
		""
		"§6§r§6Hives§r can spawn naturally in all non-ocean biomes and can also be created by glyphid scouts. They contain several glyphid egg blocks and some low-tier loot inside, lying on top of eggs. glyphid egg blocks spawn glyphids and drop glyphid eggs upon destruction."
		""
		"Glyphids now periodically retarget the closest player every 5 seconds if their current target is farther. 1/3 of glyphids do not have this behavior to prevent infinite trapping."
		""
		"§2It is recommended that all hives are destroyed as soon as possible as to prevent their spread later on."
	]
	quest.1A82FC0322F90D24.title: "Glyphids"
	quest.1A8D145B0F87408D.quest_desc: ["§2This quest provides an optional retrieval task for a small laser capable of running Helium-4 - Hydrogen Fuel at 15MHE.§r"]
	quest.1A8D145B0F87408D.title: "ICF Laser"
	quest.1AA188AB920FF1BE.quest_desc: [
		"The §3Electric Arc Furnace§r is a large automated furnace multiblock machine that can fill the role of §3Crucible§r and automated smelter, and is required for progression as it is the only machine that can produce §6Silicon§r from various sources, such as §6Sand§r, §6Flint§r, §6fiberglass§r, and §6Asbestos§r."
		""
		"To operate this machine, it will require both electrical power and crafted §7§6Electrodes§r. In terms of electricity, the machine has a maximum storage capacity of §e2.5MHE§r, and consumes §e20kHE/s§r in operation, making it reasonably power hungry. In terms of the electrodes required for operation, there are four types available, and the machine must have three installed before it can operate."
		""
		"This machine can operate in two different modes: Solid mode, which is the easiest to setup and use, great for initial crafting, and Liquid mode, which produces castable molten ores much like the crucible, with a small bonus to output, increasing efficiency of extraction from various ores."
	]
	quest.1AA188AB920FF1BE.title: "Electric Arc Furnace"
	quest.1AA3AA74AE892B42.quest_desc: ["§3Computer Casings§r come in 3 different tiers, which limit the amount of components that ca be placed inside of them."]
	quest.1AA3AA74AE892B42.title: "Computer Casings"
	quest.1AA445F3BD99827B.quest_desc: ["Nobody knows who they are, or where they came from. They're just annoying at night, and too stupid to make a crafting table."]
	quest.1AA445F3BD99827B.title: "Time to Kill (Zombie)"
	quest.1AAC3D6D65404826.quest_desc: [
		"With casting available through the §3Crucible§r, many gun parts can now be created such as §6Barrels§r and §6Grips§r. An §3Ammo Press§r is used to create the various ammunitions guns use."
		""
		"A §3Weapon Modification Table§r can be used to install weapon mods, such as §6Silencers§r and §6Scopes§r."
		""
		"The §6Bullet Casing Bag§r will retrieve some of the casings when guns are fired."
	]
	quest.1AAC3D6D65404826.title: "Ammo Press and Guns"
	quest.1AAC7F9101B38EFB.quest_desc: ["The §3HE to RF Converter§r will convert energy produced by NTM machines into usuable power for both the §dMatter Energy Network§r and §dOpenComputers§r. It has a very large internal energy buffer, so it is recommended that a Diode is used to limit throughput."]
	quest.1AAC7F9101B38EFB.title: "HE to RF Converter"
	quest.1AB40D3AC02BE29C.quest_desc: [
		"§dOpenComputers§r is a very useful mod which will let one automate many processes which normaly couldnt be done even with an ME system."
		""
		"Make sure to always check the §6OC Manual§r as it provides additional information of stuff that the quest book doesnt cover."
	]
	quest.1AB40D3AC02BE29C.title: "Welcome to OC!"
	quest.1AC24BC1D0B38101.quest_desc: [
		"The §3Gas Giant Harvester Station§r is a device for collecting atmospheric air samples from gas giants."
		""
		"The concept is quite simple: on a planet that is a satellite of the giant (for example, to fly to the green giant Jool, you need to go to Laythe), the station is set up. After refueling with §bLiquid Oxygen§r and §bHydrogen§r, the §3harvester rocket§r is sent for air. In one trip, it delivers 16,000 mB§r. As you can understand, the harvester's§r functionality is completely analogous to the operation of §3MiningModules§r."
	]
	quest.1AC24BC1D0B38101.title: "Gas Giant Harvester"
	quest.1AD310A504B3AC56.quest_desc: [
		"While the §6Quest Book§r tries to give as much information as possible, it is not a full guide to all the content in the game."
		""
		"That's what §6Guide Book§r is used for! Community-curated, constantly growing and &zawesome§r-looking!"
		""
		"§2Note: this Guide Book can be opened via the keybind"
	]
	quest.1AD310A504B3AC56.title: "Guide Book"
	quest.1ADB92EFB4325917.quest_desc: ["This modpack is §cHARD§r and constantly get updates, so be ready to get your ass beaten."]
	quest.1ADB92EFB4325917.title: "NOT FOR CASUALS"
	quest.1AE165D3C9B2904A.quest_desc: ["The §6Military Grade Circuit Board§r is an advanced Circuit Board used in more complicated machines, such as the §3Gas Centrifuge§r."]
	quest.1AE165D3C9B2904A.title: "Military Grade Circuit Board"
	quest.1AFC270B71E88DB6.quest_desc: [
		"§6Crystalline Fullerite§r is an material which is primarely used in endgame machines, such as the §3ICF§r and the §3FEnSU§r."
		""
		"§2It is recommended that an Effectiveness 3 upgrade is installed on the Acidizer to increase the chance of not consuming the Fullerene, as fullerite can be expensive to produce large quantities."
	]
	quest.1AFC270B71E88DB6.title: "Crystalline Fullerite"
	quest.1B10C9D819AA3067.quest_desc: [
		"Three mods overhaul farming and food in this pack."
		""
		"§dPam's HarvestCraft§r adds 40+ crops, many fruit trees, 10 fish, beekeeping, and 75+ foods. Key blocks: §3Presser§r (produces oils, honey, etc.), §3Market§r (buys seeds and saplings for emeralds), §3Shipping Block§r (sells crops for emeralds). Right-clicking a mature crop harvests and replants it."
		""
		"§dAgriCraft§r adds genetics-based crop breeding. Plants have six stats - Growth, Gain, Strength, Resistance, Fertility, and Mutativity - inherited from parent crops when cross-breeding. Higher stats are dominant. Mutations can unlock new crop species entirely. Weeds will compete with and eventually kill unmanaged crops. Plants have specific soil, light, and fluid requirements, so placement matters."
		""
		"§dHunger Overhaul§r requires farmland to be placed adjacent to water - untouched dry tilled soil will not function."
		""
		"§2Note that the crops should be planted on the Crop Sticks."
	]
	quest.1B10C9D819AA3067.title: "Agriculture and Farming"
	quest.1B1FAF6B95238232.quest_desc: ["The §6Yharonite Billet§r is created in a tungsten crate that has §6Polonium Billets§r in it while being shot from a §3DFC Emitter§r. This is the final material obtained in the mod."]
	quest.1B1FAF6B95238232.title: "Yharonite Billet"
	quest.1B2E3C6470F548C0.quest_desc: [
		"The §3Spent Fuel Pool Drum§r is used to cool down hot nuclear fuel rods for the §3RBMK§r, §3ZIRNOX§r and §3PWR§r. It has 12 slots."
		""
		"The drum needs to have atleast one of its sides touching §bWater§r to work. The more sides that have water the faster the fuels inside will cool down."
	]
	quest.1B2E3C6470F548C0.title: "Spent Fuel Pool Drum"
	quest.1B448C68A88BFC8C.quest_desc: ["Be mean."]
	quest.1B448C68A88BFC8C.title: "Delinquent"
	quest.1B5E020C1730743D.quest_desc: [
		"The §3Vacuum Refinery§r is an oil refinery which processes §bPressurized/Desulfurized Crude Oil§r into 4 liquid products. It is a good way to make §bHigh-Performance Solvent§r by using §bReformate Gas§r and §bChlorine Gas§r in an §3Industrial Mixer§r."
		""
		"§2Compressors are needed for the oil to be inserted inside the Vacuum Refinery."
	]
	quest.1B5E020C1730743D.title: "Vacuum Refinery"
	quest.1B7135D6523C70BE.quest_desc: [
		"Satellites require dedicated infrastructure to launch, identify, and communicate with."
		""
		"Before anything leaves the ground, every satellite must be assigned a unique frequency using the §3Satellite ID Manager§r. Place the satellite in its right slot to generate a random frequency, then use the left and center slots to copy that frequency onto §6Satellite ID Chips§r or other linked devices such as designators. ID Chips are soldered, so prepare them in advance. The assigned frequency appears in the item's tooltip."
		""
		"Satellites can be launching using a custom rocket or Soyuz-FG."
		""
		"Once a satellite is in orbit, a §3Satellite Ground Station§r handles communication. It does not process §dRedstone-over-Radio§r signals directly - it requires an external RoR receiver or transmitter. It connects to one satellite at a time, switched via the appropriate §6Satellite ID Chip§r or an RoR command. RX reads data transmitted down from the satellite; TX sends commands up to it."
		""
		"§2The Ground Station's capabilities expand significantly when paired with an §3AUTOCAL§r§2, enabling automated satellite tracking, data processing, and chained multi-satellite logic."
	]
	quest.1B7135D6523C70BE.title: "Houston, We Have a Signal"
	quest.1B7EF17872CF0A80.quest_desc: [
		"§6Hazmat Suits§r provide protection against many hazards, mainly radiation. §6Hazmat Cloth§r can be further strengthened to create more resistant hazmat suits."
		""
		"To provide additional protection against environmental dangers, a §6Gas Mask Filter§r is needed, which can be equiped by right-clicking while holding it."
	]
	quest.1B7EF17872CF0A80.title: "Hazmat Suits"
	quest.1B80FA2F7E9C13ED.quest_desc: [
		"The §6§3Centrifuge§r allows for the seperation of ores, giving back more items than the usual mining method. It also seperates items into their respective items. Additionally, they are used in processing §e§6Bedrock Ores§r."
		""
		"Operating the centrifuge will consume §e4kHE/s§r."
	]
	quest.1B80FA2F7E9C13ED.title: "Centrifuge"
	quest.1B84DA25309DF7B0.quest_desc: ["The §3Orbital Station§r is a space station which is located at the orbit of §eEarth§r. §3Solar Panels§r in combination with §3Air Vents§r can be used to make a sustainable living environment in the station. Make sure to make airlocks to minimise air loss."]
	quest.1B84DA25309DF7B0.title: "Orbital Station"
	quest.1B883F2E0DAC40D7.quest_desc: ["§6Magnetized Tungsten§r is the product of combining §6Schrabidium§r and §6Tungsten§r in a §3Blast Furnace§r. It can also be rarely dropped by cybercrabs in §eMeteorite Dungeons§r."]
	quest.1B883F2E0DAC40D7.title: "Magnetized Tungsten"
	quest.1B8F15C92A14FA6C.quest_desc: ["The §3Energy Cell§r acts as a battery for the ME network. It becomes useful when the ME system begins to consume large amounts of energy, so a buffer is needed so it doesnt turn on and off constantly."]
	quest.1B8F15C92A14FA6C.title: "Energy Cell"
	quest.1B93730E2D94C8AB.quest_desc: [
		"§6Uranium-238§r is the most common uranium isotope in the game."
		""
		"This material has many uses, some of which are: §6Ferrouranium§r, MOX fuel, depleted uranium ammunition, absorber Pellets for the §3Watz§r powerplant and can also be turned into §6Schrabidium§r later on in the §3Exposure Chamber§r."
	]
	quest.1B93730E2D94C8AB.title: "Uranium-238"
	quest.1BB0959AA95E7F11.quest_desc: ["With fissile materials obtained from either §3Gas Centrifuges§r or nuclear fuel processing, nuclear bombs are made available."]
	quest.1BB0959AA95E7F11.title: "Fissile Materials"
	quest.1BB24BFB054A8FFD.quest_desc: [
		"The §3Mining Charge§r is an explosive made with the express purpose of mining, as such it's commonly used to mine depth ores, since it doesn't destroy drops, before getting a pickaxe that can do the same. Mining Charges are a great way of obtaining §6Zirconium§r from depth ores for nuclear fuel rods."
		""
		"It has an explosion radius of about 3 blocks and explodes instantly upon being powered by redstone, while exploding it does no damage to entities."
		""
		"There are two other variants of this, being the §3Timed Mining Charge§r and the §b§3Semtex Mining Charge§r, they are both timed explosives with the semtex one being stronger than the regular one and having §eFortune 3§r, meanwhile the timed mining charge does not seem to have enhanced capabilities, other than being timed and thus more convinient to use."
	]
	quest.1BB24BFB054A8FFD.title: "Mining Charge"
	quest.1BB26449680A844F.quest_desc: [
		"The §3Dyson Anatmogenesis Terraformer§r provides the most utility out of all the currently available §3Dyson converters§r, accepting a beam from a receiver and providing a direct energy to mass conversion, producing planetary scale atmospheric gases, terraforming any planet or moon as a player sees fit."
		""
		"By default it will release oxygen into an atmosphere, making it breathable once it crosses the 0.1atm threshold for breathing. A fluid identifier can be used to switch the gas emitted, and a screwdriver can switch it between emitting or extracting gases from the atmosphere."
		""
		"If powered with §e150THE/s§r power from a swarm (equivalent to a swarm size of 1,024), it will take 8 hours to reach 0.1atm of pressure."
	]
	quest.1BB26449680A844F.title: "Dyson Anatmogenesis Terraformer"
	quest.1BBC7FA8D31D1FA8.quest_desc: ["The §3Atmospheric Compressor§r collects air from different planets. In combination with a §3Cryogenic Distillation Machine§r it can produce many useful fluids and gasses."]
	quest.1BBC7FA8D31D1FA8.title: "Atmospheric Compressor"
	quest.1BC87262F103F37F.quest_desc: [
		"The §3Battery Socket§r is used to hold §6Batteries§r or §6Capacitors§r."
		""
		"Batteries have more energy storage, but a slower discharge time, meaning that only a small amount of stored power can be outputted to the grid."
		""
		"Capacitors on the other hand, have less energy storage, but a faster discharge time."
	]
	quest.1BC87262F103F37F.title: "Batteries"
	quest.1BC8B0DAB9784645.quest_desc: ["The §6Machine Upgrade Template§r is the baseline for all machine upgrades. Machine upgrades are not only used to increase the efficiency of machines but also to unlock new functions."]
	quest.1BC8B0DAB9784645.title: "Machine Upgrade Template"
	quest.1BCAE9E5FA92A6E7.quest_desc: ["§6Stainless Steel§r is an alloy made of §6Steel§r and §6Nickel§r."]
	quest.1BCAE9E5FA92A6E7.title: "Stainless Steel"
	quest.1BE3FBEB2F68BC80.quest_desc: [
		"The §3Steam Engine§r is an early game method of turning §bSteam§r into energy. It requires an external source to provide steam and a way to dump or reprocess the §bLow-Pressure Steam§r it produces."
		""
		"The Steam Engine has an energy efficiency of §e85%§r, making it better than the §3Stirling Engine§r. However, it still has a throughput limit as it can only hold up to 2000 mB of steam. Its maximum processing rate is 2000 mB/t, producing a considerable §e3400 HE/t§r or §e68 kHE/s§r. It is therefore the best generator available before §3Steam Turbines§r."
		""
		"A boiler being heated up by a heating oven using coal will produce §e17kHE/s§r."
	]
	quest.1BE3FBEB2F68BC80.title: "Steam Engine"
	quest.1BEAF4C7891989A1.quest_desc: ["§6Bobmazon§r is an in-game shop where players can spend §6Bottle Caps§r to purchase various items such as building blocks, plants, resourses and many more. To purchase items, one must have unlocked the achievements listed below as \"Ratings\"."]
	quest.1BEAF4C7891989A1.title: "Bobmazon"
	quest.1BEF5568CBFF8AB8.quest_desc: [
		"§6Pollution§r is a mechanic affecting several machines related to industrialization. It must be properly mitigated, lest suffer the consequences of a polluted world. There are 3 subtypes of pollution - soot, poison and heavy metal."
		""
		"§6Soot§r is most common, produced by fossil fuel burning and some other sources. It increases generic mob health and strength. At high enough levels, it becomes visible as smog."
		""
		"§6Poison§r harms unprotected entities at high enough levels, and is produced exclusively as the consequence from spilling fluids such as CO2 or various oil products."
		""
		"§6Heavy metal§r comes from the combustion of leaded fuels. It also increases mob strength, but also harms them at high enough levels."
		""
		"It can also be harmful to entities and players if they aren't wearing gas protection."
		""
		"Compatible machines can be connected to special exhaust pipes, which are effectively specialized box-ducts, to output to a §6Smokestack§r to reduce the amount of pollution."
		""
		"The §3Smokestack§r is used to reduce pollution made from machines. §3Exhaust Pipes§r, made in anvils, can be used to transport the fumes to the Smokestack. The §3Industrial Smokestack§r is needed to produce §6Fine Soot§r, required for making §6Fullerite§r in the late game."
		""
		"An §3Ashpit§r can be installed beneath the Smokestack which will collect §6Ash§r, that can be used as a cheap black dye alternative as well as in the creation of §6Industrial Fertilizer§r."
	]
	quest.1BEF5568CBFF8AB8.title: "Pollution and Smokestack"
	quest.1BF0A884722C6AF8.quest_desc: ["The §6Survey Scanner§r is a handheld device that will point out underground resourse deposits, such as §eDepth Rock§r and §eBedrock Ores§r."]
	quest.1BF0A884722C6AF8.title: "Survey Scanner"
	quest.1BF4118750F79376.quest_desc: ["§6Poisonous Mud§r is the byproduct of the §3Watz§r operating. This is the solidified version of it which can be used in a §3Crucible§r to create §6CMB Steel§r."]
	quest.1BF4118750F79376.title: "Solid Mud Brick"
	quest.1BFDF130D16DE962.quest_desc: ["The §6Overflow Void Card§r acts as a voiding upgrade for AE2 §6Storage Cells§r. It can be added to a storage cell using the §3Cell Workbench§r."]
	quest.1BFDF130D16DE962.title: "Overflow Void Card"
	quest.1C1E3341A3822D91.quest_desc: ["The §6Settings Tool§r is used to copy settings of machines. It is especially useful when making large refineries."]
	quest.1C1E3341A3822D91.title: "Settings Tool"
	quest.1C2CDAEB924B0EF6.quest_desc: ["The §6Jetpack§r can be used to travel upwards. It can be upgraded to unlock additional abilities, and can be equiped as an armor modification."]
	quest.1C2CDAEB924B0EF6.title: "Jetpack"
	quest.1C3A54B36D734855.quest_desc: [
		"The §6DNT Nanosuit§r is final goal of the mod. By crafting this armor you have reached the end of progression."
		""
		"§5Thanks for playing!"
	]
	quest.1C3A54B36D734855.title: "DNT Nanosuit"
	quest.1C423F24CB1D3EA0.quest_desc: [
		"§3Spatial IO§r is a way to cut-and-paste physical volumes of space in your world. It works by swapping the defined volume with an identically-sized volume in the spatial storage dimension, sending whatever's in the pylon array to the spatial storage dimension, and whatever's in the dimension to the pylon array."
		""
		"Spatial IO requires a specific arrangement of its components in order to function, and define the volume to be cut-and-pasted. All of the components must be on the same network in order to function, and you can have only one spatial IO setup on a network. Thus, a subnetwork is recommended."
		""
		"The §3Spatial IO Port§r controls the spatial IO operation. It shows stats on the multiblock setup, and holds the spatial cells"
		""
		"To perform a spatial IO operation, place a §6Spatial Storage Cell§r in the input slot and give the spatial IO port a redstone pulse. It will then swap the volume in the pylons with the volume in the spatial storage dimension. This means that if you send some set of blocks to the spatial storage dimension, then put another set of blocks in the pylons, put the cell back in the input slot, and trigger the IO port again, the 2nd set of blocks will disappear and the 1st set of blcks will reappear."
		""
		"Any entity in the defined volume, including you, will be carried along, and if you have no way of getting out, you will be trapped in the spatial storage dimension."
		""
		"§3Spatial Pylons§r are the main part of a spatial IO setup, and define the volume to be affected. The volume is defined by the bounding box of the outside of the pylons, contracted in by 1 block in all directions."
	]
	quest.1C423F24CB1D3EA0.title: "Spatial IO"
	quest.1C43F4B44387A2AC.quest_desc: [
		"§6Schrabidium§r is a dangerous material, but one which is needed for the creation of other items, such as §6Magnetized Tungsten§r and §6Ferric Schrabidate§r. It also makes for great reactor fuel. It can be created from exposing uranium ore to radiation using either a nuclear weapon or, more easily, by exploding radioactive barrels found in the abandoned nuclear powerplants in deserts."
		""
		"§2When holding Schrabidium, the player will receive the blindness effect, so it is recommended that a Suit which provides protection from both Bright Lights and Radiation is used."
	]
	quest.1C43F4B44387A2AC.title: "Schrabidium"
	quest.1C53A972D554D1EF.quest_desc: [
		"A §6Component Bus§r is a server-specific upgrade that allows the server to communicate with more components at the same time, without shutting down."
		""
		"Like with §6CPUs§r, higher tier buses provide higher component limits. Higher tier servers are also capable of taking more component buses, allowing for communication with many more components."
	]
	quest.1C53A972D554D1EF.title: "Component Buses"
	quest.1C5B32466A3966C0.quest_desc: ["The §6Quantum Processing Unit§r is the first quantum circuit one makes, used in the §3Particle Accelerator§r and §3ICF§r reactor."]
	quest.1C5B32466A3966C0.title: "Quantum Processing Unit"
	quest.1C64246D0553436F.quest_desc: ["Witches bring stitches because they are always infernal and very dangerous. Be careful since they throw potions at you."]
	quest.1C64246D0553436F.title: "Time to Kill (Witch)"
	quest.1C70908457578102.quest_desc: [
		"A §3Quantum Network Bridge§r is a multiblock structure that connects 2 potentially distant, or even in different dimensions, network fragments together. Created by crafting 8 §3ME Quantum Ring§r and a §3ME Quantum Link Chamber§r and placing the ME quantum link chamber in the center, and sourrounding it in the 8 ME quantum rings."
		""
		"[img height=1000]betterquesting:textures/QB_Qring1.png[/img]"
		""
		"Each quantum network bridge requires power to function. This power must be provided from the network fragment it is attached to until the bridge is linked; at which time power from either side will be available. However if power is lost, connectivity will fail and power will be drained from the side the bridge is on in attempt to restore connection."
		""
		"To establish a link between 2 quantum network bridges, you must create a pair of §6Quantum Entangled Singularities§r. One of each will be placed inside of a particular connection. Each Bridge may only connect to one other bridge."
		""
		"[img height=1000]betterquesting:textures/QB_Qring2.png[/img]"
		""
		"AE2 Singularities are created by dumping 256k of any block inside a §3Matter Condenser§r. Singularities can become quantum entangled by dropping a singularity and ender dust and then exploding them together."
	]
	quest.1C70908457578102.title: "Quantum Network Bridge"
	quest.1C81208DE6B8896D.quest_desc: [
		"§6Cadmium§r is a material needed to make §6Cadmium Stee§rl, which is a substitute of §6Technetium Steel§r."
		""
		"Cadmium can be obtained by smelting cadmium powder, which can be obtained acidizing 10 §6Mustard Willow leaves§r with 250mB of §bHigh-Perfomance Solvent§r in the §3Ore Acidizer§r."
		""
		"The mustard willow is a plant that can be found near §eBedrock Oil Deposits§r. When it's fully matured, the main item can be obtained, that being the mustard willow leaf."
	]
	quest.1C81208DE6B8896D.title: "Cadmium"
	quest.1C82F8ADB3945E4E.quest_desc: ["Eeeek! Wall climbing monsters, gross! Slay them. Quickly! Watch out for the witch spiders, they can give as good as they get."]
	quest.1C82F8ADB3945E4E.title: "Time to Kill (Spiders)"
	quest.1C95FBD68510E55B.quest_desc: [
		"§6Gerald the Construction Android§r is the most powerful weapon in the mod. Using this has the side effect of setting the world on fire but also getting tektite, which contains §6Osmiridium§r."
		""
		"Gerald is the hardest recipe of the mod requiring hundreds of thousands of items, mainly circuit related."
		""
		"Vast quantities of §6Bismuth§r, §6Tantalium§r and §6Silicon§r are needed, so dont hold back on bedrock ore processing and parallelisation of many processes. If you havent already used §dAE2§r, it is highly recommended at this stage of the game."
		""
		"Launching Gerald will result in a global firestorm that will decimate all life, including all trees and grass. Make sure to keep a backup of your world before launching him."
		""
		"§2Blueprints for Gerald and the Orbital Module can be found in structures or purchased from Bobmazon."
	]
	quest.1C95FBD68510E55B.title: "Gerald the Construction Android"
	quest.1C9AC8BF2BED9A29.quest_desc: [
		"Welcome to the Stone Age. This stage covers the essential survival mechanics you will need to progress, as well as several changes made to vanilla Minecraft that affect how you play from the very beginning."
		""
		"Work through the quests in this chapter to get up to speed before moving on."
		""
		"§2Complete these quests before progressing - later stages assume you know this material.§r"
	]
	quest.1C9AC8BF2BED9A29.title: "Stone Age"
	quest.1C9D095605C94133.quest_desc: [
		"The §3Orbital Death Ray§r is a high-destruction orbital weapon. Before launch, link it to a §6Satellite (Laser) Designator§r using the §3Satellite ID Manager§r. With a standard designator, enter target coordinates manually; with a laser designator, aim and hold right-click on the target block."
		""
		"Unlike the §3Orbital Precision Laser§r, it has no entity-tracking capability and cannot intercept rockets or hit fast-moving targets. The beam strikes the first surface in its path, so targets in deep cover are safe. Recharge time is §e5 minutes§r. RoR commands: \"fire\" fires at the current target position if the weapon is ready; \"canfire\" writes TRUE or FALSE to RX depending on whether it has finished recharging."
	]
	quest.1C9D095605C94133.title: "Orbital Death Ray"
	quest.1CA9EB89246687DD.quest_desc: ["The §3Compressor§r is a specialized multiblock machine for compressing fluids. It can perform this operation on any fluid to increase its pressure, for use in other machines. Some of these fluids are compressed into different fluids entirely as special recipes for this machine."]
	quest.1CA9EB89246687DD.title: "Compressor"
	quest.1CAE88C164F76E3E.quest_desc: ["The §6Charm of Protection§r diverts meteorites away from the player and prevents them from destoying blocks. It is recommended that one is obtained as soon as possible as to prevent costly damages in the future."]
	quest.1CAE88C164F76E3E.title: "Charm of Protection"
	quest.1CB583226B4B2AC1.quest_desc: [
		"Storage Drawers§r are an easy and cheap way of storing large amounts of items. They can be further upgraded to increase storage capacity as well as other abilities, such as voiding. They can also be §dChiseled§r to change their wood type."
		""
		"§2Many drawers may cause lag."
	]
	quest.1CB583226B4B2AC1.title: "Storage Drawers"
	quest.1CBDE43D6872421D.quest_desc: ["Oh no, not the poor sheep! Fluffy and red, I'm so sad."]
	quest.1CBDE43D6872421D.title: "Time to Kill (Sheep)"
	quest.1CCDEEC664979FC2.quest_desc: ["The§3 Crystal Growth Chamber§r is a machine in which crystals can grow at an increased speed, while also being in a block instead of being dropped in the ground."]
	quest.1CCDEEC664979FC2.title: "Crystal Growth Chamber"
	quest.1CD592A6CCD6B166.quest_desc: ["An upgraded version of the §3Anvil§r, [T7], which unlocks additional recipes."]
	quest.1CD592A6CCD6B166.title: "Dineutronium Anvil"
	quest.1CDBE4F8F1E03431.quest_desc: [
		"The §3Flare Stack§r is a generator that produces energy by burning flammable liquids and gases. Any fluid tagged as Flammable can serve as fuel - supply it through pipes or directly via containers."
		""
		"Operation uses three steps. First, fill the internal buffer (capacity: §e64,000 mB§r) with fuel. Second, open the §6Flow Valve§r at the top of the middle section to release fuel from the buffer into the combustion system. Third, enable the §6Ignition§r switch at the bottom of the middle section to ignite the fuel and begin power generation."
		""
		"Efficiency is low: gases burn at §e50%§r and liquids at only §e10%§r. Output also varies by fuel type."
		""
		"Two upgrades are available: the §6Speed Upgrade§r increases throughput, and the §6Effectiveness Upgrade§r improves fuel efficiency."
	]
	quest.1CDBE4F8F1E03431.title: "Flare Stack"
	quest.1CF116ECDBF4CAE1.quest_desc: [
		"The §3Deuterium Extraction Tower§r is a much larger version of the Deuterium Extractor, making it an easy and viable way of making cheap fuel for the §b§r§3Fusion Reactor§r."
		""
		"§2A Ferrouranium Anvil is required.§r"
	]
	quest.1CF116ECDBF4CAE1.title: "Deuterium Extraction Tower"
	quest.1CF136DA97CE3422.quest_desc: [
		"With the §6§3Automatic Buzz Saw§r one can automatically farm trees for their §6Wood§r, aswell as other crops such as §6Hemp§r and §6Wheat§r."
		""
		"§3Fans§r, when powered by redstone, can be used to push the dropped items into hoppers or conveyors for storage. Use a §6Drill§r on them to remove the diminishing behaviour of pushing force."
	]
	quest.1CF136DA97CE3422.title: "Automatic Buzz Saw"
	quest.1CF8B411E574DE10.quest_desc: ["You should be careful with this task. Fire protection is highly recommended. [warn]Blazes are always spawning infernal.[/warn]"]
	quest.1CF8B411E574DE10.title: "Time to Kill (Blaze)"
	quest.1D048B3A49C39557.quest_desc: ["The §3Arc Welder§r is a machine needed for the creation of many components, such as §6Welded Plates§r, §6Missile Parts§r and more. Some Recipes will require a fluid inserted into the welder to work."]
	quest.1D048B3A49C39557.title: "Arc Welder"
	quest.1D051E9EDF4E6E21.quest_desc: [
		"The §3Electric Furnace§r is a furnace that is powered by electricity. it is slightly faster than the vanilla furnace without upgrades. it consumes from §e1 kHE/s§r without upgrades up to §e4 kHE/s§r."
		""
		"Due to it only being slightly faster than the vanilla furnace, it isn't used much beyond early game, but it can be used in automation, if speed isn't the main objective."
	]
	quest.1D051E9EDF4E6E21.title: "Electric Furnace"
	quest.1D087FE98E04A431.quest_desc: ["A beautiful water world, teeming with life, oceans lit up with fields of glowgrass. §bJool gas§r can be harvested from here using a §3Gas Giant Harvester§r."]
	quest.1D087FE98E04A431.title: "Laythe"
	quest.1D0F5C3AB499F32F.quest_desc: [
		"Before §bCrude Oil§r can be processed, it must be heated up in a §3Boiler§r."
		""
		"The §3Oil Refinery§r splits Hot Crude Oil(or later on §bCracked§r) into four different fluid products and one solid byproduct."
		""
		"After that, those fluids can be sent through a §3Fractioning Tower§r to obtain different kinds of fuels, such as §bKerosene§r and §bDiesel§r. A §3Fractioning Tower Seperator§r can be used to stack fractioning towers ontop of eachother."
	]
	quest.1D0F5C3AB499F32F.title: "Basic Oil Processing"
	quest.1D110B29CE6F7414.quest_desc: ["§6Bakelite§r is an alternative to Polymer and can be used for the same recipes. Since it doesnt require any §6Coal Powder§r or §6Fluorite§r to be made, it is easier and more convenient to automate than §6Polymer§r."]
	quest.1D110B29CE6F7414.title: "Bakelite"
	quest.1D223AEDA900F997.quest_desc: ["The §6Pattern Capacity Card§r can be used to add 9 more slots for patterns in an §3ME Interface§r. Up to 3 cards can be inserted."]
	quest.1D223AEDA900F997.title: "Pattern Capacity Card"
	quest.1D309F469AE7BE3C.quest_desc: [
		"Not a bug, a &zFEATURE§r!"
		""
		"When you consume food your hands may shake weirdly, as if Steve was EXTREMELY happy for that lunch."
		""
		"If you experience any stutters/micro-lags while playing, try turning Vsync on/off. If that does not help, contact in Discord #help."
		""
		"Currently we have no idea how to fix those bugs, but we are trying our best!"
	]
	quest.1D309F469AE7BE3C.title: "Known Issues"
	quest.1D34CDBC26BFF5BE.quest_desc: [
		"The §3Rocket Transporter Station§r is essential for sending and receiving cargo between celestial bodies."
		""
		"§3Transport rockets§r, similar to §3resource modules§r or §3Gas Giant Harvesters§r, automatically move various cargoes. To make the system work, you need at least one pair of linked platforms§r."
		""
		"The platforms have compartments for outgoing and incoming items (blue and orange, respectively)§r, and they can handle liquids with §3dedicated buffers§r."
		""
		"To link platforms, Shift+Right-Click with the §6Rocket Transporter Connector§r on one platform to save it, then Right-Click on another platform. To open the linker interface§r, Right-Click on a platform with the connector: it will display information about the linked platforms' locations."
		""
		"To designate one of these points as the receiving point, click the button at the beginning of the row§r."
		""
		"To launch the transporter rocket§r, the station must be fueled with §bliquid oxygen§r and §bhydrogen§r."
	]
	quest.1D34CDBC26BFF5BE.title: "Rocket Transporter Pad"
	quest.1D37CC19F9969E69.quest_desc: [
		"§2This quest serves an a guide on how to order items using the ME system. The example item will be an Analog Circuit.§r"
		""
		"With an §3ME Drive§r providing item storage, a §3Crafting CPU§r and §3Interfaces§r, one can request any item to be crafted. The image below makes use of a §3Molecular Assembler§r, a §3Soldering Station§r, an §3Electric Press§r aswell as two §3Import Buses§r which serve as an output for the solderer and press."
		""
		"[img height=1000]betterquesting:textures/BQ_Auto1.png[/img]"
		""
		"The first step in automating crafting recipes is to encode §6ME Patterns§r. There are two types of patterns, crafting and processing. The crafting pattern is created by having the §3Pattern Terminal§r set to the crafting table. After placing the items in the terminal, press the arrow to finish encoding the recipe."
		""
		"[img height=1000]betterquesting:textures/BQ_Auto2.png[/img]"
		""
		"For recipes which arent made in a crafting table, such as the §6Wires§r and the §6Analog Circuit§r itself, the pattern terminal needs to be switched to the processing mode, which has a furnace icon."
		""
		"[img height=1000]betterquesting:textures/BQ_Auto3.png[/img]"
		""
		"After all the patterns have been created, insert them into their respective interfaces."
		"Make sure to enable blocking mode on the interfaces as not to have multiple different recipes enter the interface at once."
		""
		"[img height=1000]betterquesting:textures/BQ_Auto4.png[/img]"
		""
		"Finally, after everything has been set up, the option to order items will be shown in the ME terminal."
		""
		"[img height=1000]betterquesting:textures/BQ_Auto5.png[/img]"
	]
	quest.1D37CC19F9969E69.title: "AE2 Autocrafting"
	quest.1D531637DF250FB0.quest_desc: ["The §6Starmetal Pickaxe§r is used as a crafting component for the §6Molten§r and §6Bismuth Pickaxes§r, both being unbreakable and having a lot of abilities. Additionally, both can be used to mine §eDepth Rock§r."]
	quest.1D531637DF250FB0.title: "Starmetal Pickaxe"
	quest.1D56C1A1F6A837D1.quest_desc: [
		"The §6Central Processing Unit§r (CPU), is a core part for each computer or §6Server§r. It defines the architecture of the computer, and the number of components that can be connected to the computer before it stops working."
		"Higher tier CPUs also provide a higher per-tick direct call limit to the computer - in simpler terms: better CPUs run faster."
	]
	quest.1D56C1A1F6A837D1.title: "CPUs"
	quest.1D6E066FCC7EC13B.quest_desc: [
		"The §3Wideband Radio Emission Detector Satellite§r monitors the entire map for high-energy events with no range limit, returning only an approximate location. Use it as a first-pass detection layer - once a hit is found, follow up with the §3Narrowband Emission Scanning Satellite§r or §3Radar Satellite§r to pinpoint the source."
		""
		"Events are grouped by intensity. LOW covers mini-nuke detonations, accurate to within 10,000 m. MEDIUM covers active radars and particle accelerators, accurate to within 2,500 m. HIGH covers nuclear explosions, accurate to within 500 m. MEDIUM events persist for only half a second while others last up to a minute, so rapid repeated scans are recommended."
		""
		"RoR commands: \"esurvey\" collects all active results; \"ecount\" writes the total to RX; \"egettype\" writes LOW, MEDIUM, or HIGH for a given index; \"egetposition\" writes approximate X/Z coordinates for a given index."
		""
		"§2Route this satellite's output through an §3AUTOCAL§r§2 to automatically cue more precise instruments when a hit is detected."
	]
	quest.1D6E066FCC7EC13B.title: "Wideband Radio Emission Detector Satellite"
	quest.1D717092047E53B7.quest_desc: [
		"This mod adds several environmental hazards that will kill you if ignored."
		""
		"§6Radiation§r is measured in RAD. Effects begin at §e200 RAD§r and worsen steadily - instant death occurs at §c1000 RAD§r. Use a §6Geiger Counter§r to monitor your dose. Radiation-resistant armor and §6Rad-X§r reduce incoming RAD; a §3Player Decontaminator§r or §6Antirads§r remove accumulated dose."
		""
		"§lMesothelioma§r develops from asbestos exposure. Items tagged §c[Contains Asbestos]§r and certain blocks like Chrysotile release asbestos particles. Progresses to death if untreated."
		""
		"§lBlack Lung§r develops from coal dust exposure. Mining coal ore and carrying items tagged §c[Coal Dust]§r are the main sources. Also fatal."
		""
		"A gas mask protects against both mesothelioma and black lung simultaneously. Both diseases are cured by §6SIOX Cancer Medication§r or, early-game, §6Herbal Paste§r - the latter being weaker and carrying side effects."
	]
	quest.1D717092047E53B7.title: "Hazards"
	quest.1D722BB05E76CB80.quest_desc: ["The §6Screwdriver§r is used to rotate conveyor blocks as well as to create a §3Chicago Pile§r. It can also be used in combination with §6Bobby Pins§r to unlock §6Safes§r found in various structures."]
	quest.1D722BB05E76CB80.title: "Safes and lockpicking"
	quest.1D72E846B4557074.quest_desc: [
		"§6Tantalium§r is a material needed for the creation of some items, most importantly §6Capacitor Boards§r. Tantalium Polycrystal production requires §6Coltan§r which can be located by the use of a §6Coltass§r. Coltan can also be obtained by using the mining drill in a §eBedrock Ore Coltan Deposit§r located randomly on planet Dres. Tantalum can also be obtained via §3Watz Reactor§r."
		""
		"§2Coltan Processing at its early stage can provide Niobium needed for Catalytic Cracking Towers."
	]
	quest.1D72E846B4557074.title: "Tantalium"
	quest.1D7ED03601FF01B9.quest_desc: [
		"The §6Graphics Card§r is an essential part for most computers and allows the computer to display text on a connected §6Screen§r."
		""
		"Graphics cards come in several tiers, and like screens, support different resolutions and color depths."
	]
	quest.1D7ED03601FF01B9.title: "Graphics Cards"
	quest.1D7F94AD79D71FEB.quest_desc: ["The §3Charging Station§r will charge electric tools aswell as electric suits when standing near it. Placing more next to eachother will increase the speed at which items are being recharged."]
	quest.1D7F94AD79D71FEB.title: "Charging Station"
	quest.1D82B446ADF69301.quest_desc: ["The §3Dairy Processing Tank§r, while it can be crafted earlier, is very useful on Minmus because of the infinite §bMilk§r production from §3Pumps§r. It can be used to process milk into different liquids, which can then be used to make food items."]
	quest.1D82B446ADF69301.title: "Dairy Processing Tank"
	quest.1D97071132605915.quest_desc: [
		"The §6Digamma Laser Crystal§r is the fastest and final laser crystal which can be used in a SILEX."
		""
		"§2If the laser touches any block, the surrounding area will be atomized."
	]
	quest.1D97071132605915.title: "Digamma Laser Crystal"
	quest.1D99529D9F5D9A65.quest_desc: [
		"The §3Electronic Assembler§r is an advanded workstation that can be used to build more complex electronic devices, such as §3Robots§r, §3Drones§r and §6Tablets§r."
		""
		"They require a large amount of energy to assemble devices, so it is recommended to power them sufficiently with a §3Capacitor Bank§r."
	]
	quest.1D99529D9F5D9A65.title: "Electronic Assembler"
	quest.1DBA66B6B45B29E0.quest_desc: [
		"The §3Crucible§r is a block from §dEx Nihilo§r used to melt solid blocks down into fluids. It is crafted first as an §6Unfired Crucible§r from §6Porcelain Clay§r, then fired in a furnace to produce a usable §3Crucible§r."
		""
		"To operate it, place the §3Crucible§r above a heat source and right-click it with an eligible block to load it. The block will slowly melt into fluid over time. The speed of melting depends entirely on the heat source below - stronger heat sources melt faster. Burning §6Netherrack§r is among the most efficient vanilla options."
		""
		"The primary output is §blava§r, produced by melting cobblestone, stone, and similar blocks. The §3Crucible§r can hold fluids indefinitely, making it a cheap fluid storage vessel in a pinch. Drain it using fluid pipes connected to its side or bottom."
		""
		"§2A bank of Crucibles over burning Netherrack is a reliable early lava farm."
	]
	quest.1DBA66B6B45B29E0.title: "Primitive Crucible"
	quest.1DC1DCA6C05D48BE.quest_desc: ["The §6Acceleration Card§r increases the speed of various AE2 devices."]
	quest.1DC1DCA6C05D48BE.title: "Acceleration Card"
	quest.1DC35BA81CB72EFB.quest_desc: ["§6Ferrouranium§r is an alloy of §6Uranium-238§r and §6Steel§r."]
	quest.1DC35BA81CB72EFB.title: "Ferrouranium"
	quest.1DE9A912FE1A04C4.quest_desc: [
		"The §3Bricked Furnace§r is almost the same as the vanilla furnace, but it can smelt construction materials faster, such as §6Sand§r and §6Cobblestone§r being smelted at double the speed. §6Clay§r and §6Fire Clay§r can be smelted at §e§rquadruple§r the speed, which means that making a full brick block can be done within a vanilla furnace operation. It can also make §6Charcoal§r at double the speed. It can also collect Ashes from burnt fuel."
		""
		"The §3Iron Furnace§r has the base smelting speed §e20%§r faster than the vanilla furnace, which means it can complete an operation within 8 seconds instead of 10 seconds. Besides being able to smelt faster, it consumes fuel only during operation, so the fuel is never wasted. It also has burn time bonuses for various kinds of fuel, ranging from §e+25%§r for lignite to §e+100%§r for solid fuel."
		""
		"§dEt Futurum Requiem§r also backports modern furnaces, such as the §3Smoker§r, which cooks food faster, and the §3Blast Furnace§r, which smelts ores faster."
	]
	quest.1DE9A912FE1A04C4.title: "Better Furnaces"
	quest.1DEAF4AF8B3B372A.quest_desc: [
		"§3Dyson Swarms§r consist of thousands of swarm members encircling the parent star of a system, and energy production from the swarm scales based on the number of members in a swarm. These satellites do not last indefinitely however, they attenuate (decay) over time, with the chance of decay increasing as the number of swarm members increase."
		""
		"§6Dyson Swarm Members§r must be launched into solar orbit via the use of a huge centrifugal launch platform, known as the §3Spinlauncher§r. The spinlauncher launches 4 swarm members at a time, consuming a large amount of electricity to do so."
		""
		"The §3Dyson Receiver§r is the main machine required for collecting energy from the swarm. It collimates the immense energy collected from the swarm into a immensely powerful beam. Setting up requires only a satellite ID chip that is matched to an existing swarm. The energy beam must be pointed towards a Dyson Power Converter."
		""
		"The §3Satellite Dyson Relay§r can be used to allow dyson swarms to provide power during night time."
	]
	quest.1DEAF4AF8B3B372A.title: "Dyson Swarms"
	quest.1DEF378DEEC7DC5C.quest_desc: [
		"§cWelcome to Nuclear Tech: New Horizons!§r"
		""
		"Please read the following information before starting out."
		""
		"§b1) Remember to Claim your base and Chunkload your reactors using Server Utilities (from the inventory)."
		""
		"&b2) If shaders are glitching out try to use fancy textures."
		""
		"&b3) If you are encountering any rendering problems, try to scroll around in NEI."
		""
		"&b4) If you are playing with friends, make sure to invite them in your FTB Team as to share progression and rewards."
	]
	quest.1DEF378DEEC7DC5C.title: "Modpack information"
	quest.1DF0D5047E667298.quest_desc: [
		"§dStorage Drawer Keys§r can be used to modify Drawers in many ways."
		""
		"The §dDrawer Key locks drawers§r, so no new item types can be inserted into the drawer when its empty."
		""
		"The §dConcealment Key§r hides the item icon of drawers."
		""
		"The §dQuantify Key§r shows the item quantities of drawers."
		""
		"The §dPersonal Key§r protects drawers from other players (outside of claims)."
	]
	quest.1DF0D5047E667298.title: "Storage Drawer Keys"
	quest.1DFCB70685681FC1.quest_desc: ["The §3Charger§r is a machine which will charge §6Certus Quartz Crystals§r into their charged form at the expense of power."]
	quest.1DFCB70685681FC1.title: "Charger"
	quest.1E0B29A380453710.quest_desc: [
		"Increasus damge takn by 5x tims"
		"Bestest armr in da wurld!!!!!!1!!1!!"
		""
		"Staje of da gaim - Brayn Partiklz"
		"Protekshun levl - Funtastick"
		"Feetchurs - Yoor Btes Chois"
	]
	quest.1E0B29A380453710.title: "Dineurtom amrr"
	quest.1E1A826BE90B9287.quest_desc: ["The §3ICF Laser Turbocharger§r can be placed next to §3ICF Laser Capacitors§r to increase the laser's power by a substantial amount, allowing for the §3ICF§r to run higher grade fuels."]
	quest.1E1A826BE90B9287.title: "ICF Laser Turbocharger"
	quest.1E2209D4F9E3A40E.quest_desc: ["The §3Electric Groundpump§r can be used to quickly generate §bWater§r, making it very useful later on for filling large §3Tanks§r and reactors. The pump requires a 3x3 cube of dirt directly beneath it and must be below Y:70, otherwise it won't work."]
	quest.1E2209D4F9E3A40E.title: "Electric Groundwater Pump"
	quest.1E372968399CB4B8.quest_desc: ["The §3Mining Laser§r is a laser drill which can be used to quickly dig large areas. It has a §e100 MHE§r internal power buffer and a 64,000mB internal §bCrude Oil§r buffer. Its default radius is 3, which can be increased by the use of an effectiveness upgrade. It can also be equiped with various upgrades to unlock new functions such as shredding or voiding."]
	quest.1E372968399CB4B8.title: "Mining Laser"
	quest.1E3E8D49CA3C7BFA.quest_desc: ["The §6HEV Mark IV§r is a strong electric armor set, with the intent of keeping the user safe primarely from dangerous hazards, such as high levels of radiation, fire, certain air particles and more. The suit comes equiped with an §6Geiger Counter§r and custom hud."]
	quest.1E3E8D49CA3C7BFA.title: "HEV Mark IV"
	quest.1E4202ED4767F8C1.quest_desc: [
		"The §3FEL§r or Free Electron Laser is a large multiblock utilized with the SILEX to produce various laser wavelengths needed for all SILEX recipes."
		""
		"A single FEL can power up to 5 SILEX'es. In order to stop the laser any concrete block can be in the its path."
		""
		"The lower the wavelength of the crystal, the faster recipes will be completed."
		""
		"The §6§3SILEX§r is a machine that separates isotopes and elements from compounds or other materials via the SILEX (Separation of Isotopes by Laser Exitation) process. It allows for easier enrichment of §6Uranium§r, §6Plutonium§r, and §6Australium§r."
		""
		"The SILEX can also process §6Lapis Lazuli§r into §6Sulfur§r, §6Aluminium§r, and most importantly §6Cobalt§r. It can use §bHydrogen Peroxide§r to liquify any material to be processed, the material may even be in a powder state. The processed items come out into the right side collection of slots."
		""
		"The SILEX must be placed at least 2 blocks away from activated FEL laser, or else its going to melt."
	]
	quest.1E4202ED4767F8C1.title: "FEL and SILEX"
	quest.1E4A94D1B54C2B24.quest_desc: [
		"The §3Microgravity Algae Film§r is a machine is made of specialized layers of laythe plants that will convert §bCarbon Dioxide§r directly into §bLiquid Oxygen§r. They however only function when in orbit."
		""
		"The §3CO2 Scrubber§r allows you to recover carbon dioxide from a pressurized room. This is occasionally useful when building space stations."
	]
	quest.1E4A94D1B54C2B24.title: "Microgravity Algae Film"
	quest.1E5C81B64F30ABA9.quest_desc: [
		"The §3Precision Assembly Machine§r is a machine which can produce §6Blueprints§r. Due to the recipes having a low success rate, automation of the ingredient is recommended."
		""
		"Pufferfish can be obtained from throwing §6Fishing Dynamite§r in water."
	]
	quest.1E5C81B64F30ABA9.title: "Precision Assembly Machine"
	quest.1E5E412B7517C5F1.quest_desc: ["When a §6Tectonic Missile§r hits, it creates a volcano that immediately starts to splash volcanic lava everywhere. Which is what you need to get the volcanic gem!"]
	quest.1E5E412B7517C5F1.title: "Tectonic Missile"
	quest.1E74A2890D202D40.quest_desc: [
		"In this modpack, §dApplied Energistics 2§r has been changed to fit in more with §dNTM§r. Many components have been changed to include NTM materials and some machines, like the §3Grinder§r and §3Inscriber§r, have had their functions moved to the §3Shredder§r and §3Press§r. The meteors have also been removed, but §6Skystone§r can still be crafted for building purposes."
		""
		"This Chapter of the quests has its information derived from the FTB Wiki. If anything else is missing from the quest book, please visit the wiki."
		""
		"[ { \"text\": \"https://ftbwiki.org/Applied_Energistics_2\",\"color\":\"aqua\", \"underlined\": true, \"clickEvent\": { \"action\": \"open_url\", \"value\": \"https://ftbwiki.org/Applied_Energistics_2\" } } ]"
	]
	quest.1E74A2890D202D40.title: "AE2 Changes"
	quest.1E89A57BDA20048E.quest_desc: [
		"§6Silkworms§r are items from §dEx Nihilo§r and the primary way to produce §6String§r on resource-limited maps. They cannot be crafted - the only way to obtain one is as a rare drop when breaking leaves with a §6Crook§r."
		""
		"To use a §6Silkworm§r, right-click it onto any leaves block. The leaves will slowly become infested, turning white over time, and the infestation will spread on its own to adjacent leaves. Fully white leaves produce more §6String§r than partially infested ones, so it is worth waiting."
		""
		"Once the leaves are fully infested, break them with a §6Crook§r or your fist to collect §6String§r and additional §6Silkworms§r, keeping the process renewable. Note that infested leaves do not drop saplings or apples, so keep spare saplings set aside before"
		"infesting a tree."
		""
		"§2Silkworms can also be composted in a Barrel if you have a surplus."
	]
	quest.1E89A57BDA20048E.title: "Silkworm"
	quest.1E90A5D5C9E15358.quest_desc: [
		"§cNTNH§r is a modular modpack, so you are free to add/remove/modify config/mods if it works!"
		""
		"§dNTM§r offers a very modular config file, which also comes with additional modes one can activate. These can be enabled in the hbm.cfg file."
		""
		"§2Expensive Mode§r makes everything more expensive by requiring not only more resourses, but also new components. The quest book will not reflect the changes in progression if its enabled."
		""
		"§2528 Mode§r introduces gates in the form of templates which are unlocked by destroying a certain amount of items in an §3Annihilator§r. Additionally, some items, mainly circuits, are percentage based now to be crafted. Along with that, theres also more changes that make the game harder, such as §6Tantalum§r generating in a certain area, landmines spawning more frequently and all §dAE2§r blocks §4EXPLODE§r when used."
		""
		"Many recycling probabilities of the §3Precision Assembler§r are massively lowered with expensive mode enabled, increasing effective cost massively."
		""
		"§2Rampant Mode§r makes glyphids a very big threat as pollution now makes them way stronger and more aggresive. New more destructive types of glyphids will also become more common. If high enough pollution has been reached, glyphid scouts can spawn passively, which makes automated defense systems necessary as to prevent new hives from being created."
		""
		"§2For modes with recipe changes, the modpack's recipes have to be inserted again after a new hbmrecipes folder has been created and modes enabled.§r"
	]
	quest.1E90A5D5C9E15358.title: "Additional NTM Modes"
	quest.1E988AB08E35D064.quest_desc: [
		"There are many tools which will help you progress through the mod, the most important ones being:"
		""
		"§6Tungsten Reachers§r, which reduce the radiation the player gets exposed to from items in their inventory, as well as allowing them to hold some very hot items."
		""
		"§6Mk.V Crate Opening Device \"Crowbar\"§r, which is used to open crates for loot such as food and ammunition found in various structures."
	]
	quest.1E988AB08E35D064.title: "Useful Tools"
	quest.1E9A936AD946336B.quest_desc: ["§6Saturnite§r is a very durable, heat-resistant and corrosion-resistant alloy that is commonly used for making stronger gun parts. It is also used to make §6Starmetal§r and is an important component of the §3Watz§r reactor."]
	quest.1E9A936AD946336B.title: "Saturnite"
	quest.1E9DF41EA718D1DC.quest_desc: ["§6Dineutronium§r is the mod's (almost) ultimate material. It's a final tier material and is a higher tier than even §6Euphemium§r. It is very difficult to produce and it's used to make the most absurd and broken items this mod has. The only material that is more difficult to make, would be §6Osmiridium§r."]
	quest.1E9DF41EA718D1DC.title: "Dineutronium"
	quest.1EA4C567A87DD07E.quest_desc: [
		"The §3Solar Tower Boiler§r is an earlygame machine that can use sunlight from heliostat mirrors to boil water and therefore turn it into steam."
		""
		"The Solar Tower Boiler gets heat from heliostat mirrors pointed at it. Aiming a mirror at the boiler can be done using the mirror adjustment tool, right-click on the boiler will save its position to the tool, and subsequently clicking on mirrors will aim them at the linked boiler. The maximum range for mirrors is 25 blocks, mirror efficiency does not degrade with range. A boiler consumes 1mB of water for every 12.5 mirrors each tick at full sunlight level, and 100mB of steam per mB of water consumed. However, the water consumption rate is rounded down to the millibucket. Thus it takes 13 mirrors to raise your first 100mB/t of steam, 12 mirrors for the next hundred, then 13, 12, and so on."
		""
		"As the heat provided by each mirror is based on sunlight, mirrors with solid blocks above them will not work, and the amount of heat diminishes with the amount of light in the evening until it produces no heat at night."
		""
		"The solar tower boiler can only produce regular steam, and thus the liquid type cannot be changed using fluid identifiers."
	]
	quest.1EA4C567A87DD07E.title: "Solar Tower Boiler"
	quest.1EA587D90CC0D8B5.quest_desc: [
		"The §3CO2 Scrubber§r is a mechanism for cleaning air in sealed environments under increased pressure."
		""
		"The device absorbs §bCarbon Dioxide§r from the surrounding air and collects it. It only works if two conditions are met: the room is sealed and isolated, and the air pressure is elevated (above 1.0 atm). The latter can be achieved by adding a stream of §bOxygen§r from the ventilation to the Earth's air (resulting in a total pressure of 1.1 atm)."
		""
		"§2The maximum number of scrubbers in a room is 5; any additional units placed will not collect carbon dioxide.§r"
	]
	quest.1EA587D90CC0D8B5.title: "CO2 Scrubber"
	quest.1EA5C2328A243F9D.quest_desc: [
		"A strange world, similar to §eEarth§r, where life is different because the vegetation, the only form of life there, is made of complex polymers, like rubber§r and plastic§r."
		""
		"Tekto bedrock ore doesn’t have the non-metal variant; instead, it is replaced by the plastic variant, from which the player can obtain §6Polymer§r, §6Rubber§r, §6Semtex§r and §6PVC§r."
	]
	quest.1EA5C2328A243F9D.title: "Tekto"
	quest.1EBF756D7C061141.quest_desc: ["§bReformate Gas§r is used in welding very durable materials, as well as used in making §6Saturnite§r."]
	quest.1EBF756D7C061141.title: "Reformate Gas"
	quest.1EC8517F35850615.quest_desc: ["§6Welded Osmiridium Plates§r cost 300 Billion §eHE§r to produce, so good energy generation and storage infrastructure is needed."]
	quest.1EC8517F35850615.title: "Welded Osmiridium Plate"
	quest.1ECCA2CD4B86F294.quest_desc: [
		"The §3Boiler§r, when receiving heat from below, heats up fluids. Two important uses of the boiler are for §bSteam§r and §bOil§r processing which will come later on. The Boiler can explode if its output is full."
		""
		"Steam, when used by machines, such as reactors sending steam through §3Turbines§r or §3Chemical Factories§r produce §bLow-Pressure Steam§r. The low-pressure steam can be recycled back to retrieve 100% of the water by using a §3Steam Condenser§r. Closed water loops are recommended for reactors."
	]
	quest.1ECCA2CD4B86F294.title: "Boiler and Steam Condenser"
	quest.1ED84AE80B2D3BC0.quest_desc: ["§6Modifier Cards§r allow for modification to various ME components, such as speeding them up or being able to toggle them on and off using redstone."]
	quest.1ED84AE80B2D3BC0.title: "Modifier Cards"
	quest.1EF0AB411591ECE3.quest_desc: ["§6Wood§r obtained from a tree farm can be smelted or processed in a §3Combination Oven§r to produce §6Charcoal§r, which has many uses, such as fuel for §3Furnaces§r or even the §3Blast Furnace§r, §6Flux§r or §6Carbon§r in a Crucible for §6Steel§r production, or even §6Gunpowder§r for ammunition."]
	quest.1EF0AB411591ECE3.title: "Charcoal Automation"
	quest.1EFA6A34B4EFE73F.quest_desc: ["The §6Solid State Quantum Processor§r is the first quantum circuit related component needed to make §6Quantum Processing Units§r and §6Quantum Computers§r."]
	quest.1EFA6A34B4EFE73F.title: "Solid State Quantum Processor"
	quest.1EFC19737593AB7D.quest_desc: ["§6Starmetal§r is a unique alloy made from combining §6Saturnite§r with §6Meteorite Powder§r in a §3Blast Furnace§r."]
	quest.1EFC19737593AB7D.title: "Starmetal"
	quest.1F09B697D9EEF23B.quest_desc: ["The §3Steel Furnace§r, unlike the other furnaces, runs off of §eTU§r. It can also process up to 3 items at a time, but each slot consumes more TU, which makes it slow without a strong heat source. It also has a bonus output for ores and wood, where every smelted item gives §e25%§r to the bonus output meter, which means every 4 items give an extra 5th item for free (§e+15 items from a single stack§r)."]
	quest.1F09B697D9EEF23B.title: "Steel Furnace"
	quest.1F2E4A4B330C11BC.quest_desc: [
		"§dHunger Overhaul§r makes hunger a genuine threat rather than a mild inconvenience."
		""
		"Hunger now drains passively over time, even while idle. Reaching zero kills you instantly. Low hunger inflicts slowness, weakness, and reduced mining speed before that point. Eating grants a §6Well Fed§r effect that boosts health regeneration - the larger the meal, the longer it lasts."
		""
		"Food values are re-balanced by meal size. Raw ingredients restore very little; prepared meals restore substantially more. Larger meals take longer to eat and stack less in your inventory."
		""
		"Crops only grow during daytime and take much longer to mature. Wood and stone hoes are removed - you need at least an iron hoe to till soil. Farmland must be placed adjacent to water or it will not function."
		""
		"§dSpice of Life: Carrot Edition§r rewards dietary variety. Each unique food eaten for the first time permanently increases your maximum health. Eating the same food repeatedly provides no bonus."
		""
		"§2The more diverse your diet, the more hearts you have - build a varied farm as early as possible.§r"
	]
	quest.1F2E4A4B330C11BC.title: "Hunger System"
	quest.1F321F03B106834D.quest_desc: ["Now, as you have a better anvil, you can start §erecycling§r some stuff you may found in dungeons."]
	quest.1F321F03B106834D.title: "Recycling"
	quest.1F32BA07059CE534.quest_desc: [
		"§6Memory§r is like the §6CPU§r, an essential part in all computers."
		""
		"Depending on the CPU's architecture, the memory has a very essential effect on what a computer can and cannot do. For the standard Lua architecture, for example, it controls the actual amount of memory Lua scripts can use. This means that to run larger and more memory-intensive programs, you will need more memory."
	]
	quest.1F32BA07059CE534.title: "Memory"
	quest.1F35037770E8878E.quest_desc: [
		"The §6PLSS§r is an armor modification which will allow you to breathe in space. It will only work on airtight sealed suits."
		""
		"The §6Heavy Boots§r can be used to quickly descend down in low-gravity environments."
	]
	quest.1F35037770E8878E.title: "Space Equipment"
	quest.1F37B19A8C14A45C.quest_desc: [
		"Jool is a gas giant planet with Laythe and two other small unnamed planets orbiting it."
		""
		"As is logical, landing on a gas giant is impossible, but this doesn't prevent us from gathering resources from this giant."
		""
		"§2Jool's atmosphere consists of §bHelium-3§r §2(25%), §bLiquid Hydrogen§r §2(25%), §bChlorine§r §2(20%), and §bNeon§r §2(12%). To collect all these gases, we will need a §3Harvester§r.§r"
	]
	quest.1F37B19A8C14A45C.title: "Jool"
	quest.1F3A87714A445B52.quest_desc: [
		"The §6Gravity Gun§r is an advanced tool which can lift and throw blocks. It is particularly useful for moving highly hazardous blocks, such as corium from a reactor meltdown, or throwing explosives."
		""
		"§2The gravity gun can be supercharged in a Cyclotron using Ionized Particles, further increasing its range and power."
	]
	quest.1F3A87714A445B52.title: "Gravity Gun"
	quest.1F40BB03E81F8402.quest_desc: [
		"Congratulations. You have done it. You have actually done it."
		""
		"While the rest of the world clung desperately to their beef and their bread, you - yes, YOU - reached into your inventory, pulled out a §6Silkworm§r, and thought: \"yes. This is food now.\" Klaus is proud. Klaus is, in fact, emotional. Somewhere in a Swiss"
		"chalet, a single tear rolls down his turtleneck. You will own nothing. You will have no hunger bar. Und you will be happy."
	]
	quest.1F40BB03E81F8402.title: "You WILL eat ze bugs!"
	quest.1F41F975FBC7B97C.quest_desc: [
		"The §3Nuclear Waste Disposal Drum§r is used to decay §3RBMK§r nuclear waste. The decayed nuclear waste can then be used with a §3FEL§r and §3SILEX§r to obtain some rare elements, such as §6Bismuth§r."
		""
		"§2The drum also emmits radiation when theres fuel inside it."
	]
	quest.1F41F975FBC7B97C.title: "Nuclear Waste Disposal Drum"
	quest.1F56C60DF4C51CAF.quest_desc: [
		"The §6Quantum Computer§r is the most powerful out of any other control unit. It currently only used to build §6Gerald§r and §6DFC§r."
		""
		"§2A whole stack of them will be required, so now would be the time to upgrade circuit crafting infrastructure."
	]
	quest.1F56C60DF4C51CAF.title: "Quantum Computer"
	quest.1F59017853D3C788.quest_desc: ["The §6Crucible§r is a weapon that deals extreme amount of damage. It can be recharged inside a Tungsten Crate shot by a §3DFC Emitter§r."]
	quest.1F59017853D3C788.title: "The Crucible"
	quest.1F62AB4D8C9DF1EF.quest_desc: ["Be wary, they like to disguise and clone themselves in stone-related blocks! (Applies to Vanilla blocks only) Can be found within dungeons and hills. Can also be found in Drowning Creeper spawned cobblestone blocks."]
	quest.1F62AB4D8C9DF1EF.title: "Time to Kill (Silverfish)"
	quest.1F7F6B4EC351642D.quest_desc: [
		"Unlike its counterpart from the original mod, the Magma Drill does not literally drill into the depths. It is designed for extracting magma from Moho, which, as known, is abundant on this planet both on the surface and in caves. To start working, the mechanism must be installed directly on the surface of a lava lake so that the lava touches the drill head and reaches the edges of the recess. Supply power to the drill, and it will operate automatically."
		""
		"Magma is output through casting channels into molds. Cooled magma forms Vulcanite, which should then be processed to obtain useful resources."
		""
		"In addition to volcanite, the device extracts regular slag (much more than Vulcanite)."
	]
	quest.1F7F6B4EC351642D.title: "Magma Drill"
	quest.1F902265C0D88BD0.quest_desc: ["A §3Screen§r is used in combination with a §6Graphics Card§r, to allow computers to display text. Different screen tiers have different capabilities, such as supporting different resolutions and olor depths. Screens range from low-resolution, monochrome displays to high-resolution displays with up to 256 colors."]
	quest.1F902265C0D88BD0.title: "Screens"
	quest.1F9246C573F28F0C.quest_desc: [
		"The §3Orbital Station Computer§r, when having a drive inserted into it, can move the station to its destination."
		""
		"§3Thrusters§r with fuel are required to be attached to the station."
	]
	quest.1F9246C573F28F0C.title: "Orbital Station Computer"
	quest.1F9A59DD636D49DA.quest_desc: [
		"The §3Pumpjack§r is a more efficient §3Oil Derrick§r which extracts 750mb of §bCrude Oil§r and a random amount of §bNatural Gas§r between 50 and 250mb in a 1.25 second cycle. It depletes a single block of a deposit after extracting a random number of cycles of oil that is on average twice as large compared to the derrick."
		""
		"In total, this means that the pumpjack is on average 3x as efficient at extracting oil and 3x as fast at doing so while producing the same amount of natural gas as the derrick."
	]
	quest.1F9A59DD636D49DA.title: "Pumpjack"
	quest.1F9B5162A6991E61.quest_desc: ["Mmm... turn on the grill. We need more meat."]
	quest.1F9B5162A6991E61.title: "Time to Kill (Pig)"
	quest.1FB1FC01953D37C1.quest_desc: ["The §3Auxiliary Cooling Tower§r is a larger version of the Steam Condenser able to process up to 50 mb/t of §bLow-Pressure Steam§r."]
	quest.1FB1FC01953D37C1.title: "Auxilary Cooling Tower"
	quest.1FBC21D9A76F590E.quest_desc: ["This is something new; don't ask questions like how a cow survives on the Mun without food or where it got a PLSS module. The fact is, they feel quite well on the Mun, and due to the vacuum, the milk inside them has curdled."]
	quest.1FBC21D9A76F590E.title: "Mun Cow?!"
	quest.1FC3D99E55848D49.quest_desc: ["The §3Catalytic Cracking Tower§r is a large oil processing multiblock machine which produces many fluids, such as §bAromatic Hydrocarbons§r used for §6Bakelite§r."]
	quest.1FC3D99E55848D49.title: "Catalytic Cracking Tower"
	quest.1FC4C632E91887DE.quest_desc: ["The §3Industrial Solidification Machine§r is a general use machine for the solidification of various fluids. An important product of this machine is §6Tar§r, which can be used to create §3Tanks§r."]
	quest.1FC4C632E91887DE.title: "Industrial Solidification Machine"
	quest.1FDBCF428C951B76.quest_desc: [
		"The §3Gas Centrifuge§r is used to centrifuge §bUranium/Plutonium Hexafluoride§r to obtain enriched fuel for bombs and reactor fuel."
		""
		"Two gas centrifuges in a row will yield §6Uranium-238§r and §6Uranium Fuel§r used in reactors. The uranium hexafluoride processing line does not consume the §6Sulfur§r and §6Fluorite§r, so loops are recommended."
		""
		"The §6Gas Centrifuge Overclocking Upgrade§r is needed to obtain §6Uranium-235§r. Four gas centrifuges will have to be placed in a row and the upgrade on the last of them to obtain uranium-235 nuggets."
		""
		"[F1] For more information."
	]
	quest.1FDBCF428C951B76.title: "Gas Centrifuge"
	quest.1FE28712872298AC.quest_desc: [
		"The §3Teleporter§r can be used to teleport players, and entities in general, to a specific location."
		""
		"Right-click a block with the §6Telelinker§r to set the desired exit position, then shift-click the teleporter with the telelinker to configure the teleporter."
		""
		"§2The teleporter is a one way trip so it is advised that multiple are made."
		""
		"Interdimensional teleportation using teleporters requires a very expensive type of fuel, so it is recommended that other teleportations methods are used, such as AE2 Spatial."
	]
	quest.1FE28712872298AC.title: "Teleporter"
	quest.1FE521A2E7D6A6ED.quest_desc: ["The §6Pollution Detector§r will monitor and show the levels of pollution present in the environment. High levels of pollution will decrease the visibility, give debuffs to the player and buff mobs, including skeletons spawning with firearms."]
	quest.1FE521A2E7D6A6ED.title: "Pollution Detector"
	quest.1FF9D990D8DC66E9.quest_desc: ["§6Arsenic§r is a substitute of §6Bismuth§r which can be made from acidizing §6Oily Dirt§r, found near §ebedrock oil deposits§r or from the environmental damage the §3Fracking Tower§r does, with §bHigh-Performance Solvent§r."]
	quest.1FF9D990D8DC66E9.title: "Arsenic"
	quest.1FFBCAC78CA35CFF.quest_desc: ["§6Ferric Schrabidate§r is an alloy made from §6Iron§r, §6Ionized Particles§r and §6Schrabidium§r. It can also be used to create schrabidate capacitors, which are a great way of storing energy."]
	quest.1FFBCAC78CA35CFF.title: "Ferric Schrabidate"
	quest.20C1FBD6FBD285CF.quest_desc: [
		"The &3Rock Mill&r is an early game material grinding machine which grinds down stones into finer items while producing additional byproducts, such as &6Boron&r, &6Niobium&r and &6Titanium&r. It is also used to get big amounts of &bColloid&r, which can be used for making clay."
		""
		"The machine consumes &e500HE/s&r."
	]
	quest.2191CAFC754CAF27.quest_desc: [
		"&3Multi-Lane Conveyor Belts&r let you transport items on separate lanes within the same block, so you can run multiple item streams side by side. "
		""
		"&6Express Conveyor Belts&r move items twice as fast as standard belts, making them useful when throughput or travel distance becomes a bottleneck."
	]
	quest.226D9E8A5B55AD1D.quest_desc: [
		"The &3Cargo Landing Pad&r receives resource shipments from &3Asteroid Mining Ships&r."
		""
		"Assign a &bSatellite ID&r to an Asteroid Mining Ship and launch it using a fueled &3Soyuz&r. Insert a &bSatellite ID Chip&r with the same ID into the landing pad. The miner operates at &6Dres&r and prepares a shipment every &b15 minutes of running game time&r, while the pad can receive deliveries on any planet."
		""
		"Keep the pad’s chunk loaded and the space above it unobstructed. If multiple pads share the same ID, the &efirst to request a ready shipment&r receives it; no planet has priority."
	]
	quest.229C2D229EC07E7B.quest_desc: [
		"The RoR &6Logic Receiver&r is an advanced receiver with an extended interface that lets you define conditions for when it should output a redstone signal. Instead of simply passing a signal through, it compares the received signal against constants you set, using operators such as MATCHES, DOES NOT MATCH, CONTAINS, DOES NOT CONTAIN, GREATER, GREATER OR EQUAL, LESS, and LESS OR EQUAL. Each condition is evaluated in order, and higher outputs take priority - you can flip the evaluation order with the button near the ID field."
		""
		"This makes the Logic Receiver especially useful with the Item Counter, since item counts can exceed the normal redstone limit of 15. Set a condition like GREATER than 1000, and the receiver will output only when your container holds more than that many items."
	]
	quest.229C2D229EC07E7B.title: "Logic Reciever"
	quest.2AF74FFE189B3CBD.quest_desc: [
		"&3Gauges&r measure how much energy or fluid is moving through your network, so you can spot bottlenecks and tune your setups."
		""
		"The &6Flow Gauge Pipe&r works like a normal fluid pipe but also reports flow rate in mB/s and mB/t. Just hover over it to see the values. It connects to any universal fluid pipe, including Boxcar pipes, and treats branched pipe systems joined by a single tank as one system. It does not work with exhaust pipes."
		""
		"The &6Power Gauge&r sits inline with your cables and measures the energy passing through per tick and per second. Because it is a variation of red copper cable, it conducts power normally, so you can place it in the middle of a wire without breaking the connection. Separate networks linked by energy storage blocks are treated as one network."
	]
	quest.2AF74FFE189B3CBD.title: "Gauges"
	quest.34838278F309AC85.quest_desc: [
		"The RoR &6Item Counter&r counts individual items inside a container rather than just measuring how full it is. Place it on any block with an inventory - including item ports on multiblock machines - and specify which item to count using the filter slots on the right side of its interface. Right-click a filter to switch between Item Matches and Item and Meta Matches."
		""
		"It can transmit to up to 3 different receivers using separate ID fields. Unlike vanilla comparators, the Item Counter's signal strength is not limited to 15, so it can report exact counts even for large inventories. Pair it with a Logic Receiver to trigger outputs based on specific item thresholds."
	]
	quest.34838278F309AC85.title: "Item Counter"
	quest.35DB2F5A407B1A65.quest_desc: ["&6Sodalite&r is a gem recovered as a &3Centrifuge&r byproduct of many ores. Run lapis through a &3Combination Oven&r to get &bChlorine Gas&r plus sodiumr. Melt sodium down to &bLiquid Sodium&r: a powerful &3Pressurized Water Reactor&r coolant, far stronger than water loops. Stockpile it before your first PWR core."]
	quest.36A6887005727069.quest_desc: [
		"&dNTM&r introduces &eRedstone-Over-Radio&r (RoR), a system for sending redstone signals wirelessly across your base. Every RoR component requires glowstone, so you'll need to visit the Nether first."
		""
		"The core components are the &6Transmitter&r and &6Receiver&r. Place a transmitter on a block that outputs a comparator signal (like a fluid tank or crate), set an &eID&r (any 10 characters), and set the same ID on a receiver. Press \"Save Settings\" on both - changes are not saved automatically. The receiver will then output a redstone signal matching the transmitter's input. Multiple receivers can listen to one transmitter, but multiple transmitters on the same ID will overwrite each other, with the last one winning."
		""
		"RoR can replace vanilla comparators for remote monitoring and control. Advanced components like the Item Counter, Logic Receiver, Reader, and Controller unlock more possibilities, such as reading exact item counts beyond 15 or sending commands to machines."
	]
	quest.36A6887005727069.title: "Redstone-Over-Radio"
	quest.37EAB53DBAC7ED03.quest_desc: [
		"&2This quest is a guide to feeding items into an Arc Furnace precisely, so you don't waste electrode durability.&r"
		""
		"With no upgrades in the &3Arc Furnace&r, you have exactly 20 item slots to work with. Start by routing all input items into a &3Conveyor Boxer&r, which then feeds a &3Conveyor Unboxer&r. Add Speed Ejection and Stack Ejection upgrades to the unboxer - this is strongly recommended so items enter fast enough to keep up."
		""
		"{image:quests:textures/arc1.png width:427 height:240 align:center}"
		""
		"Place a &3Redstone-Over-Radio Item Counter&r on one side of the boxer, set the item filter, and give it an ID."
		""
		""
		"{image:quests:textures/arc2.png width:427 height:240 align:center}"
		""
		"Next, place a &3Redstone-Over-Radio Logic Receiver&r, set it to the same ID, and configure it to emit redstone when the item count reaches 20."
		""
		""
		"{image:quests:textures/arc3.png width:427 height:240 align:center}"
		""
		"Finally, make sure the boxer is set to redstone mode."
		""
		"{image:quests:textures/arc4.png width:427 height:240 align:center}"
	]
	quest.3D1C4555EAD0B081.quest_desc: [
		"Attaching a &3Drive Enclosure&r to one of the ports of a &3Satellite Ground Station&r which is linked to a satellite will allow it to receive data. &2A linked satellite ground station, when looking at it, will reveal information about the satellite.&r The &6Space Laboratory&r is a modular satellite which produces data for drives. &2All of the Space Laboratory related satellites must have the same ID.&r"
		""
		"Quest requirements: Attach a &3Drive Enclosure&r to a &3Satellite Ground Station&r that is linked to a &6Space Laboratory&r satellite. Ensure all Space Laboratory related satellites share the same ID. Receive data from the satellite."
		""
		"[F1] For more information."
	]
	quest.46C1ADA0012E3001.quest_desc: ["Orbital Data is used for making &6Gerald&r. Due the amount it requires, it is highly recommended that a large amount of &6Satellite Sensor Relays&r are launched."]
	quest.46C1ADA0012E3001.title: "Orbital Data"
	quest.49A929AB52F79EFD.quest_desc: [
		"The &3Automatic Crafting Table&r performs a set recipe automatically as long as it has power. Define the recipe by placing ingredients into the blue crafting grid - you can use items from your inventory or drag them from NEI. Once set, input items go into the gray grid and are consumed, with the product appearing in the gray output slot. It costs 100 HE per operation and runs one operation per tick regardless of recipe complexity."
		""
		"It works with hoppers, crates, and conveyor machines for full automation. For 2x2 or 3x3 recipes where every ingredient is the same item, use the &6Combinator Funnel&r instead - it needs no power."
	]
	quest.5239ED0B7218C058.quest_desc: [
		"The &3Lambda Launch Pad&r is a mechanism for launching the &6Lambda-98 Rocket&r, which can be used to launch satellites for cheaper and faster than the Soyuz. This launch pad works much faster than the Soyuz facility: loading the rocket and fueling takes noticeably less time, and instead of a 30 second wait after pressing the launch button, Lambda offers only 10 seconds. It also supports automatic launch after all preparation procedures are complete."
		""
		"The launch pad constantly consumes &e200kHE/s&r. Each launch consumes 16000mB of &bLeaded Gasoline&r and &bHydrogen Peroxide&r. If the pad is in auto-launch mode, a countdown begins after all required slots and buffers are filled. In manual mode, the pad waits for your signal."
		""
		"Quest requirements: Build a &3Lambda Launch Pad&r, supply it with &e200kHE/s&r and stock &bLeaded Gasoline&r and &bHydrogen Peroxide&r. Launch a &6Lambda-98 Rocket&r. Optionally, enable auto-launch mode for automatic countdown and launch."
		""
		"[F1] For more information."
	]
	quest.5318527B6F045F14.quest_desc: [
		"The &6Servo Set&r is an armor modification which grants various buffs, such as &eHaste&r, &eStrength&r, &eSpeed&r and &eJump Boost&r. It can be equiped both for the chestplate and leggings."
		""
		"It can later be upgraded with &6Desh&r to further boost its buffs."
	]
	quest.5512F548BFFD55B3.quest_desc: ["&3Telex Machine&r sends and receives text messages between Telex units. Set the recipient's ID and your own ID, type a message up to 33 characters, then press SND to send. Incoming messages appear in the lower field and can be printed to paper with PRT. It needs no energy, can be found in rocket silos and towers, and crafts two at a time. Special characters add useful effects - BEL rings a bell at the destination, PRT auto-prints the message for all recipients, and PSE delays sending. It also works as an infinite paper source since PRT functions even on an empty message."]
	quest.5512F548BFFD55B3.title: "Telex"
	quest.55C85EC43AFA7511.quest_desc: [
		"&6Depth Ores&r are large ore deposits found at bedrock level. There are many types of deposits, most of them giving ore crystals which can be smelted for 3 ingots per."
		""
		"&3Mining Charges&r of any kind are required to extract the resources from the depth rock."
		""
		"Two important resources found in depth deposits are &6Borax&r, which can later be put in an &3Arc Furnace&r or &3Acidizer&r to yield &6Boron&r used in reactors, and &6Zirconium&r which is used in reactor fuel rods."
	]
	quest.55C85EC43AFA7511.title: "Depth Ores"
	quest.56CD962DD557F4EA.quest_desc: [
		"&6Ilmenite&r is a mineral that serves as a natural source of titanium. It is produced by centrifuging &6Titanium Ore&r. By itself, it can be placed in an &3Arc Furnace&r to produce 3 &6Titanium Ingots&r, or it can be further processed in a &3Chemical Plant&r using &bTitanium Tetrachloride&r to increase its yield. The most efficient recipe is in the &3Pyrolysis Oven&r, where on top of giving the most titanium per Ilmenite, it also recycles back all the &bChlorine&r."
		""
		"Quest requirements: Obtain &6Ilmenite&r by centrifuging &6Titanium Ore&r. Build an &3Arc Furnace&r, &3Chemical Plant&r, or &3Pyrolysis Oven&r. Produce at least one &6Titanium Ingot&r from &6Ilmenite&r. For maximum efficiency, use the &3Pyrolysis Oven&r and recover &bChlorine&r."
		""
		"[F1] For more information."
	]
	quest.56CD962DD557F4EA.title: "Ilmenite"
	quest.6161F9C9E2B317A2.quest_desc: ["The &3Flow Control Pump&r controls how fluids move through your pipe network. Use it to set priorities between fluid networks and to limit fluid throughput, similar to how a Network Separator manages power. It passes a maximum of 10,000 mB per tick and supports fluid pressure from 0 to 5 PU. Configure it through its GUI and hover over the pump to see current flow data. It needs no power, has no upgrades, and is 3x1x1. Note that drain pipes, incinerators, and gas towers have low fluid priority by default."]
	quest.66D7F48F29CABD92.quest_desc: [
		"&eRedstone-Over-Radio&r can be combined with a &3Redstone Fluid Valve&r to detect when a tank is starting to fill and then release its contents. This lets you use tanks as buffers without wasting fluid."
		""
		"A typical setup is a tank that only outputs fluid once it is full. Place a &6RoR Transmitter&r on one port of the tank, give it an ID, and enable Polling."
		""
		"{image:quests:textures/qb_fluid1.png width:427 height:240 align:center}"
		""
		"Then place a &6RoR Logic Receiver&r next to the fluid valve and configure it so the received signal must be greater than or equal to your desired buffer threshold. Each redstone level equals 16,000 mB, so set the condition based on how large a buffer you want."
		""
		""
		"{image:quests:textures/qb_fluid2.png width:427 height:240 align:center}"
	]
	quest.66D7F48F29CABD92.title: "Fluid Overflow"
	quest.6B71FA0F85A0202C.quest_desc: ["&60G Assemblers&r allow for the production of certain items in orbit, mainly the &6Crystal Circuite Board&r. Launching more assemblers will speed up the recipe. The input items must be launched from a rocket."]
	quest.6B71FA0F85A0202C.title: "0G Assembler"
	quest.6CFF17120419CE60.quest_desc: [
		"&3Conveyor Grabber&r grabs items directly off a conveyor belt without needing the belt to feed into it. It has no internal buffer, so items are pulled straight from the belt and placed into an adjacent inventory or machine. It includes whitelist and blacklist filters with 9 slots each, and without the Stack Amount upgrade it only grabs one item at a time - a full stack on the belt will be taken one piece per operation. With the upgrade it can grab groups. Use a screwdriver to set its orientation and input/output sides: right-click sets input, Shift-right-click sets output, and double right-click places ports on opposite sides."
		""
		"&2Factorio inserter says \"Hi!\"&r"
	]
	quest.772A1777CCE85569.quest_desc: [
		"&3AUTOCAL Automatic Calculator&r is an earlygame 1x1x2 programmable machine that runs MS-ES1 scripts line by line. Use it to do math, store values in a buffer or named variables, make comparisons and branches, and send or receive Redstone-over-Radio signals - especially useful for automating RoR devices and controlling satellites."
		""
		"To program it, open hbmComputerUpload/script.txt with the machine’s file button, write your MS-ES1 script, upload it, then press ON/OFF to run or stop it. Keep Ignore Errors off while debugging; Automatic Reboot restarts the script after it ends but wipes saved variables. Use clockspeed to control lines processed per tick, and endtick if you need to avoid overwriting multiple RoR signals sent on the same channel in one tick."
		""
		"&2The in-machine documentation button is your best reference for commands."
	]
	quest.772A1777CCE85569.title: "AUTOCAL Automatic Calculator"
	quest.7C109A48F15A6741.quest_desc: [
		"The &3Supercomputer&r is a late-game machine essential for processing both &6Flash Drives&r and &6Disk Drives&r. It is made in an &3Assembly Machine&r. The machine measures 12x5x9 blocks and requires energy to operate, with consumption depending on the operation. It does not require heat."
		""
		"Flash Drives are inserted into the &3Supercomputer&r and can be made into &eFlight Simulation Data&r, used in making the &6Soyuz&r and &6Orbital Module&r, or &eParticle Simulation Data&r, used in the &3Fusion Reactor&r."
		"{@pagebreak}"
		"Most of the Supercomputer's operations work like those of the &3Precision Assembly Machine&r: they have a chance of returning a broken version of the input, which can be recycled for a portion of its materials. Operations involving data drives require cooling. Compatible coolants, from slowest to fastest, are &bWater&r, &bCold Perfluoromethyl&r, and &bHelium-4&r. Faster fluids speed up the process substantially but also increase the chance of a broken output. Overall, this makes for more successful outputs on average. The Supercomputer can also manufacture cheaper &6Blueprint Booklets&r and &6Klaus&r."
		""
		"&2Processing drives is extremely time consuming. The fastest operations take 60 seconds, while the longest can take up to 1 hour of real time. Plan your resource and energy usage accordingly."
		""
		"&2Quest requirements: Build a &3Supercomputer&r, supply it with &bWater&r, &bCold Perfluoromethyl&r, or &bHelium-4&r as coolant, and process at least one &6Flash Drive&r into &eFlight Simulation Data&r or &eParticle Simulation Data&r."
		""
		"[F1] For more information."
	]
	reward_table.4D209E9E28DE8FF9.title: "LV2-Desh"
	reward_table.5D37C76863781491.title: "LV3-Centrifuge"
	reward_table.64DCD9F3259E3D0F.title: "LV2-EAF"
	reward_table.FFFFFFFFFFFFFFFF.title: "Internal"
	task.3BD6A11BA7CC4ADD.title: "RBMKSim"
	task.69B28AFED34E91D6.title: "Arc Furnace Automation"
	task.7B3CAB87AEF65AF1.title: "depth_ores"
}
